// 2. Grammar MCQ (~40 道)
const GRAMMAR_QUESTIONS = [{"q":"He ___ to school every day.","opts":["go","goes","going","gone"],"ans":1,"diff":1,"tag":"主谓","explain":"every day是一般现在时信号词, 主语He是第三人称单数, 动词要加s, 所以选goes。选go的同学漏了三单规则, He/She/It后面动词必须变形。考点: PSLE爱考every day/always这类频率词配一般现在时三单。"},{"q":"They ___ playing football.","opts":["is","are","am","be"],"ans":1,"diff":1,"tag":"主谓","explain":"主语They是复数, be动词要用are, 后接playing构成现在进行时。最迷惑的是is, 但is只配单数主语, They是多个人。考点: PSLE爱考be动词和主语单复数配对, 先圈主语再选。"},{"q":"I ___ a student.","opts":["am","is","are","be"],"ans":0,"diff":1,"tag":"主谓","explain":"主语是I, be动词固定搭配am, 这是铁规则没有例外。选is的同学错在把I当第三人称, is只给he/she/it用。考点: PSLE基础题必考I am/You are/He is三组固定配对。"},{"q":"She ___ a book now.","opts":["read","reads","is reading","are reading"],"ans":2,"diff":1,"tag":"现在进行","explain":"now是现在进行时的信号词, 表示此刻正在做, 用is reading(be+动词ing)。最迷惑的是reads, 它是一般现在时, 表示习惯不是此刻。考点: PSLE爱考now/Look!这类信号词锁定present continuous tense。"},{"q":"My brother ___ tall.","opts":["is","are","am","be"],"ans":0,"diff":1,"tag":"主谓","explain":"主语My brother是单数第三人称, be动词用is。选are的同学可能被brother联想成兄弟们, 但这里只有一个brother。考点: PSLE爱考单数主语配is, 看清主语有没有s或and。"},{"q":"Yesterday I ___ a movie.","opts":["watch","watches","watched","watching"],"ans":2,"diff":2,"tag":"过去时","explain":"Yesterday是过去时信号词, 动词要用过去式watched。最迷惑的是watch, 原形只能配现在或将来, 昨天的事必须变过去式。考点: PSLE爱考yesterday/last week这类时间词定simple past tense。"},{"q":"Tomorrow we ___ to the park.","opts":["go","went","will go","going"],"ans":2,"diff":2,"tag":"将来时","explain":"Tomorrow指将来, 要用will go表示将来时。最迷惑的是went, 它是过去式, 和明天矛盾。先找时间词再选时态就不会错。考点: PSLE爱考tomorrow/next week配will+动词原形。"},{"q":"I ___ my homework already.","opts":["finish","finished","have finished","finishing"],"ans":2,"diff":2,"tag":"完成时","explain":"already表示已经完成, 配现在完成时have finished(have+过去分词)。最迷惑的是finished, 单独过去式不能和already搭出完成的意思, 少了have。考点: PSLE爱考already/just/yet锁定present perfect tense。"},{"q":"When I arrived, she ___ TV.","opts":["watch","watched","was watching","watching"],"ans":2,"diff":2,"tag":"过去进行","explain":"我到达那一刻她正在看电视, 过去某时刻正在进行的动作用was watching。最迷惑的是watched, 它只说她看过, 表达不出当时正在看。考点: PSLE爱考When/While+过去时间点配past continuous tense。"},{"q":"He ___ in Singapore for 5 years.","opts":["live","lived","has lived","living"],"ans":2,"diff":2,"tag":"现在完成","explain":"for 5 years表示从过去持续到现在, 用现在完成时has lived。最迷惑的是lived, 过去式暗示已经不住了, 而他现在还住着。考点: PSLE爱考for/since+时间段配present perfect tense。"},{"q":"She is ___ than me.","opts":["taller","more taller","tallest","tall"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"比较级","explain":"两人比较用比较级, tall是单音节形容词直接加er变taller。最迷惑的是more taller, er和more不能同时用, 这是双重比较错误。考点: PSLE爱考than前必用比较级且er和more二选一。"},{"q":"This is the ___ book I have read.","opts":["good","better","best","well"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"最高级","explain":"the...I have read表示读过的所有书里最好的, 用最高级best。最迷惑的是better, 比较级只比两个, 这里是全部书里挑第一。考点: PSLE爱考the+最高级+范围, good变best是不规则变化。"},{"q":"The cat is ___ the chair.","opts":["under","at","in","on top"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"介词","explain":"猫在椅子下面, under表示在正下方, 语义最通。最迷惑的是on top, 但正确说法是on top of the chair, 少了of不成立。考点: PSLE爱考介词短语的完整搭配, 缺of的选项是陷阱。"},{"q":"I am good ___ math.","opts":["at","in","on","to"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"介词搭配","explain":"be good at是固定搭配, 表示擅长某事, at不能换。最迷惑的是in, 中文说在数学方面好容易误选in, 但英文习惯就是at。考点: PSLE爱考固定搭配, good at/interested in要整组背。"},{"q":"Be careful ___ the hot soup.","opts":["with","of","to","in"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"介词","explain":"be careful with+具体东西, 表示小心对待热汤。最迷惑的是of, careful of多用于抽象危险, 面对具体物品用with更地道。考点: PSLE爱考careful with/afraid of这类形容词+介词搭配。"},{"q":"If it rains, I ___ at home.","opts":["stay","will stay","stayed","staying"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"条件句","explain":"条件句规则: if从句用现在时, 主句用will+原形, 所以选will stay。最迷惑的是stay, 主句不能也用现在时, 那样两边都没将来的意思。考点: PSLE爱考first conditional主句必带will。"},{"q":"Neither John ___ Mary likes durian.","opts":["or","nor","and","but"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"neither/nor","explain":"neither固定和nor配对, 表示两者都不喜欢。最迷惑的是or, 它是either的搭档, neither...or是不存在的组合。考点: PSLE爱考连词配对, neither/nor和either/or不能混搭。"},{"q":"She speaks English ___ than her brother.","opts":["good","better","best","more well"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"副词比较","explain":"speaks是动词, 要用副词well的比较级better来修饰。最迷惑的是good, 它是形容词只能修饰名词, 不能修饰动词speak。考点: PSLE爱考形容词副词之分, well的比较级是better不规则。"},{"q":"I would rather ___ tea than coffee.","opts":["drink","drinks","drinking","to drink"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"would rather","explain":"would rather后面直接跟动词原形drink, 这是固定句型。最迷惑的是to drink, 很多同学习惯加to, 但rather后不要to。考点: PSLE爱考would rather+原形, had better也一样不加to。"},{"q":"The book ___ I borrowed is interesting.","opts":["who","which","whom","whose"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"关系代词","explain":"先行词book是物, 关系代词用which。最迷惑的是who, 它只能指人, book是东西不能用who。考点: PSLE爱考relative pronoun选择, 人用who物用which, that两边通吃但选项里优先对号。"},{"q":"Neither of them ___ here.","opts":["is","are","were","have"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓陷阱","explain":"neither of them意思是两个都不, 语法上按单数处理, 动词用is。最迷惑的是are, 看到them复数就选are是经典陷阱, 真正的主语是neither。考点: PSLE爱考neither of/either of+复数名词仍配单数动词。"},{"q":"Each of the boys ___ a prize.","opts":["receive","receives","receiving","have"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓陷阱","explain":"each of意思是每一个, 主语核心是each, 单数, 动词加s用receives。最迷惑的是receive, 被the boys复数带偏了, 但of后面的词不是主语。考点: PSLE爱考each of/every one of后动词永远单数。"},{"q":"The news ___ shocking.","opts":["is","are","were","being"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"不可数主谓","explain":"news虽然以s结尾, 但它是不可数名词, 按单数算, 用is。最迷惑的是are, 看到s尾巴就当复数是最常见的坑。考点: PSLE爱考假复数单词, news/mathematics/physics都配单数动词。"},{"q":"Hardly ___ I sat down when the phone rang.","opts":["have","had","did","was"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"倒装","explain":"Hardly...when是固定倒装句型, 表示刚一坐下电话就响, 用过去完成时had提前。最迷惑的是did, 但这个句型固定配had+过去分词, 不用did。考点: PSLE爱考Hardly had...when/No sooner had...than固定倒装。"},{"q":"Not only ___ smart, but also kind.","opts":["he is","is he","he was","was him"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"倒装","explain":"Not only放句首必须倒装, 把is提到he前面, 变成is he。最迷惑的是he is, 正常语序在这里反而错, 句首否定词强制倒装。考点: PSLE爱考Not only/Never/Seldom开头的句子要inversion。"},{"q":"I saw ___ elephant at the zoo.","opts":["a","an","the","/"],"ans":1,"diff":2,"tag":"冠词-元音","explain":"elephant开头是元音音/e/, 元音音前用an, 而且第一次提到用不定冠词。选A(a)的最多, 只看拼写不听发音, a碰上元音音读起来会卡壳。 考点: PSLE爱考冠词看发音不看字母, an hour和a university是姐妹陷阱"},{"q":"My mother is ___ teacher.","opts":["a","an","the","/"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"冠词-辅音","explain":"teacher是辅音音/t/开头的单数可数职业名词, 说职业用a。选D(不加冠词)的人以为职业像play football一样免冠词, 错了, 单数可数名词前必须有冠词。 考点: PSLE爱考『be + a + 职业』结构, 冠词不能丢"},{"q":"He plays ___ football every weekend.","opts":["a","an","the","/"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"冠词-球类不加","explain":"球类运动名词前不加任何冠词, play football/badminton/chess都是裸奔的。最迷惑是C(the), 因为play the piano确实要the——但那是乐器, 不是运动。 考点: PSLE爱考play+运动不加冠词 vs play the+乐器加the"},{"q":"The Sun rises in ___ east.","opts":["a","an","the","/"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"冠词-方位the","explain":"东南西北这类方位名词是独一无二的方向, 固定用the: in the east。选D(不加)的孩子以为方位词像国家名一样免冠词, 但east前the是铁规矩。 考点: PSLE爱考独一无二事物加the, 如the sun/the east/the world"},{"q":"She is ___ honest student.","opts":["a","an","the","/"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"冠词-h不发音","explain":"honest的h不发音, 开头实际是元音音/ɒ/, 所以用an。最坑的是A(a), 眼睛看到辅音字母h就选a, 忘了要用耳朵判断。 考点: PSLE爱考h不发音的词, an honest/an hour是必背清单"},{"q":"I want to be ___ engineer when I grow up.","opts":["a","an","the","/"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"冠词-元音音","explain":"engineer开头是元音音/e/, 用an; 职业+单数可数=不定冠词。选A(a)的只顾职业规则忘了元音音规则, 两条规则要叠加用。 考点: PSLE爱考an+元音音开头职业, an engineer/an artist成对记"},{"q":"My brother and ___ went to the park.","opts":["I","me","my","myself"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"代词-主格","explain":"这里是句子的主语(和My brother一起去公园), 主语位置必须用主格I。选B(me)的最多, 因为口语常说me and my brother, 但书面语法里主语不能用宾格。 考点: PSLE爱考并列主语选I还是me, 遮住and前面的人单独读一遍就知道"},{"q":"The teacher gave the prize to John and ___.","opts":["I","me","my","myself"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"代词-宾格","explain":"to是介词, 介词后面的代词一律用宾格me。最迷惑是A(I), 很多孩子被大人教『说I显得有礼貌』带偏了, 其实gave to I读起来就不通。 考点: PSLE爱考介词后接宾格, 删掉John and单独试读是万能验证法"},{"q":"She did the homework by ___.","opts":["her","herself","she","hers"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"代词-反身","explain":"by oneself是固定搭配表示『独自/自己完成』, she对应的反身代词是herself。选A(her)的以为介词后用宾格就行, 但by her意思变成『被她』, 和原意完全不同。 考点: PSLE爱考by+反身代词=独自做, herself/himself/themselves要配对"},{"q":"This pen is ___, not yours.","opts":["my","mine","me","I"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"代词-名词性物主","explain":"空格后没有名词, 要用名词性物主代词mine, 它一个词顶my pen两个词。最坑是A(my), my后面必须跟名词, 光秃秃的my是病句。 考点: PSLE爱考mine/yours/hers独立用 vs my/your/her后必接名词"},{"q":"The cat licked ___ paws.","opts":["it","its","it's","itself"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"代词-its陷阱","explain":"paws前需要形容词性物主代词, 猫的爪子用its, 不带撇号。最毒的是C(it's), 那是it is的缩写, 意思是『它是爪子』, 完全讲不通——但长得太像了。 考点: PSLE爱考its(它的)和it's(它是)的撇号陷阱, 拆开读一遍就现形"},{"q":"Everyone should bring ___ own pencil.","opts":["his or her","their","its","one's"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"代词-everyone","explain":"everyone是单数代词, 正式书面语要用his or her来对应。最迷惑是B(their), 日常口语大家都这么说, 但PSLE标准语法里everyone配their算数不一致。 考点: PSLE爱考everyone/everybody按单数处理, 后面代词和动词都跟着单数走"},{"q":"Between you and ___, this is a secret.","opts":["I","me","my","myself"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"代词-between后宾格","explain":"between是介词, 介词后代词必须宾格, between you and me是标准搭配。最坑是A(I), 因为听起来『高级』, 但between you and I恰恰是最经典的错误说法。 考点: PSLE爱考between you and me, 越像客气话的I越是陷阱"},{"q":"A group of students ___ waiting outside.","opts":["is","are","was","have"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓-集合主语","explain":"主语核心词是a group(一个团体, 单数), of students只是修饰, 动词跟group走用is。选B(are)的被就近的students骗了, 眼睛要盯住真正的主语头。 考点: PSLE爱考a group of/a box of结构, 动词看of前面的量词不看后面"},{"q":"One of the books ___ missing.","opts":["is","are","were","being"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"主谓-one of","explain":"真正的主语是one(一本), of the books只是范围, 单数配is。最迷惑是B(are), 因为空格紧挨着books, 但books不是主语只是陪衬。 考点: PSLE爱考one of the+复数名词+单数动词, 划掉of短语再选"},{"q":"Were it not for the rain, we ___ the match.","opts":["would have won","won","had won","will win"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"虚拟-倒装","explain":"Were it not for是If it were not for的倒装, 属于对现在事实的虚拟, 主句配would have won表示『本来会赢』。选B(won)的把虚拟句当真事陈述, 丢了would这个虚拟标志。 考点: PSLE高分题爱考Were it not for倒装虚拟, 主句必带would"},{"q":"Scarcely ___ the house when it started raining.","opts":["had I left","I had left","I left","did I leave"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"倒装-scarcely","explain":"Scarcely放句首必须倒装, 且『刚做完A就发生B』用过去完成时, 所以had I left。最迷惑是B(I had left), 时态对了但没倒装, scarcely在句首就必须had提前。 考点: PSLE爱考Scarcely/Hardly...when句型, 句首否定词触发倒装+过去完成"},{"q":"The committee ___ divided in their opinions.","opts":["is","are","was","were"],"ans":1,"diff":6,"tag":"集合名词-意义复数","explain":"committee在这里『内部意见分裂』, 强调成员各自不同, 集合名词按复数处理用are, 后面的their也是铁证。最坑是A(is), 平时committee确实常用单数, 但divided in their opinions说明这次看的是一个个人。 考点: PSLE爱考集合名词两面派, 整体=单数, 内部分歧=复数, 看their抓线索"},{"q":"He demanded that she ___ the report immediately.","opts":["submit","submits","submitted","submitting"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"虚拟-demand that","explain":"demand/suggest/insist后的that从句用虚拟语气, 动词一律原形submit, 不管主语是she。最迷惑是B(submits), 按平时第三人称单数加s的习惯选它, 但虚拟从句里这条规则失效。 考点: PSLE高阶爱考demand that+动词原形, 见到demand/insist就把s扔掉"},{"q":"So profound ___ his speech that everyone was moved.","opts":["was","is","had been","being"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"so...that倒装","explain":"So+形容词放句首触发倒装, be动词提到主语前, 且后文was moved定调过去时, 所以选was。最迷惑是B(is), 倒装对了但时态错了, 前后半句时态要咬合。 考点: PSLE爱考So...that句首倒装, 先看倒装再对齐后半句时态"},{"q":"She ___ her homework before dinner every day.","opts":["does","do","doing","did"],"ans":0,"diff":1,"tag":"一般现在","explain":"every day是一般现在时信号, 主语she是第三人称单数, 动词加s/es用does。最迷惑是D(did), 有孩子看到before dinner以为是过去, 但every day说的是天天如此的习惯。 考点: PSLE爱考every day/always配一般现在时, 第三人称单数别忘s"},{"q":"The sun ___ in the east.","opts":["rise","rises","rose","rising"],"ans":1,"diff":1,"tag":"一般现在-事实","explain":"太阳从东边升起是永恒事实, 用一般现在时, 主语the sun单数所以rises加s。最迷惑是A(rise), 时态选对了却丢了第三人称单数的s, 白白丢分。 考点: PSLE爱考自然规律/科学事实用一般现在时, 单数主语动词必加s"},{"q":"Look! The children ___ in the playground.","opts":["play","plays","are playing","played"],"ans":2,"diff":2,"tag":"现在进行","explain":"Look!是现在进行时的经典信号词, 说话这一刻正在发生, 用are playing。最迷惑是A(play), 以为children天天都玩就选一般现在, 但Look!锁死了『此刻正在』。 考点: PSLE爱考Look!/Listen!信号词, 见到必配is/are+ing"},{"q":"She ___ to Japan twice.","opts":["goes","went","has been","is going"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-经历","explain":"twice(两次)说的是到今天为止的人生经历, 用现在完成时has been, been表示去过已回来。最迷惑是B(went), 过去时只说某一次具体的事, 配不上twice这种累计经历。 考点: PSLE爱考has been to=去过(回来了) vs has gone to=去了(没回来)"},{"q":"I ___ him since last year.","opts":["know","knew","have known","am knowing"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-持续","explain":"since last year表示从去年持续到现在, 用现在完成时have known。最坑是A(know), 以为『现在还认识』就用现在时, 但since一出现必须完成时。另外knowing也错, know不用进行时。 考点: PSLE爱考since/for信号词锁定现在完成时, 见since选have/has+过去分词"},{"q":"By the time we arrived, the movie ___.","opts":["started","has started","had started","starts"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"过去完成","explain":"By the time + 过去时, 说明电影开始发生在「我们到达」之前, 过去的过去要用 had started (past perfect)。选A started 最迷惑: 它只说过去发生, 分不清先后, 会变成「我们一到电影才开始」。考点: PSLE爱考 by the time + 过去时配 past perfect。"},{"q":"She ___ for two hours before the bus came.","opts":["waited","has waited","had been waiting","waits"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"过去完成进行","explain":"公交来之前她已经持续等了两小时, 「过去某点之前一直在做」用 had been waiting (past perfect continuous), for two hours 强调持续。选B has waited 错在: has是现在完成, 但全句在过去(the bus came), 时间轴对不上。考点: PSLE爱考 for+时长 + before过去时 选过去完成进行。"},{"q":"This time tomorrow, I ___ on the plane.","opts":["sit","will sit","will be sitting","am sitting"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"将来进行","explain":"This time tomorrow 指明天某一刻正在进行的动作, 用 will be sitting (future continuous), 像给未来拍快照。选B will will sit 最迷惑: 它只说会坐, 不能表达「那一刻正坐在飞机上」的进行画面。考点: PSLE爱考 this time tomorrow 定 future continuous。"},{"q":"By next March, he ___ here for ten years.","opts":["works","will work","will have worked","worked"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"将来完成","explain":"By next March 是未来的截止点, 到那时工作满十年, 「未来某点前累计完成」用 will have worked (future perfect)。选B will work 错在: 只说将来会工作, 表达不了「到那时已满十年」的累计感。考点: PSLE爱考 by+将来时间 配 will have + 过去分词。"},{"q":"While I ___ dinner, the phone rang.","opts":["cook","cooked","was cooking","am cooking"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"过去进行","explain":"While 引导过去正在进行的长动作(做饭), 被短动作(电话响)打断, 长动作用 was cooking (past continuous)。选B cooked 最迷惑: 两个都用过去时会变成先做完饭电话才响, 丢了「正在做」的背景感。考点: PSLE爱考 while+过去进行 配 when+一般过去。"},{"q":"The train ___ by the time we reach the station.","opts":["leaves","left","will have left","has left"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"将来完成","explain":"By the time we reach 指将来我们到站那一刻, 火车在那之前已开走, 用 will have left (future perfect)。选D has left 错在: 现在完成说的是「现在已走」, 但到站是将来的事, 时间点不符。考点: PSLE爱考 by the time+一般现在(表将来) 配 future perfect。"},{"q":"She said she ___ the book the day before.","opts":["bought","had bought","has bought","buys"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"过去完成-间接引语","explain":"间接引语里主句 said 是过去时, 买书发生在说话之前(the day before), 过去的过去用 had bought。选A bought 最迷惑: 直接引语可以用过去时, 但转述时要往前退一格, 否则分不清买书在说话前。考点: PSLE爱考间接引语时态后移(backshift)。"},{"q":"I ___ to call you, but I forgot.","opts":["mean","meant","have meant","had meant"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"一般过去","explain":"「本来打算但忘了」是过去一件事, 用一般过去 meant, 和 forgot 同一时间线。选D had meant 最迷惑: 句中没有两个过去动作分先后的需要, meant to do 本身就含「打算了没做成」, 不必用过去完成。考点: PSLE爱考 meant to + but 表过去未实现的打算。"},{"q":"We ___ in Singapore since 2020.","opts":["live","lived","have lived","are living"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-since","explain":"since 2020 表示从过去持续到现在, 用现在完成 have lived。选B lived 最迷惑: 一般过去表示住过但现在不住了, 和 since 的「一直住到现在」矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考 since+年份 是 present perfect 的信号词。"},{"q":"The students ___ their project by Friday.","opts":["finish","finished","will have finished","are finishing"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"将来完成-deadline","explain":"by Friday 是将来的截止日, 到那天之前会完成项目, 用 will have finished (future perfect)。选B finished 错在: 一般过去表示已经完成了, 但周五还没到, 时间方向反了。考点: PSLE爱考 by+deadline 定 future perfect。"},{"q":"He ___ TV when the earthquake struck.","opts":["watches","watched","was watching","has watched"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"过去进行-中断","explain":"地震发生(短动作, struck)打断了看电视(长动作), 长动作用过去进行 was watching。选B watched 最迷惑: 两个一般过去读起来像先看完电视地震才来, 丢了「正在看时被打断」的画面。考点: PSLE爱考 when+短动作 配 past continuous 背景动作。"},{"q":"I wish I ___ harder last semester.","opts":["study","studied","had studied","have studied"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"虚拟-wish过去","explain":"wish + 对过去的后悔, 要比过去再退一格用 had studied (past perfect), last semester 已经过去改不了。选B studied 最迷惑: wish+过去式是对现在的愿望, 但这里后悔的是上学期, 必须用过去完成。考点: PSLE爱考 wish 后悔过去用 had+过去分词。"},{"q":"If I were you, I ___ accept that offer.","opts":["will","would","shall","can"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"虚拟-条件句2","explain":"If I were you 是第二条件句(与现在事实相反的假设), 主句固定用 would + 动词原形。选A will 最迷惑: will 用于真实条件句(第一条件), 但「如果我是你」根本不可能, 必须降级成 would。考点: PSLE爱考 If I were you... I would 固定搭配。"},{"q":"She acts as if she ___ the boss.","opts":["is","was","were","being"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"虚拟-as if","explain":"as if 后说与事实相反的情况(她并不是老板), 虚拟语气一律用 were, 不分单复数。选B was 最迷惑: 口语常听到 she was, 但正式语法和考试里虚拟语气只认 were。考点: PSLE爱考 as if/as though 虚拟用 were。"},{"q":"It is time we ___ home.","opts":["go","went","have gone","going"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"虚拟-it is time","explain":"It is time (that) 后面接过去式 went, 表示「早该回家了」, 是固定虚拟结构, 不是真的过去。选A go 最迷惑: 按字面「是时候走了」好像该用原形, 但 It is time we 后必须退一格用过去式。考点: PSLE爱考 It is (high) time + 过去式。"},{"q":"She ___ here since Monday.","opts":["is","was","has been","had been"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-since","explain":"since Monday 表示从周一持续到现在, 用现在完成 has been。选D had been 最迷惑: 过去完成需要另一个更晚的过去动作作参照, 这句没有, 一直连到「现在」就用 has。考点: PSLE爱考 since+时间点 选 present perfect。"},{"q":"They ___ married for 20 years next month.","opts":["are","will be","will have been","have been"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"将来完成-持续","explain":"next month 是将来时间点, 到那时结婚满20年, 「将来某点前持续满」用 will have been (future perfect)。选D have been 最迷惑: 现在完成说「已经满20年」, 但满20年是下个月的事, 还没到。考点: PSLE爱考 for+时长 + next时间 配 future perfect。"},{"q":"The children ___ already ___ their lunch.","opts":["have/eaten","had/eaten","has/eaten","are/eating"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-already","explain":"already 配现在完成, children 是复数, 助动词用 have, 所以 have eaten。选C has/eaten 最迷惑: 时态选对了但主谓不一致, children 不是单数, has 只配第三人称单数。考点: PSLE爱考 already 定现在完成+主谓一致双重陷阱。"},{"q":"He ___ to school every day last year.","opts":["walks","walked","has walked","was walking"],"ans":1,"diff":2,"tag":"一般过去-习惯","explain":"last year 是明确的过去时间, every day 说的是过去的习惯, 用一般过去 walked。选D was walking 最迷惑: 进行时描述某一刻正在走, 表达不了「每天都走」的反复习惯。考点: PSLE爱考 last year 等过去时间词锁定 simple past。"},{"q":"I ___ never ___ such a beautiful sunset.","opts":["have/seen","had/seen","was/seeing","am/seeing"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-never","explain":"never 配现在完成表示「至今从未见过」, 主语 I 用 have seen。选B had/seen 最迷惑: 过去完成要有另一个过去动作作参照点, 这句是感叹到现在为止的经历, 没有参照点就用 have。考点: PSLE爱考 never/ever 是 present perfect 信号词。"},{"q":"We ___ just ___ when it started to rain.","opts":["had/left","have/left","were/leaving","did/leave"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"过去完成-just","explain":"just 表示「刚刚离开」, 而离开发生在下雨(过去时 started)之前, 过去的过去用 had left。选B have/left 最迷惑: 现在完成不能和过去时间点连用, 全句锚在过去的雨, 必须退到 had。考点: PSLE爱考 had just done + when 过去时。"},{"q":"She ___ the piano since she was five.","opts":["plays","played","has played","is playing"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"现在完成-since从句","explain":"since she was five 从五岁持续弹到现在, 用现在完成 has played; since 从句里用过去式是正常的。选B played 最迷惑: 主句用一般过去就成了「以前弹过现在不弹了」, 和 since 的持续义冲突。考点: PSLE爱考 since+过去时从句 主句配 present perfect。"},{"q":"Don't disturb her. She ___.","opts":["sleeps","slept","is sleeping","has slept"],"ans":2,"diff":2,"tag":"现在进行-此刻","explain":"「别打扰她」说明她此刻正在睡, 用现在进行 is sleeping。选A sleeps 最迷惑: 一般现在表示习惯(她平时睡觉), 不能表达「现在正睡着」这个当下状态。考点: PSLE爱考语境暗示 now 定 present continuous。"},{"q":"My father ___ before I woke up.","opts":["leaves","left","had left","has left"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"过去完成-先于过去","explain":"before I woke up 是过去时, 爸爸离开在我醒来之前, 过去的过去用 had left (past perfect)。选B left 最迷惑: 有 before 好像也能分先后, 但PSLE标准是主句先发生的动作用过去完成, 强调先后关系。考点: PSLE爱考 before+过去时 主句用 past perfect。"},{"q":"I promise I ___ you tomorrow.","opts":["call","called","will call","am calling"],"ans":2,"diff":2,"tag":"将来时-promise","explain":"promise 承诺的是明天的事, tomorrow 定将来时, 用 will call。选D am calling 最迷惑: 现在进行也能表将来, 但那要是已定好的计划安排, 承诺一个动作用 will 才对。考点: PSLE爱考 tomorrow+promise 定 simple future。"},{"q":"You ___ finish your homework before playing.","opts":["must","can","may","might"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-must义务","explain":"must表示义务, 意思是「必须先做完作业才能玩」, 语气强硬没商量。can错在只说「能不能」, 不带任何强制要求, 放这句里就变成「你可以做作业」, 完全丢了规矩的意思。考点: PSLE爱考情态动词强弱, 义务规定用must"},{"q":"She ___ swim when she was three.","opts":["can","could","may","must"],"ans":1,"diff":2,"tag":"情态-could过去能力","explain":"when she was three是过去时间, 过去的能力要用could, 即can的过去式。can最迷惑, 表示的是现在的能力, 和「三岁时」这个过去时间信号词冲突, 时间对不上。考点: PSLE爱考when she was...过去信号词逼你把can改成could"},{"q":"___ I borrow your pen?","opts":["May","Must","Should","Will"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"情态-may请求","explain":"借东西是礼貌请求许可, 用May I...?最正统, 意思是「我可以借吗」。Must错得最有迷惑性, Must I意思变成「我非得借你的笔不可吗」, 像在抱怨, 不是请求。考点: PSLE爱考礼貌请求, May I是标准客气句型"},{"q":"You ___ not park here. It is illegal.","opts":["must","need","can","may"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-must not禁止","explain":"must not表示禁止, 「这里不准停车」, 后面It is illegal点明是法律禁止, 语气必须最强。may最迷惑, may not只是「可能不」或「不允许」的弱说法, 撑不起illegal这种硬规定。考点: PSLE爱考禁止类, 看到illegal/against the rules就选must not"},{"q":"He ___ be at home. His car is in the driveway.","opts":["must","can","may","should"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-must推测","explain":"must在这里不是「必须」而是「一定是」, 表示有把握的推测: 车在门口, 他一定在家。may最迷惑, 只表示「可能在家」, 但证据这么明显, 弱弱的may配不上这份把握。考点: PSLE爱考must的第二个身份=肯定推测, 后句必给证据"},{"q":"You ___ see a doctor. That cough sounds bad.","opts":["should","must","can","may"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-should建议","explain":"should表示建议, 「你该去看医生」, 语气温和是关心不是命令。must最迷惑, 语气太硬变成强制命令, 朋友间提建议不用它, 而且咳嗽严重也只是建议理由不是法规。考点: PSLE爱考建议用should, 命令才用must"},{"q":"She ___ have left already. The door is locked.","opts":["must","can","should","would"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"情态-must have过去推测","explain":"must have + 过去分词表示对过去的肯定推测: 门锁了, 她一定已经走了。should最迷惑, should have left意思是「本该走却没走」, 是责备不是推测, 和门锁着的证据矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考must have done=对过去事情的肯定推断"},{"q":"You ___ not have eaten so much cake.","opts":["should","must","can","may"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-should not have","explain":"should not have + 过去分词表示「本不该做却做了」, 事后责备吃太多蛋糕, 正合语境。must最迷惑, 但must not have done表示「一定没做过」, 是推测不是责备, 意思全反了。考点: PSLE爱考shouldn't have done=事后后悔责备句型"},{"q":"He ___ speak three languages fluently.","opts":["can","may","must","shall"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"情态-can能力","explain":"can表示能力, 「他会说三门语言」, fluently说明这是他的本事。may最迷惑, 表示可能性或许可, He may speak变成「他也许会说」, 把确定的本领说成了猜测。考点: PSLE爱考can表能力, 看到speak/swim等技能动词优先想can"},{"q":"Students ___ hand in their work by Monday.","opts":["shall","may","can","must"],"ans":3,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-must要求","explain":"must表示硬性要求, 「必须在周一前交作业」, by Monday是死线, 老师规定没商量。shall最迷惑, 放第一格看着像正式规定, 但现代英语shall很少这样用, PSLE按ans选must。考点: PSLE爱考截止日期by+时间配must表强制要求"},{"q":"___ you help me carry this box?","opts":["Could","Must","Should","May"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"情态-could请求","explain":"Could you...?是礼貌请求帮忙的标准句型, 比Can更客气, 「能帮我搬箱子吗」。Should最迷惑, Should you意思变成「你是否应该」, 是在讨论对方的义务, 不是开口求助。考点: PSLE爱考请人帮忙用Could you, 礼貌请求固定搭配"},{"q":"She ___ be the new teacher. She looks very young.","opts":["can't","mustn't","shouldn't","won't"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-can't否定推测","explain":"can't表示否定推测「不可能是」: 她看着太年轻, 不可能是新老师。mustn't最迷惑, 很多孩子以为must的推测否定还用must, 但mustn't只表示「不准」, 推测的否定必须换成can't。考点: PSLE爱考推测否定, must be的反面是can't be不是mustn't be"},{"q":"You ___ worry. Everything will be fine.","opts":["needn't","mustn't","can't","shouldn't"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-needn't","explain":"needn't表示「不必」, 「你不用担心, 一切会好的」, 是安慰话。mustn't最迷惑, 意思是「不准担心」, 变成下命令禁止人担心, 安慰话不能这么凶。考点: PSLE爱考needn't不必 vs mustn't禁止, 意思差很远"},{"q":"He ___ to apologize for his rude behaviour.","opts":["ought","must","should","need"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-ought to","explain":"空格后有to, 只有ought能接to, ought to = should表示应该道歉。should最迷惑, 意思完全对但should后面直接跟动词原形, 不能加to, 填进去变should to就错了。考点: PSLE爱考ought to是唯一带to的情态词, 看到to锁定ought"},{"q":"You ___ better hurry or you will miss the bus.","opts":["had","would","should","could"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-had better","explain":"had better是固定短语「最好快点」, 否则误车, 只有had能填。should最迷惑, 意思相近但没有should better这个搭配, 想表达同义得说should hurry。考点: PSLE爱考had better+动词原形, 固定搭配不能拆开换字"},{"q":"I ___ rather stay home than go out in the rain.","opts":["would","should","had","could"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"情态-would rather","explain":"would rather...than...是固定句型「宁愿在家也不出门」, 只能用would。had最迷惑, 因为有had better这个近亲, 孩子容易串台, 但rather只跟would搭。考点: PSLE爱考would rather配than, 和had better别混成一家"},{"q":"She ___ have arrived by now. The flight was at 6.","opts":["should","must","could","would"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"情态-should have预期","explain":"should have + 过去分词表示「按理现在该到了」, 航班6点起飞, 这是合理预期。must最迷惑, must have arrived是「肯定已经到了」, 但说话人其实没把握, 只是推算时间, 语气过头。考点: PSLE爱考should have done表按理该发生的预期"},{"q":"Need I ___ this form?","opts":["fill","to fill","filling","filled"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"情态-need原形","explain":"Need放句首当情态动词用, 后面必须接动词原形fill, 「我需要填这张表吗」。to fill最迷惑, 因为need也能当普通动词接to do, 但那样句子得写成Do I need to fill, 这里Need已提前, 只能配原形。考点: PSLE爱考need双重身份, 情态用法后接原形"},{"q":"You ___ as well take a taxi. The bus is late.","opts":["may","must","should","can"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"情态-may as well","explain":"may as well是固定短语「不如就」, 公交晚点, 不如打车, 只有may能填。must最迷惑, 看着语气通顺, 但英语里没有must as well这个搭配, 固定短语一个字都不能换。考点: PSLE爱考may as well=不如做某事, 整体记不拆字"},{"q":"He ___ swim across the river when he was young.","opts":["was able to","can","is able to","could have"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"情态-was able to具体","explain":"was able to表示过去的能力, when he was young是过去时间, 只有它时态对。could have最迷惑, could have swum意思是「本可以游但没游」, 表示没发生的事, 和陈述他当年会游泳矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考过去能力用could/was able to, could have done是没做成"},{"q":"The cake ___ by my mother yesterday.","opts":["baked","was baked","is baked","bakes"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"被动-过去","explain":"蛋糕是被烤的, 要用被动语态, yesterday定过去时, 所以was baked。baked最迷惑, 看着像过去式很顺眼, 但主动语态变成「蛋糕自己烤了」, 蛋糕不会烤东西。考点: PSLE爱考主语是物+by某人=被动, 再看时间词定时态"},{"q":"English ___ in many countries.","opts":["speaks","spoke","is spoken","spoken"],"ans":2,"diff":3,"tag":"被动-一般现在","explain":"英语是被人说的, 主语是物要用被动, 一般现在的事实用is spoken。spoken最迷惑, 分词形式对但缺了be动词, 被动语态必须be+过去分词两件套, 少一件都不行。考点: PSLE爱考被动结构be+过去分词, 光有分词没有be是陷阱"},{"q":"The homework ___ before dinner.","opts":["must finish","must be finished","must finished","finishing"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-情态","explain":"作业是被完成的, 情态动词的被动是must be + 过去分词, 所以must be finished。must finished最迷惑, 有过去分词像被动, 但情态动词后不能直接跟分词, 中间必须夹be。考点: PSLE爱考情态被动公式must/can/should+be+done, be不能省"},{"q":"The window ___ by the strong wind.","opts":["broke","was broken","broken","breaking"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"被动-过去","explain":"窗户是被风吹破的, by the strong wind点明动作发出者, 被动用was broken。broke最迷惑, 是break的过去式看着通顺, 但主动语态意思成了「窗户打破了别的东西」, 和by冲突。考点: PSLE爱考by短语是被动语态信号, 见by先想was/were+done"},{"q":"A new school ___ in our area next year.","opts":["will build","will be built","builds","built"],"ans":1,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-将来","explain":"学校是被建的, next year定将来时, 将来被动=will be + 过去分词, 选will be built。will build最迷惑, 将来时对了但是主动语态, 意思变成「学校自己去盖楼」, 主语是物必须被动。考点: PSLE爱考将来被动will be done, 时态和语态两关都要过"},{"q":"The thief ___ by the police last night.","opts":["caught","was caught","catches","is caught"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"被动-过去","explain":"last night是过去时间, 小偷是「被抓」, 被动语态要 be + 过去分词, 所以用 was caught。最迷惑的是 caught, 它只有动词没有 be, 变成小偷主动去抓, 意思反了。考点: PSLE爱考「主语是动作承受者」就必须加be动词。"},{"q":"These books ___ to the library tomorrow.","opts":["return","returned","will be returned","returning"],"ans":2,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-将来","explain":"tomorrow是将来信号词, 书是「被还」, 将来被动 = will be + 过去分词, 选 will be returned。最迷惑的是 returned, 单独用像过去式, 既没有will也没有be, 时态和语态双错。考点: PSLE爱考时间信号词定时态, 被动还要补齐 be。"},{"q":"The room ___ cleaned every day.","opts":["is","was","has","be"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"被动-一般现在","explain":"every day表示习惯, 用一般现在时被动: is + cleaned。主语 room 是单数, 所以选 is。最迷惑的是 was, 语法结构对但时态错, every day 说的是天天如此, 不是过去某次。考点: PSLE爱考 every day/always 锁定 simple present。"},{"q":"The letter ___ already ___.","opts":["has/been sent","was/sent","is/sending","had/sent"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-现在完成","explain":"already是现在完成时信号词, 完成时被动 = has been + 过去分词, 拆开就是 has...been sent。最迷惑的是 was/sent, 看着通顺, 但 already 强调「已经完成、影响到现在」, 该用 present perfect 不用 past。考点: PSLE爱考 already/just/yet 配 has been done。"},{"q":"The bridge ___ being repaired when we passed.","opts":["is","was","has","had"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"被动-过去进行","explain":"when we passed 是过去的时间点, 桥当时正在被修, 过去进行被动 = was being repaired, 所以填 was。最迷惑的是 is, 后面接 being 结构没错, 但和过去的 when 从句时态打架。考点: PSLE爱考主句从句时态要一致。"},{"q":"She ___ given a prize for her hard work.","opts":["is","was","has","had"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"被动-间接宾语","explain":"奖已经发了, 是过去发生的事, 过去被动 = was + given, 选 was。最迷惑的是 had, 有人以为 had given 是完成时, 但那是主动语态「她给了别人」, 意思全反。考点: PSLE爱考人做主语的被动句, be动词不能丢。"},{"q":"All tickets ___ sold out by noon.","opts":["have been","had been","were being","are being"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-现在完成","explain":"by noon到中午时票「已经卖光」, 强调结果持续到现在, 用现在完成被动 have been sold。tickets复数配 have。最迷惑的是 had been, 那是过去完成, 要有另一个更晚的过去动作作参照才用, 这里没有。考点: PSLE爱考 have been 和 had been 的分界线。"},{"q":"The results ___ announced next week.","opts":["will be","will","are","were"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"被动-将来","explain":"next week是将来信号词, 结果是「被宣布」, 将来被动 = will be + announced, 选 will be。最迷惑的是 will, 少了 be 就成了主动「结果自己去宣布」, 不通。考点: PSLE爱考将来被动 will be done, be 是送分也是丢分点。"},{"q":"He ___ known to be a generous man.","opts":["is","has","was being","being"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-be known","explain":"be known 是固定被动表达, 「他是出了名的慷慨」是现在的事实, 用 is known。最迷惑的是 has, has known 是主动完成时「他认识...」, 主语变成认识别人的人, 意思错。考点: PSLE爱考 be known to/as/for 固定搭配。"},{"q":"The meeting ___ postponed until Friday.","opts":["has been","has","is being","was being"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"被动-现在完成","explain":"会议「已被推迟」到周五, 强调现在的结果, 现在完成被动 = has been postponed。最迷惑的是 was being, 过去进行被动指「当时正被推迟中」, 推迟是一瞬间的决定, 不能进行中。考点: PSLE爱考推迟取消类动词配 has been。"},{"q":"I stayed home ___ I was feeling sick.","opts":["because","although","unless","so"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"连词-because原因","explain":"前果后因: 待在家是结果, 生病是原因, 引出原因用 because。最迷惑的是 so, 它也表因果但方向相反, so 后面接结果, 这里空格后是原因, 用 so 逻辑就倒了。考点: PSLE爱考 because 接原因、so 接结果, 方向别搞反。"},{"q":"___ it was raining, we went out to play.","opts":["Although","Because","Unless","Since"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-although让步","explain":"下雨和出去玩相反, 是让步关系, 用 Although「虽然」。最迷惑的是 Because, 「因为下雨所以出去玩」逻辑不通, 连词题先看两句意思顺不顺。考点: PSLE爱考前后句意思相反选 although, 顺承选 because。"},{"q":"You will fail ___ you study harder.","opts":["unless","if","because","although"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-unless","explain":"unless = if...not, 「除非你更用功, 否则会不及格」, 逻辑通。最迷惑的是 if, 「如果你更用功就会不及格」意思完全反了, 很多孩子只看结构不读意思就掉坑。考点: PSLE爱考 unless 藏着否定, 翻成「除非」再检查逻辑。"},{"q":"He ran fast ___ he could catch the bus.","opts":["so that","because","although","unless"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-so that目的","explain":"跑得快是为了赶上巴士, 表目的用 so that, 后面常配 could/can。最迷惑的是 because, 「因为能赶上巴士所以跑得快」因果颠倒, 目的和原因方向相反。考点: PSLE爱考 so that + can/could 表目的。"},{"q":"I will wait ___ you come back.","opts":["until","unless","although","because"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-until","explain":"「一直等到你回来」, 表动作持续到某时刻, 用 until。最迷惑的是 unless, 长得像但意思是「除非」, 「除非你回来否则我等」逻辑别扭。考点: PSLE爱考 wait/stay 配 until, 看到等待类动词先想 until。"},{"q":"___ I finish my work, I will join you.","opts":["Once","Unless","Although","Because"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-once","explain":"Once = 一旦...就..., 「一旦做完作业就来找你」, 时间顺承通顺。最迷惑的是 Unless, 「除非我做完否则来找你」意思拧了, 两句是先后关系不是条件否定。考点: PSLE爱考 once 表「一...就」, 从句用现在时代替将来时。"},{"q":"She is ___ kind ___ helpful.","opts":["both/and","either/or","neither/nor","not only/but"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-both...and","explain":"kind 和 helpful 两个优点都有, 两者兼有用 both...and。最迷惑的是 not only/but, 意思也通, 但正确格式是 not only...but also, 选项缺 also, 结构不完整。考点: PSLE爱考成对连词要原封不动配对, 缺一个词就错。"},{"q":"___ only is he smart, ___ also hardworking.","opts":["Not/but","Both/and","Either/or","Neither/nor"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-not only...but also","explain":"Not only...but also 固定搭配「不但...而且」, 首词 Not 对上题目里的 only, 后半 but 对上 also。最迷惑的是 Both/and, both 后面不能接 only, and 也和句尾 also 不搭。考点: PSLE爱考 not only 放句首, 拿题目已给的 only 和 also 当钥匙。"},{"q":"You can have ___ tea ___ coffee.","opts":["either/or","neither/nor","both/and","not/but"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-either...or","explain":"茶或咖啡二选一, 用 either...or。最迷惑的是 both...and, 「两个都要」在 can have 的语境也说得通, 但二选一的口气加上「或者」逻辑, either/or 才是标准答案。考点: PSLE爱考 either...or 选一个、neither...nor 全否定、both...and 全都要。"},{"q":"I like swimming ___ my brother prefers running.","opts":["while","because","so","unless"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-while对比","explain":"我爱游泳、哥哥爱跑步, 两人对比用 while「而」。最迷惑的是 because, 「因为哥哥爱跑步所以我爱游泳」毫无因果, 硬套就错。考点: PSLE爱考 while 表两人两事对比, 不只是「当...时候」。"},{"q":"___ hard she tried, she could not solve it.","opts":["However","Although","Because","Unless"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"连词-however让步","explain":"However + 形容词/副词 = 无论多么..., 「无论多努力都解不出」, 直接修饰 hard。最迷惑的是 Although, 意思接近但语法不容许 Although hard she tried 这种语序, although 后要接完整句子。考点: PSLE爱考 however + adj/adv + 主语的倒装式让步。"},{"q":"Take an umbrella ___ it rains.","opts":["in case","unless","although","because"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"连词-in case","explain":"in case = 以防万一, 「带伞以防下雨」, 是预防不是原因。最迷惑的是 because, 「因为下雨所以带伞」好像也通, 但句子说的是还没下雨先防着, 不是已经在下。考点: PSLE爱考 in case 表预防, 和 because 用「事情发生没有」区分。"},{"q":"She speaks ___ she were the boss.","opts":["as if","because","although","so that"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"连词-as if","explain":"as if = 好像, 「她说话好像她是老板似的」, 后面配 were 表示假设不是事实。最迷惑的是 so that, 表目的要配 can/could, 这里没有, 且「为了当老板而说话」不通。考点: PSLE爱考 as if + were 表虚拟, she 后接 were 不是错。"},{"q":"I have not seen him ___ he left Singapore.","opts":["since","until","while","because"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-since","explain":"since + 过去时间点, 主句用现在完成时 have not seen, 「自从他离开就没见过」完全吻合。最迷惑的是 until, 「直到他离开才没见他」逻辑混乱, until 配的是动作的终点不是起点。考点: PSLE爱考 have done + since 黄金组合, 见完成时先找 since。"},{"q":"___ he is rich, he is not happy.","opts":["Although","Because","Since","Unless"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"连词-although","explain":"有钱和不快乐相反, 让步用 Although。最迷惑的是 Since, 它有「既然」的意思, 「既然有钱所以不快乐」因果不成立, 前后相反就不能选表原因的词。考点: PSLE爱考句意转折选 although, 先判断两句是顺是反。"},{"q":"She is a teacher, ___?","opts":["isn't she","is she","doesn't she","does she"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"反问-be肯→否","explain":"前句是肯定句用了be动词is, 反问尾巴要变否定并沿用同一个动词, 所以是isn't she。选doesn't she错在: 句中已有is, 不能另请do家族来帮忙, does只服务实义动词。考点: PSLE爱考question tag前肯后否+动词照抄原句"},{"q":"They don't like pizza, ___?","opts":["do they","don't they","are they","aren't they"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"反问-do否→肯","explain":"前句don't like是否定, 尾巴要反过来变肯定, 助动词沿用do, 所以是do they。最迷惑的是don't they: 它和前句同为否定, 违反一正一反的规则。考点: PSLE爱考否定句反问尾巴必须翻成肯定"},{"q":"He can swim, ___?","opts":["can't he","can he","does he","doesn't he"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"反问-can","explain":"句中有情态动词can, 尾巴就用can的否定can't he, 情态动词自己当家不请do。选doesn't he错在: 有can在场时不能换成do家族, 动词必须原班人马。考点: PSLE爱考情态动词句的question tag直接用该情态词"},{"q":"Let's go to the park, ___?","opts":["shall we","will we","do we","can we"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"反问-let's","explain":"Let's开头的建议句是固定搭配, 尾巴一律用shall we, 表示邀请对方一起。选will we错在: Let's句不看主语将来时, 这是死规矩不是推理题。考点: PSLE爱考Let's..., shall we固定句型"},{"q":"You won't tell anyone, ___?","opts":["will you","won't you","do you","don't you"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"反问-won't→will","explain":"won't是否定, 尾巴反过来用肯定will you, 助动词沿用will。最迷惑的是won't you: 前后都否定就重复了, 违反前否后肯规则。考点: PSLE爱考缩写词里藏着的否定(won't=will not)"},{"q":"There is a book on the table, ___?","opts":["isn't there","is there","aren't there","are there"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"反问-there is","explain":"There is句型的尾巴把there当主语用, 肯定句配否定尾巴isn't there。选aren't there错在: 主语a book是单数, 动词必须保持is, 不能换成are。考点: PSLE爱考there be句型反问用there不用it"},{"q":"She has finished her work, ___?","opts":["hasn't she","has she","didn't she","did she"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"反问-has完成","explain":"句子用了现在完成时has finished, 尾巴沿用has变否定hasn't she。最迷惑的是didn't she: finished看着像过去式, 但前面有has坐镇, 是完成时不是过去时。考点: PSLE爱考has+过去分词的尾巴用hasn't不用didn't"},{"q":"Nobody came to the party, ___?","opts":["did they","didn't they","did he","didn't he"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"反问-nobody","explain":"Nobody本身含否定意思, 尾巴要用肯定did they; nobody回指时惯用they。选didn't they错在: 前句已经否定(nobody=没人), 尾巴再否定就双重否定了。考点: PSLE爱考nobody/no one自带否定且代词用they"},{"q":"I am late, ___?","opts":["aren't I","am I","isn't I","don't I"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"反问-I am特殊","explain":"I am的反问是英语特例, 没有amn't I这个词, 一律借用aren't I。选isn't I错在: is配he/she/it, 从来不配I, 纯属生造。考点: PSLE爱考I am..., aren't I?这个不讲理的特殊搭配"},{"q":"Everyone enjoyed the show, ___?","opts":["didn't they","did they","didn't he","don't they"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"反问-everyone","explain":"everyone语法上是单数但反问代词用they, 前句enjoyed是过去时肯定句, 尾巴用didn't they。最迷惑的是didn't he: everyone不指某个男生, 回指必须用they。考点: PSLE爱考everyone/everybody尾巴代词统一用they"},{"q":"She said, \"I am tired.\" → She said that she ___ tired.","opts":["was","is","has been","will be"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"间接引语-am→was","explain":"直接引语变间接引语, 主句said是过去时, 引语里的时态要跟着退一步: am退成was。选is错在: 报告过去说的话, 现在时不退等于没换挡, said和is时态打架。考点: PSLE爱考reported speech时态倒退一格(backshift)"},{"q":"He said, \"I will come.\" → He said he ___ come.","opts":["would","will","can","shall"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"间接引语-will→would","explain":"said是过去时, 引语里的will要退成would, 这是情态动词的倒退规则。选will错在: 主句已是过去, will原地不动就和said不配套了。考点: PSLE爱考will→would/can→could成对倒退"},{"q":"Tom said, \"I have finished.\" → Tom said he ___ finished.","opts":["had","has","have","having"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-have→had","explain":"said过去时带动引语时态后退: have finished(现在完成)退成had finished(过去完成)。选has错在: 主语he本可配has, 但间接引语必须倒退, has没退到位。考点: PSLE爱考现在完成时转述后变past perfect"},{"q":"She asked, \"Do you like coffee?\" → She asked ___ I liked coffee.","opts":["if","that","what","do"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-一般疑问","explain":"转述一般疑问句(yes/no问题)要用if或whether来引导, 表示是否。最迷惑的是that: that只转述陈述句, 转述问题就把疑问的味道弄丢了。考点: PSLE爱考yes/no问句转述用if/whether引导"},{"q":"He asked, \"Where do you live?\" → He asked where I ___.","opts":["lived","live","living","had lived"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-特殊疑问","explain":"转述特殊疑问句, where后面改用陈述语序, 时态跟asked倒退: live退成lived。选live错在: 语序改对了但时态没退, asked是过去, 引语也要过去。考点: PSLE爱考wh-问句转述要变陈述语序+时态倒退"},{"q":"She told me, \"Don't be late.\" → She told me ___ be late.","opts":["not to","don't","to not","didn't"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-祈使否定","explain":"否定祈使句转述的固定公式: told sb not to do, not放在to前面。最迷惑的是to not: 意思能懂但语序错, 标准写法not to才拿分。考点: PSLE爱考Don't...转述成told sb not to do"},{"q":"\"Can you help me?\" she asked. → She asked if I ___ help her.","opts":["could","can","will","may"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-can→could","explain":"asked是过去时, 引语里的can倒退成could, 情态动词也要跟着换挡。选can错在: 主句过去时, can不退就和asked不同步了。考点: PSLE爱考间接引语can→could/may→might倒退"},{"q":"He said, \"I saw her yesterday.\" → He said he ___ her the day before.","opts":["had seen","saw","has seen","sees"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"间接引语-saw→had seen","explain":"直接引语里的过去时saw, 转述时再退一格变过去完成had seen, 因为看的动作发生在说之前的之前。最迷惑的是saw: 只退了主句没退引语, yesterday变the day before也提示要双重后退。考点: PSLE爱考simple past转述后变had+过去分词"},{"q":"Mum said, \"Clean your room.\" → Mum told me ___ my room.","opts":["to clean","clean","cleaning","cleaned"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"间接引语-祈使肯定","explain":"肯定祈使句转述公式: told sb to do sth, 动词前必须加to。选clean错在: 直接照抄原话的动词原形, 忘了转述要套to do的壳。考点: PSLE爱考祈使句转述用tell/ask sb to do"},{"q":"\"I am leaving tomorrow,\" she said. → She said she was leaving ___.","opts":["the next day","tomorrow","yesterday","today"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"间接引语-时间转换","explain":"转述时时间词也要换算: tomorrow从说话那天算, 转述后变the next day/the following day。最迷惑的是tomorrow: 现在转述时那个明天早过了, 不换就时间错乱。考点: PSLE爱考间接引语时间词换算(tomorrow→the next day)"},{"q":"There is ___ milk left in the fridge.","opts":["a few","a little","many","few"],"ans":1,"diff":3,"tag":"限定-不可数little","explain":"milk是不可数名词, 只能配a little表示还有一点。最迷惑的是a few: 它专配可数复数名词如a few apples, 牛奶数不出一个两个。考点: PSLE爱考a little配不可数/a few配可数的分工"},{"q":"He has ___ friends in the new school.","opts":["a few","a little","much","little"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"限定-可数a few","explain":"friends是可数复数, 用a few表示有几个朋友, 语气是肯定的有。最迷惑的是a little: 只能配不可数名词, 朋友是一个一个数的。考点: PSLE爱考名词可数与否决定选few家族还是little家族"},{"q":"There are ___ apples on the table.","opts":["some","a","an","much"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"限定-some可数","explain":"apples是复数, 肯定句里表示一些用some。最迷惑的是much: much配不可数名词且多用于否定疑问句, 苹果可数直接排除。考点: PSLE爱考some配复数可数名词的肯定句"},{"q":"___ student must wear a uniform.","opts":["Every","All","Some","Most"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"限定-every单数","explain":"空格后的student是单数, 只有Every能配单数名词, 意思是每一个学生。最迷惑的是All: 意思相近但All后面要接复数students, 单复数不合。考点: PSLE爱考every+单数名词vs all+复数名词"},{"q":"I don't have ___ money with me.","opts":["any","some","many","few"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"限定-any否定","explain":"否定句don't have里表示任何要用any, some见到否定要变身。最迷惑的是some: 它是肯定句专用, 进了否定句就要换成any。考点: PSLE爱考some用于肯定句/any用于否定和疑问句"},{"q":"___ of the students passed the test.","opts":["Most","Every","Each","Much"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"限定-most of","explain":"Most of + the + 复数名词, 意思是「大部分学生」, 动词用复数passed也对得上。Each虽然也能配of, 但要写成Each of the students, 后面动词得用单数passes, 和句子不合。考点: PSLE爱考Most/Each/Much接of的搭配和单复数一致"},{"q":"There is ___ point in arguing with him.","opts":["no","not","none","any"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"限定-no+名词","explain":"固定短语 there is no point in doing something = 做某事没意义, no直接放名词point前面。not最迷惑, 但not是副词, 不能直接修饰名词, 要说not any point才行。考点: PSLE爱考no+名词的固定搭配, no=not any"},{"q":"We have ___ time to waste.","opts":["little","few","a few","a little"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"限定-little否定意","explain":"time是不可数名词, 又要表达「几乎没有时间」的否定意味, 用little。a little最迷惑, 它是肯定意「还有一点」, 和to waste(不能浪费)的语气矛盾。few只配可数名词。考点: PSLE爱考little/few配可数不可数+有无a的褒贬"},{"q":"___ information was given to us.","opts":["Little","Few","A few","Many"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"限定-little不可数","explain":"information是不可数名词, 「几乎没给什么信息」用Little。Few最迷惑, 意思也是「很少」, 但few只能修饰可数复数名词, information永远不可数不加s。考点: PSLE爱考information/advice/news这类不可数名词的限定词"},{"q":"He ate ___ whole cake by himself!","opts":["the","a","an","some"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"限定-the特指","explain":"whole cake是特指他吃掉的那一整个蛋糕, 说话双方都知道是哪个, 用the; a whole cake语法上也通, 但感叹「整个都吃了!」时英语习惯说the whole。a最迷惑, 因为whole前确实常见a, 但这里强调特定那一个。考点: PSLE爱考the特指vs a泛指"},{"q":"Please turn ___ the lights before you leave.","opts":["off","on","up","in"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-turn off","explain":"离开前要「关灯」, turn off=关掉电器。turn on最迷惑, 是「打开」, 但before you leave这个情境提示人走灯灭, 开着灯走反而不合常理。考点: PSLE爱考phrasal verb要靠句子情境选介词, 不能只背动词"},{"q":"I need to look ___ this word in the dictionary.","opts":["up","at","for","into"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-look up查找","explain":"look up=在词典里查(单词), 是查字典的专用搭配。look for最迷惑, 意思是「寻找丢失的东西」, 查生词的意思要用look up, in the dictionary就是信号。考点: PSLE爱考look up/look for/look at的区分, 见dictionary选up"},{"q":"She takes ___ her mother in appearance.","opts":["after","on","up","off"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-take after像","explain":"take after=长得像(长辈), in appearance(外貌上)是明显信号。take on最迷惑, 意思是「承担/呈现」, 不能表示和妈妈长得像。这类phrasal verb意思和字面无关, 要整个背。考点: PSLE爱考take after表「像家人」, 配mother/father必考"},{"q":"We must carry ___ the experiment carefully.","opts":["out","on","off","in"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-carry out执行","explain":"carry out=执行/进行(实验、计划), carry out the experiment是科学课标准搭配。carry on最迷惑, 意思是「继续」, 后面一般接doing或不接宾语, 不和experiment搭配成「做实验」。考点: PSLE爱考carry out+experiment/plan/instructions"},{"q":"He turned ___ the job offer because the pay was low.","opts":["down","off","up","on"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-turn down拒绝","explain":"turn down=拒绝(工作、邀请), 后半句because the pay was low说明他不要这份工作。turn off最迷惑, 只表示关电器, 不能拒绝offer。看到offer/invitation+拒绝理由就选down。考点: PSLE爱考turn down拒绝vs turn off关闭"},{"q":"The plane will take ___ at 3 pm.","opts":["off","on","up","in"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-take off起飞","explain":"take off=起飞, 主语是plane就是铁信号, 飞机3点起飞。take on最迷惑, 有「搭载/承担」的意思, 但表示飞机离地升空只能用take off。考点: PSLE爱考take off一词多义: 飞机起飞/脱衣服, 主语是plane选off"},{"q":"I can't make ___ what the sign says.","opts":["out","up","off","in"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-make out辨认","explain":"make out=辨认出、看清(模糊的字或东西), can't make out=看不清招牌写什么。make up最迷惑, 是「编造」, 但这里不是编故事而是看不清, sign(招牌)提示是视觉辨认。考点: PSLE爱考make out辨认vs make up编造, 看语境定"},{"q":"She made ___ a story to avoid punishment.","opts":["up","out","off","in"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-make up编造","explain":"make up=编造(故事、借口), 为了逃避惩罚编了个故事, made up a story是固定搭配。make out最迷惑, 是「辨认」, 辨认故事说不通, to avoid punishment说明是撒谎编的。考点: PSLE爱考make up+story/excuse表编造"},{"q":"Please fill ___ this form and return it.","opts":["in","out","up","on"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-fill in填写","explain":"fill in=填写(表格), fill in the form是英式/新加坡标准说法。fill out最迷惑, 美式英语也表示填表, 意思其实一样, 但PSLE按题库以fill in为准, 两个都认识最稳。考点: PSLE爱考fill in+form, 新加坡教材用英式fill in"},{"q":"He set ___ on his journey early in the morning.","opts":["off","out","up","in"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-set off出发","explain":"set off=出发、启程, set off on a journey是固定搭配, journey是信号词。set out最迷惑, 也有出发的意思, 但常见搭配是set out to do something(着手做), 接on his journey时题库以set off为准。考点: PSLE爱考set off+journey表出发"},{"q":"They called ___ the meeting due to the storm.","opts":["off","on","up","in"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-call off取消","explain":"call off=取消(会议、活动), 因为暴风雨把会议取消了, due to the storm是原因信号。call on最迷惑, 意思是「拜访/号召」, 和取消完全不同。想成: call off=cancel。考点: PSLE爱考call off+meeting/match表因故取消"},{"q":"I ran ___ my old teacher at the market.","opts":["into","on","out","off"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-run into偶遇","explain":"run into=偶然遇见(人), 在市场碰到老师是巧遇, run into=meet by chance。run out最迷惑, 因为run out of很常见, 但那是「用完」, 后面接的是物不是人。遇到人+地点就是偶遇。考点: PSLE爱考run into偶遇vs run out of用完"},{"q":"She looks ___ to her older sister.","opts":["up","down","after","into"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-look up to敬佩","explain":"look up to=敬佩、仰慕(某人), 妹妹敬佩姐姐, 注意句尾已有to, 所以填up。look after最迷惑, 是「照顾」, 但look after后面不加to, 句中的to已经把答案锁定在up。考点: PSLE爱考三词phrasal verb, 看句尾的to选look up to"},{"q":"Don't give ___. Keep trying!","opts":["up","in","off","out"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-give up放弃","explain":"give up=放弃, 后一句Keep trying!(继续努力)正好和「别放弃」呼应, give up是最基础的phrasal verb。give in最迷惑, 意思是「让步/屈服」, 和give up接近, 但鼓励人坚持时英语惯用Don't give up。考点: PSLE爱考give up放弃vs give in屈服"},{"q":"He went ___ his notes before the exam.","opts":["over","on","off","up"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-go over复习","explain":"go over=温习、复查(笔记), 考试前把笔记过一遍, before the exam是信号。go on最迷惑, 是「继续/发生」, went on his notes说不通。想成: go over=revise。考点: PSLE爱考go over+notes/work表复习检查"},{"q":"We need to cut ___ on our expenses.","opts":["down","off","up","out"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-cut down减少","explain":"cut down on=减少(开支、糖分), 是三词固定搭配, on已经在句子里, 填down。cut off最迷惑, 是「切断(水电、通话)」, 不和on连用。看到on our expenses就锁定cut down on。考点: PSLE爱考cut down on+expenses/sugar表削减"},{"q":"She stood ___ for her friend when others bullied him.","opts":["up","by","in","out"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"短语动词-stand up for","explain":"stand up for=挺身维护(某人), 别人欺负朋友时她站出来保护, 句中for是信号, 填up凑成三词短语。stand by最迷惑, 也有「支持某人」的意思, 但stand by后面直接接人不再加for, 句里的for已排除它。考点: PSLE爱考stand up for维护vs stand by支持"},{"q":"The car broke ___ on the highway.","opts":["down","off","up","out"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-break down坏","explain":"break down=(车辆、机器)抛锚坏掉, 主语是car就是信号, 车在高速上坏了。break off最迷惑, 是「折断/中断关系」, 不能形容车坏。break down还能指人情绪崩溃, 都要认识。考点: PSLE爱考break down机器故障, 主语car/machine选down"},{"q":"He gets ___ well with his classmates.","opts":["along","on","up","off"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-get along相处","explain":"get along (well) with=和某人相处融洽, gets along well with his classmates是固定三件套。get on最迷惑, 英式英语get on well with意思相同, 但句子结构此处题库以along为准, 两个都记牢。考点: PSLE爱考get along with+人表相处好坏"},{"q":"I'm looking ___ to the school holidays.","opts":["forward","up","out","after"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"短语动词-look forward to","explain":"look forward to=期待、盼望, 盼着放假, 句尾to是信号, 只有forward能和look加to组成这个短语。look out最迷惑, 是「小心/当心」, 且look out不接to。注意look forward to后接名词或doing。考点: PSLE爱考look forward to+名词/V-ing表期待"},{"q":"He drives very ___.","opts":["carefully","careful","care","caring"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"副词-修饰动词","explain":"drives是动词, 修饰动词要用副词, carefully形容开车开得怎么样。careful是adjective只能修饰名词, 比如a careful driver, 不能修饰drives。考点: PSLE爱考adjective和adverb的区别, 看空格修饰的是名词还是动词"},{"q":"This is the ___ building in Singapore.","opts":["tallest","taller","tall","most tall"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"最高级-单音节","explain":"the ___ in Singapore是在全新加坡范围内比, 三者以上比较用superlative最高级tallest。most tall错, tall是短单词, 变最高级直接加est, 不用most。考点: PSLE爱考短形容词加est, 长形容词才用most"},{"q":"She sings ___ than her sister.","opts":["more beautifully","beautifuller","most beautifully","beautiful"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"比较级-多音节副词","explain":"than是比较信号词, beautifully是长副词, 比较级要用more beautifully。beautifuller是编出来的假词, 长词不能直接加er。考点: PSLE爱考than后面配comparative, 多音节词用more不加er"},{"q":"The test was ___ difficult than I expected.","opts":["more","most","much","very"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"比较级-more","explain":"看到than就要comparative, difficult是长形容词, 前面加more组成more difficult。much不行, much只能加强比较级, 说much more difficult, 单独用不构成比较级。考点: PSLE爱考than搭配more+长形容词"},{"q":"He is ___ enough to reach the top shelf.","opts":["tall","taller","tallest","the tallest"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"形容词-enough后置","explain":"enough前面用形容词原级, tall enough意思是够高。taller错, enough结构不做比较, 句子里也没有than, 不能用比较级。考点: PSLE爱考adjective+enough固定语序, 原级不升级"},{"q":"The soup is ___ hot to drink.","opts":["too","very","enough","much"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"副词-too...to","explain":"too...to是固定搭配, too hot to drink意思是烫到没法喝, 带做不到的意思。very只是很烫, 不能和后面的to drink连用, very hot to drink不成立。考点: PSLE爱考too...to结构, 看到后面有to+动词就选too"},{"q":"She speaks English ___ fluently.","opts":["quite","quiet","quieter","quietest"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"副词-quite修饰","explain":"quite是副词, 修饰fluently, quite fluently意思是说得相当流利。quiet最迷惑, 长得像但意思是安静, 是形容词, 放这里意思和词性都不对。考点: PSLE爱考quite和quiet这对双胞胎, 拼写多个e差很远"},{"q":"This is ___ most expensive gift I have received.","opts":["the","a","an","/"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"最高级-the","explain":"最高级前面必须加the, the most expensive是固定规则, 独一无二的东西只能用the。a错, most expensive是最高级不是泛指一个, a只配普通单数名词。考点: PSLE爱考superlative前面固定加the, 见most先想the"},{"q":"The ___ the weather, the happier I feel.","opts":["better","best","good","more good"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"比较级-the...the","explain":"the...the...是越...越...句型, 两边都要放comparative, good的比较级是better。more good错, good是不规则变化, 直接变better, 不能加more。考点: PSLE爱考the+比较级双联句和good-better-best不规则变化"},{"q":"He arrived ___ than expected.","opts":["earlier","early","earliest","more early"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"比较级-副词","explain":"than是比较信号词, early的比较级是earlier, y变i加er。early最迷惑, 原级不能和than搭配, 有than必须升级成比较级。考点: PSLE爱考y结尾的词变比较级, 先变i再加er"},{"q":"She enjoys ___ books in her free time.","opts":["reading","to read","read","reads"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"动名词-enjoy+ing","explain":"enjoy后面固定接gerund动名词, enjoy reading是死规矩, 表示喜欢做某事。to read错, enjoy不接to+动词, 这是必须背下来的搭配。考点: PSLE爱考enjoy/mind/finish这批只接ing的动词"},{"q":"He decided ___ abroad for his studies.","opts":["to go","going","go","gone"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"不定式-decide+to","explain":"decide后面固定接to+动词, decide to go表示决定去做。going错, decide属于只接infinitive的一批词, 不能接ing。考点: PSLE爱考decide/agree/hope/plan这批只接to do的动词"},{"q":"I look forward to ___ you soon.","opts":["seeing","see","saw","seen"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"动名词-look forward to+ing","explain":"look forward to里的to是preposition介词, 介词后面动词要变ing, 所以是seeing。see最迷惑, 很多人以为to后面接原形, 但这个to不是不定式的to。考点: PSLE爱考look forward to+ing, 是介词陷阱题的老面孔"},{"q":"She stopped ___ when the teacher came in.","opts":["talking","to talk","talk","talked"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"动名词-stop+ing停止做","explain":"stop+ing表示停止正在做的事, 老师进来她停止讲话, 用talking。to talk错, stop to talk是停下来去讲话, 意思刚好相反, 不合情境。考点: PSLE爱考stop doing和stop to do意思相反, 看情境选"},{"q":"He forgot ___ the door.","opts":["to lock","locking","lock","locked"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"不定式-forget+to忘记要做","explain":"forget+to表示忘了去做该做的事, 他忘了锁门, 门没锁上, 用to lock。locking错, forget locking是忘了自己锁过门, 门其实锁了, 意思不符。考点: PSLE爱考forget to do和forget doing, 事做没做是分水岭"},{"q":"I suggest ___ early to avoid the traffic.","opts":["leaving","to leave","leave","left"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"动名词-suggest+ing","explain":"suggest后面固定接gerund, suggest leaving表示建议早点出发。to leave错, suggest不接to+动词, 这是和decide相反的一批词, 要分开背。考点: PSLE爱考suggest/recommend+ing, 不接不定式"},{"q":"They agreed ___ us with the project.","opts":["to help","helping","help","helped"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"不定式-agree+to","explain":"agree后面固定接to+动词, agree to help表示同意帮忙。helping错, agree只接infinitive, 和enjoy那批ing动词正好是两个阵营。考点: PSLE爱考agree/decide/promise+to do固定搭配"},{"q":"She can't help ___ whenever she sees a puppy.","opts":["smiling","to smile","smile","smiled"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"动名词-can't help+ing","explain":"can't help+ing是固定搭配, 意思是忍不住做某事, 所以选smiling。to smile最迷惑, help单独用确实接to, 但can't help是整体短语, 规则完全不同。考点: PSLE爱考can't help doing=忍不住, 当整块背下来"},{"q":"Would you mind ___ the window?","opts":["opening","to open","open","opened"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"动名词-mind+ing","explain":"mind后面固定接gerund, Would you mind opening是请人帮忙的礼貌句式。to open错, mind只接ing, 不接不定式, 这是硬性搭配。考点: PSLE爱考Would you mind+ing礼貌请求句型"},{"q":"He pretended ___ asleep when his mother came.","opts":["to be","being","be","been"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"不定式-pretend+to","explain":"pretend后面固定接to+动词, pretend to be asleep表示假装睡着。being错, pretend属于只接infinitive的动词, 不能接ing。考点: PSLE爱考pretend/decide/refuse+to do这批不定式动词"}];

// 3. Cloze 单空填 (~40 道)
const CLOZE_QUESTIONS = [{"sentence":"I went ___ school yesterday.","opts":["to","at","in","on"],"ans":0,"diff":1,"explain":"go to school是固定搭配, to表示去某个地方的方向。最迷惑的是at: at school是说人在学校里, 但went是移动, 要用方向词to。考点: PSLE爱考动作动词配方向介词to"},{"sentence":"The book is ___ the table.","opts":["on","at","in","to"],"ans":0,"diff":1,"explain":"书在桌面上, 有接触面就用on。最迷惑的是in: in是在里面, 书不在桌子肚子里。记住: 表面用on, 里面用in, 点用at。考点: PSLE爱考on/in/at三兄弟的位置分工"},{"sentence":"I live ___ Singapore.","opts":["in","at","on","to"],"ans":0,"diff":1,"explain":"住在国家、城市这种大地方, 一律用in。最迷惑的是at: at只配小地点, 如at the bus stop。新加坡是国家, 必须in。考点: PSLE爱考大地方in小地点at"},{"sentence":"She is afraid ___ dogs.","opts":["of","from","to","at"],"ans":0,"diff":1,"explain":"afraid of是固定搭配, 害怕什么就of什么。最迷惑的是from: 中文说'怕狗离它远点'容易想到from, 但英语没有afraid from这个说法。考点: PSLE爱考形容词+固定介词, 背死它"},{"sentence":"Class starts ___ 8 am.","opts":["at","on","in","to"],"ans":0,"diff":1,"explain":"具体钟点用at, at 8 am就是8点整这个时间点。最迷惑的是on: on配日期和星期, 如on Monday, 不配钟点。考点: PSLE爱考时间介词at钟点on日期in月份"},{"sentence":"___ apple a day keeps the doctor away.","opts":["An","A","The","One"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"冠词","explain":"apple开头是元音音a的发音, 冠词要用An。最迷惑的是A: 拼写没错但发音接不上, a apple读起来卡壳。看发音不看字母。考点: PSLE爱考元音开头用an"},{"sentence":"She is ___ honest girl.","opts":["an","a","the","one"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"冠词","explain":"honest的h不发音, 开口就是元音o的音, 所以用an。最迷惑的是a: 看到h是辅音字母就选a, 中招了, 要听发音不看拼写。考点: PSLE爱考哑音h单词honest/hour配an"},{"sentence":"I had ___ cup of tea.","opts":["a","an","the","some"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"冠词","explain":"cup是辅音开头, 一杯茶就是a cup of tea, 固定说法。最迷惑的是some: some tea可以, 但前面有cup这个量词, 单数量词前用a。考点: PSLE爱考a+量词+of+不可数名词"},{"sentence":"He plays ___ piano well.","opts":["the","a","an","/"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"冠词","explain":"弹奏乐器前必须加the, play the piano是铁规。最迷惑的是a: 弹的是钢琴这类乐器不是随便一台, 乐器名前定死用the。对比play football不加冠词。考点: PSLE爱考乐器加the运动不加"},{"sentence":"My dad goes to work ___ MRT.","opts":["by","on","in","with"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"介词","explain":"by+交通工具表示乘坐方式, by MRT/by bus/by car都是这样。最迷惑的是on: on the MRT可以说, 但那要加the; 光秃秃的MRT前只能用by。考点: PSLE爱考by+交通工具不加冠词"},{"sentence":"She arrived ___ Singapore last week.","opts":["in","at","on","to"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"explain":"arrive in配大地方, 新加坡是国家所以arrive in Singapore。最迷惑的是at: arrive at配小地点如at the airport。另外arrive绝不配to。考点: PSLE爱考arrive in大地方at小地点"},{"sentence":"I am interested ___ science.","opts":["in","at","on","about"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"explain":"interested in是固定搭配, 对什么感兴趣就in什么。最迷惑的是about: 中文'关于科学很感兴趣'会误选about, 英语只认in。考点: PSLE爱考interested in, 每年都出"},{"sentence":"Don't laugh ___ him!","opts":["at","to","of","with"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"explain":"laugh at somebody是嘲笑某人, 固定词组。最迷惑的是with: laugh with him是跟他一起笑, 意思完全反了, 这里是别嘲笑他。考点: PSLE爱考laugh at表嘲笑"},{"sentence":"We will meet ___ Monday.","opts":["on","at","in","from"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"explain":"星期几前面用on, on Monday雷打不动。最迷惑的是at: at配钟点如at 8 am, 不配星期。口诀: at点on天in月。考点: PSLE爱考星期前用on"},{"sentence":"She is married ___ a doctor.","opts":["to","with","of","at"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"explain":"married to是固定搭配, 嫁给/娶了谁都用to。最迷惑的是with: 中文'和医生结婚'直译就选with, 这是经典中式英语陷阱, 英语只说married to。考点: PSLE爱考married to不用with"},{"sentence":"I came ___ this old photo in the attic.","opts":["across","at","on","through"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"come across是偶然发现、无意中碰到, 正好配旧照片这个情景。最迷惑的是through: come through是熬过去、挺过来, 跟发现照片无关。考点: PSLE爱考phrasal verb, come across=偶遇"},{"sentence":"Please look ___ the children while I go out.","opts":["after","at","for","into"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"look after是照顾, 我出门你照看孩子, 意思吻合。最迷惑的是for: look for是寻找, 孩子没丢不用找。look at是看一眼, 也不对。考点: PSLE爱考look家族词组, after照顾for寻找into调查"},{"sentence":"The fire broke ___ at midnight.","opts":["out","in","off","down"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"break out专指火灾、战争、疾病突然爆发, 半夜起火就是broke out。最迷惑的是down: break down是机器坏掉或人崩溃, 火不会break down。考点: PSLE爱考break out=灾祸爆发"},{"sentence":"He gave ___ smoking last year.","opts":["up","off","in","out"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"give up是戒掉、放弃, 戒烟就是give up smoking。最迷惑的是in: give in是让步投降, 对烟让步反而是继续抽, 意思拧了。考点: PSLE爱考give up+动名词表戒除"},{"sentence":"They put ___ the meeting to next week.","opts":["off","in","out","down"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"phrasal","explain":"put off是推迟, 会议挪到下周正是推迟。最迷惑的是out: put out是扑灭火, 会议不能扑灭。put down是放下或写下, 也不搭。考点: PSLE爱考put off=postpone推迟"},{"sentence":"Despite ___ tired, he kept working.","opts":["being","to be","was","being a"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"explain":"Despite是介词, 后面只能接名词或动名词, 所以用being。最迷惑的是to be: 介词后不能接to do不定式, 这是硬规矩。was更不行, 介词后没动词原形句。考点: PSLE爱考despite+V-ing结构"},{"sentence":"The students were dismissed ___ the principal's announcement.","opts":["upon","at","on","in"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"explain":"upon在这里表示'一…就…', 广播一响学生就放学了, dismissed upon是正式用法。最迷惑的是at: at the announcement语法看似通, 但表达'随即发生'必须用upon。考点: PSLE爱考upon+名词表一经…立刻"},{"sentence":"She was so engrossed ___ the book.","opts":["in","at","with","on"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"explain":"engrossed in是固定搭配, 全神贯注沉浸在书里。最迷惑的是with: 中文'被书迷住'像被动会想选with, 但engrossed只配in, 跟absorbed in同款。考点: PSLE爱考engrossed/absorbed in表入迷"},{"sentence":"I prefer reading ___ watching TV.","opts":["to","than","rather","more"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"explain":"prefer A to B是固定句型, 更喜欢A胜过B, 这里to不是不定式是介词。最迷惑的是than: 看到比较就想用than, 但prefer不配than, 只配to。考点: PSLE爱考prefer...to...不用than"},{"sentence":"He had no choice ___ to apologize.","opts":["but","than","rather","then"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"explain":"have no choice but to do是固定句型, 别无选择只好道歉。最迷惑的是than: 长得像比较句就选than, 但这个词组里定死用but, but后接to do。考点: PSLE爱考no choice but to do"},{"sentence":"After working tirelessly for ten hours under the scorching sun, the construction workers were ___ exhausted.","opts":["utterly","quite","rather","barely"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"context-vocab","explain":"utterly意思是「彻底地」, 烈日下干了十小时, 累到极点, 用utterly exhausted最贴切, 这是固定强化搭配。barely最迷惑, 它是「几乎不」, 意思正好反了, 干十小时怎么会几乎不累。考点: PSLE爱考程度副词与形容词的强弱搭配, 看语境定强度。"},{"sentence":"Although the storm warning was issued early, many residents ___ to evacuate, hoping the typhoon would change course.","opts":["refused","accepted","hurried","agreed"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"context-vocab","explain":"refused「拒绝」才通: 后半句说居民盼台风改道, 说明他们不肯撤离。although提示前后转折, 警报早发但没人走。agreed最迷惑, 同意撤离的话就跟「盼台风转向」矛盾了。考点: PSLE爱考although转折逻辑, 空格要和后半句心态一致。"},{"sentence":"The teacher reminded the class that ___ a complete sentence requires both a subject and a verb.","opts":["constructing","construct","to constructs","constructed"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"context-grammar","explain":"that从句里空格是主语, 动词当主语要用gerund(动名词), 所以constructing对, 「造一个完整句子需要主谓」。construct最迷惑, 原形动词不能直接当主语, 后面已有requires这个真动词。考点: PSLE爱考动名词作主语, 一句只能有一个主要动词。"},{"sentence":"By the time the firefighters arrived, the entire building ___ to the ground.","opts":["burned","was burning","had burned","has burned"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"context-grammar-pluperfect","explain":"By the time是past perfect信号词: 消防员到之前, 楼已经烧光, 更早发生的动作用had burned。was burning最迷惑, 进行时表示「正在烧」, 但句意是烧完塌了(to the ground), 动作已结束。考点: PSLE爱考by the time + 过去时, 主句配had + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"Despite ___ the fastest runner in the school, Ahmad lost the race because he tripped over a stone.","opts":["being","been","to be","is"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"context-grammar-despite","explain":"Despite是preposition, 后面只能接noun或gerund, 所以用being。been最迷惑, 它是过去分词, 前面必须有have/has/had才成立, 不能单独跟在despite后。考点: PSLE爱考despite/in spite of + V-ing, although才接完整句子。"},{"sentence":"The librarian, ___ patience with the noisy children was wearing thin, finally asked them to leave.","opts":["who","whom","whose","which"],"ans":2,"diff":5,"tag":"context-grammar-whose","explain":"空格后的patience是名词, 表示「图书管理员的耐心」, 名词前表所属要用whose。who最迷惑, 它做从句主语, 但这里主语是patience, 不缺主语, 缺的是「谁的」。考点: PSLE爱考关系代词, 空格后紧跟名词就选whose。"},{"sentence":"If I ___ harder for the test, I would not have failed it.","opts":["studied","had studied","have studied","study"],"ans":1,"diff":5,"tag":"context-grammar-conditional3","explain":"主句是would not have failed, 这是third conditional(对过去的假设), if从句必须配had studied, 「当初要是多用功就不会挂」。studied最迷惑, 它是second conditional的搭配, 假设现在而不是过去。考点: PSLE爱考would have + p.p.反推if从句用had + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"The detective examined the crime scene ___, looking for any clue that might have been overlooked.","opts":["meticulously","barely","randomly","quickly"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"context-vocab-adv","explain":"meticulously「一丝不苟地」和后半句「找任何可能被漏掉的线索」完美呼应, 侦探查案就该细致。quickly最迷惑, 查得快不等于查得细, 和「不放过线索」的语境对不上。考点: PSLE爱考副词与语境呼应, 先读完整句再选。"},{"sentence":"The phenomenon, ___ scientists had long theorized about, was finally observed in the laboratory.","opts":["which","that","what","whom"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"context-relative-clause","explain":"从句被两个逗号夹住, 是non-defining relative clause, 只能用which, 补充说明phenomenon。that最迷惑, 平时它能代物, 但有逗号的非限定从句里that被禁用, 这是铁规。考点: PSLE爱考逗号+关系代词, 见逗号排除that。"},{"sentence":"Had the government ___ stricter measures earlier, the outbreak could have been contained.","opts":["implemented","implementing","implement","to implement"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"context-subjunctive-inversion","explain":"Had the government...是倒装的third conditional, 等于If the government had implemented, had后面接过去分词implemented。implement最迷惑, 看到had像该接原形, 但这个had是助动词, 必须配p.p.。考点: PSLE爱考Had + 主语 + p.p.的省略if倒装句。"},{"sentence":"The CEO was ___ criticized for her decision that she eventually resigned from her position.","opts":["so severely","such severely","very severely","too severely"],"ans":0,"diff":6,"tag":"context-so...that","explain":"后面有that she resigned, 是so...that句型「批评得如此严厉以至于辞职」, 修饰副词severely用so。such severely最迷惑, such只能配名词(such a harsh critic), 不能直接接副词。考点: PSLE爱考so+adj/adv+that与such+名词+that的区分。"},{"sentence":"The teacher asked us to pay ___ to her explanation.","opts":["attention","focus","notice","mind"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-pay attention","explain":"pay attention to是固定搭配「注意听」, pay只能配attention, 这是collocation死规矩。notice最迷惑, take notice of也表注意, 但动词是take不是pay, 混搭就错。考点: PSLE爱考动词+名词固定搭配, 记词组要连动词一起背。"},{"sentence":"He always takes ___ in his work.","opts":["pride","proud","proudly","priding"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-take pride","explain":"take pride in是固定搭配「以...为荣」, take后面要接noun, pride是名词形式。proud最迷惑, 它是adjective, 该用在be proud of里, 跟take不搭。考点: PSLE爱考同根词选词性, 看前面动词定名词还是形容词。"},{"sentence":"She made a good ___ on her new teacher.","opts":["impression","expression","idea","opinion"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-make impression","explain":"make an impression on是固定搭配「给...留下印象」, 对新老师留下好印象用impression。expression最迷惑, 长得像但意思是「表情/表达」, make a good expression不成立。考点: PSLE爱考形近词impression/expression, 靠搭配make...on辨认。"},{"sentence":"We need to make a ___ about where to eat.","opts":["decision","decide","decisive","deciding"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-make decision","explain":"make a decision是固定搭配「做决定」, 冠词a后面必须接noun, decision是名词。decide最迷惑, 意思对但它是verb, a后面不能放动词原形。考点: PSLE爱考make/take + 名词搭配, 见冠词就选名词形式。"},{"sentence":"He took ___ of the opportunity to travel.","opts":["advantage","benefit","profit","use"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-take advantage","explain":"take advantage of是固定词组「利用(机会)」, 三个词绑死不能换。benefit最迷惑, 意思也和好处相关, 但搭配是benefit from, 不跟take...of连用。考点: PSLE爱考三件套短语take advantage of, 整组背不拆开。"},{"sentence":"The news came as a great ___ to everyone.","opts":["shock","shocking","shocked","shocks"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-come as shock","explain":"come as a shock是固定表达「令人震惊」, a后面接noun, shock作名词。shocking最迷惑, 它是adjective, a shocking后面还得再加名词才完整, 单放句尾就错。考点: PSLE爱考a/an后接名词, 同根词看词性下手。"},{"sentence":"She bears a strong ___ to her mother.","opts":["resemblance","similar","likeness","looking"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"collocation-bear resemblance","explain":"bear a resemblance to是固定搭配「长得像」, resemblance是名词配bear。likeness最迷惑, 意思几乎一样, 但PSLE考的是bear a strong resemblance这套原装搭配, likeness不与bear强搭。考点: PSLE爱考collocation原装组合, 意思对不等于搭配对。"},{"sentence":"He made an ___ to help the old woman.","opts":["effort","effect","affect","afford"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-make effort","explain":"make an effort是固定搭配「努力」, an提示元音开头名词, effort正好。effect最迷惑, 拼写像但意思是「效果」, make an effect to help不通。考点: PSLE爱考形近词effort/effect/affect, 用搭配make an effort to锁答案。"},{"sentence":"The company suffered heavy ___ last year.","opts":["losses","lose","lost","losing"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-suffer losses","explain":"suffer losses是固定搭配「蒙受损失」, heavy后面要接noun, 商业亏损常用复数losses。lost最迷惑, 它是动词过去式或形容词, 不能当heavy修饰的名词。考点: PSLE爱考lose/loss/lost三兄弟, 形容词后面选名词loss(es)。"},{"sentence":"Please do me a ___ and close the window.","opts":["favour","help","good","kind"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-do favour","explain":"do someone a favour是固定搭配「帮个忙」, favour是名词配do。help最迷惑, 意思全对, 但英语只说do me a favour或give me some help, do me a help不存在。考点: PSLE爱考favour/help的动词搭配差异, 按词组整套记。"},{"sentence":"The students were told to keep ___ during the test.","opts":["quiet","quietly","silence","silently"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-keep quiet","explain":"keep quiet是固定搭配「保持安静」, keep后接adjective作补语, quiet是形容词。quietly最迷惑, 副词修饰动作, 但keep在这里是linking verb, 要接形容词描述状态。考点: PSLE爱考linking verb(keep/stay/remain)后用形容词不用副词。"},{"sentence":"She takes after her father in many ___.","opts":["ways","things","parts","sides"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-in many ways","explain":"in many ways是固定表达「在许多方面」, 说她像爸爸的地方很多。things最迷惑, 中文直译「很多事情」好像通, 但英语谈相似点只用ways, in many things不地道。考点: PSLE爱考固定短语in many ways, 别用中文直译选词。"},{"sentence":"I have no ___ but to agree with him.","opts":["choice","choose","chose","chosen"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-have no choice","explain":"have no choice but to是固定句型「别无选择只能」, no后面接noun, choice是名词。choose最迷惑, 它是verb, no后面不能直接放动词原形。考点: PSLE爱考choice/choose词性区分, no/the/a后面一律选名词。"},{"sentence":"He lost his ___ and shouted at the waiter.","opts":["temper","anger","mood","feeling"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-lose temper","explain":"lose one's temper是固定搭配「发脾气」, 后面冲服务员大吼正是发火。anger最迷惑, 意思也是怒气, 但lose his anger反而像「消气」, 搭配错意思也反。考点: PSLE爱考idiom原装搭配lose one's temper, 换近义词就丢分。"},{"sentence":"We caught a ___ of the famous actor at the airport.","opts":["glimpse","glance","look","sight"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"collocation-catch glimpse","explain":"catch a glimpse是固定搭配, 意思是「瞥见一眼」, 匆匆看到名人一眼。最迷惑的是glance: glance是你主动扫一眼(take a glance), 而glimpse是碰巧看见, 和catch搭配的只有glimpse。考点: PSLE爱考glimpse和glance这对形近词的搭配区别"},{"sentence":"The heavy rain ___ havoc on the crops.","opts":["wreaked","made","did","caused"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"collocation-wreak havoc","explain":"wreak havoc是固定搭配, 专门表示「造成严重破坏」, havoc只认wreak这个动词。最迷惑的是caused: cause damage可以, 但havoc的地道搭配是wreak, 考的就是这个词组原形。考点: PSLE爱考collocation固定动词名词搭配, 背词组要整个背"},{"sentence":"She broke the ___ by telling a joke.","opts":["ice","silence","quiet","cold"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-break the ice","explain":"break the ice是习语, 意思是「打破尴尬气氛」, 讲笑话正是为了让大家放松。最迷惑的是silence: break the silence只是字面上打破安静, 但这里讲笑话是social场合暖场, 习语break the ice才贴切。考点: PSLE爱考idiom习语的整体意思, 不能逐字直译"},{"sentence":"He has a good ___ of humour.","opts":["sense","feeling","taste","meaning"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-sense of humour","explain":"a sense of humour是固定搭配「幽默感」, sense表示对某种东西的感知力。最迷惑的是feeling: feeling是情绪感受, 不和of humour搭配, 英语里只说sense of humour。考点: PSLE爱考sense of搭配(sense of humour/direction/responsibility)"},{"sentence":"The students must hand ___ their essays by Friday.","opts":["in","out","up","off"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"collocation-hand in提交","explain":"hand in是phrasal verb「上交」, 交作业给老师就用hand in。最迷惑的是hand up: 举手是put up your hand, hand up不是交东西的意思, 别被「向上交」的中文思维骗了。考点: PSLE爱考phrasal verb, hand in交/hand out发/hand over移交要分清"},{"sentence":"She kept an ___ on the children while they played.","opts":["eye","look","watch","attention"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"collocation-keep eye on","explain":"keep an eye on是习语「照看、留意」, 妈妈看着玩耍的孩子就是这个词组。最迷惑的是watch: keep watch要说keep watch on(不加an), 空格前有an, 只能填eye。考点: PSLE爱考idiom里的冠词细节, an后面跟的词是关键线索"},{"sentence":"The weather was cold. ___, we decided to go hiking.","opts":["Nevertheless","Because","Since","Unless"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-nevertheless","explain":"前句天冷, 后句照样去远足, 意思相反转折, Nevertheless「尽管如此」正合适。最迷惑的是Because: 天冷不是去远足的原因, 逻辑反了; 而且Because不能单独放句首带逗号这样用。考点: PSLE爱考connector逻辑方向, 先判断两句是顺着说还是对着说"},{"sentence":"He studied hard. ___, he failed the exam.","opts":["However","Therefore","Moreover","Furthermore"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-however","explain":"努力学习却考砸, 前后结果出乎意料, However表转折最对。最迷惑的是Therefore: 它表因果「所以」, 用了就变成努力所以不及格, 逻辑完全反了。考点: PSLE爱考However和Therefore对换设陷阱, 抓句意方向再选"},{"sentence":"She was tired. ___, she continued working.","opts":["Nonetheless","Therefore","Hence","Thus"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"connector-nonetheless","explain":"很累却继续工作, 转折关系, Nonetheless=nevertheless「尽管如此」。最迷惑的是Therefore: 累了「所以」继续工作说不通, 因果词放转折句就是错。考点: PSLE爱考Nonetheless这类高级转折词, 记住它和However是一家"},{"sentence":"The road was flooded. ___, we took a detour.","opts":["Therefore","However","Moreover","Nevertheless"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-therefore","explain":"路淹了「所以」绕道走, 前因后果, Therefore正确。最迷惑的是Nevertheless: 它表转折, 用了就成「路淹了但我们还是绕道」, 绕道明明是被逼的结果不是对着干。考点: PSLE爱考因果connector, 问自己后句是不是前句导致的"},{"sentence":"He is smart. ___, he is also hardworking.","opts":["Moreover","However","Nevertheless","Therefore"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-moreover","explain":"聪明「而且」还勤奋, 两个优点往上叠加, Moreover表递进。最迷惑的是However: also已经提示是补充不是转折, 两句都是夸人, 方向一致不能用转折词。考点: PSLE爱考递进词Moreover/Furthermore, 看到also就找加法词"},{"sentence":"The food was delicious. ___, the service was excellent.","opts":["Furthermore","However","Nevertheless","Instead"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-furthermore","explain":"菜好吃「而且」服务也棒, 两句都在夸, Furthermore表递进补充。最迷惑的是However: 好吃和服务好不矛盾, 没有转折; Instead更错, 没有替代关系。考点: PSLE爱考connector, 先判断两句是同方向(加法)还是反方向(转折)"},{"sentence":"She did not study. ___, she did not pass.","opts":["Consequently","However","Nevertheless","Moreover"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-consequently","explain":"没学习「结果」没及格, 标准因果, Consequently=as a result。最迷惑的是However: 不学习和不及格顺理成章, 一点不意外, 转折词放这就是逻辑错误。考点: PSLE爱考Consequently这类结果词, 和Therefore/Hence是一家"},{"sentence":"He was not invited. ___, he went to the party.","opts":["Nevertheless","Therefore","Furthermore","Moreover"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-nevertheless","explain":"没被邀请「却还是」去了派对, 出乎意料的转折, Nevertheless正确。最迷惑的是Therefore: 没被邀请「所以」去派对完全讲不通, 因果方向反了。考点: PSLE爱考转折connector, 后句和前句唱反调就选Nevertheless家族"},{"sentence":"The show was cancelled ___ the heavy rain.","opts":["due to","however","although","despite of"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-due to","explain":"due to+名词表原因「由于大雨」, 空格后是名词短语the heavy rain, 语法意思都对。最迷惑的是despite of: 这是经典陷阱, despite后面直接加名词, 根本没有despite of这个说法, 而且转折意思也不对。考点: PSLE爱考due to/because of接名词, despite of是永远的错误选项"},{"sentence":"___ his wealth, he lives a simple life.","opts":["Despite","Although","Because","Since"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-despite+名词","explain":"Despite+名词「尽管有钱却过得简朴」, 空格后his wealth是名词短语, 只有Despite能直接带名词。最迷惑的是Although: 意思也是转折, 但Although后面必须接完整句子(主语+动词), 不能接名词短语。考点: PSLE爱考Despite+名词 vs Although+句子的结构区别"},{"sentence":"He was ill. ___, he stayed home.","opts":["Hence","However","Moreover","Nevertheless"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-hence","explain":"生病「因此」待在家, 因果关系, Hence=therefore「所以」。最迷惑的是However: 生病待在家理所当然, 没有意外转折, 用However逻辑就断了。考点: PSLE爱考Hence/Thus/Therefore三胞胎, 都是因果词可互换"},{"sentence":"The project was difficult. ___, we managed to finish it.","opts":["Nonetheless","Therefore","Hence","Consequently"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"connector-nonetheless","explain":"项目很难「但我们还是」完成了, managed暗示克服困难, Nonetheless表转折。最迷惑的是Therefore: 难「所以」完成说不通, 另外三个全是因果词, 只有Nonetheless是转折。考点: PSLE爱考排除法, 三个选项同类时答案往往是落单的那个"},{"sentence":"She enjoys reading. ___, she loves writing stories.","opts":["In addition","However","Therefore","Nevertheless"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-in addition","explain":"爱读书「另外」也爱写故事, 两个爱好叠加, In addition表递进。最迷惑的是However: 读和写是好朋友不是对头, 没有转折; 看到后句和前句同方向就用加法词。考点: PSLE爱考In addition/Moreover/Furthermore递进三件套"},{"sentence":"He is not only smart ___ also kind.","opts":["but","and","or","yet"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"connector-not only but also","explain":"not only...but also是固定关联词组「不但…而且」, 中间只能填but。最迷惑的是and: 单独看smart and kind没错, 但前面出现了not only, 就必须配套用but also, 拆散词组就丢分。考点: PSLE爱考not only...but also配对连词, 见到前半必接后半"},{"sentence":"I want to go; ___, I have no time.","opts":["however","therefore","moreover","furthermore"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-semicolon however","explain":"想去「但是」没时间, 分号加逗号中间放转折副词however, 意思结构都对。最迷惑的是therefore: 想去「所以」没时间讲不通, 前后是愿望和现实的冲突, 必须转折。考点: PSLE爱考分号+connector+逗号的标点结构, however最常驻"},{"sentence":"___ the fact that he was sick, he came to school.","opts":["Despite","Because","Since","Due to"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"connector-despite the fact","explain":"Despite the fact that+句子「尽管他病了」, 这是despite带从句的唯一方式。最迷惑的是Due to: 后面接the fact that语法也通, 但「因为生病所以来上学」逻辑不通, 带病上学是转折。考点: PSLE爱考Despite the fact that整串结构, 先过语法再过逻辑"},{"sentence":"She arrived late ___ of the traffic jam.","opts":["because","in spite","despite","although"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"connector-because of","explain":"because of+名词「因为塞车」, 空格后有of, 只有because能和of组队表原因。最迷惑的是in spite: in spite of语法上也成立, 但意思变成「尽管塞车她还是迟到了」, 塞车明明是迟到的原因不是被克服的困难。考点: PSLE爱考because of vs in spite of, 语法都对时拼逻辑"},{"sentence":"He worked hard ___ that he could earn more money.","opts":["so","because","although","despite"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-so that","explain":"so that表目的「为了能多赚钱」而拼命工作, so...that前有could更是目的从句标志。最迷惑的是because: 空格后已有that, because that不是英语说法; 而且赚钱是目的不是原因。考点: PSLE爱考so that目的从句, 空格后的that是解题钥匙"},{"sentence":"We waited for an hour. ___, the bus did not come.","opts":["Still","Therefore","Moreover","Furthermore"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"connector-still","explain":"等了一小时「可是」车还是没来, Still放句首表「尽管如此、还是」, 是转折。最迷惑的是Therefore: 等了一小时「所以」车不来? 车来不来不由你等多久决定, 因果不成立, 只能转折。考点: PSLE爱考Still当转折connector用, 别只记它「仍然」的副词义"},{"sentence":"___ to popular belief, bats are not blind.","opts":["Contrary","Despite","Although","However"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"connector-contrary to","explain":"Contrary to popular belief 是固定搭配, 意思是「和大家想的相反」, 只有 Contrary 能配 to。最迷惑的 Despite 后面直接接名词, 不带 to, 而且意思是「尽管」不是「相反」。考点: PSLE爱考固定搭配介词, contrary to 要整块背下来。"},{"sentence":"By the time she ___ home, her parents had already gone to bed.","opts":["reached","reaches","has reached","reaching"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-past perfect","explain":"By the time 后面用 simple past (reached), 主句用 past perfect (had gone), 表示她到家前父母已睡了。最迷惑的 reaches 是现在式, 和后半句 had already gone 的过去时间对不上。考点: PSLE爱考 by the time + past 搭配 had done 的时态组合。"},{"sentence":"Every morning, he ___ up at 6 am and goes for a run.","opts":["wakes","woke","has woken","is waking"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"tense-context-present habit","explain":"Every morning 表示天天重复的习惯, 用 simple present, 而且 he 是第三人称单数, 动词加s = wakes。最迷惑的 is waking 是现在进行式, 只讲此刻正在做, 不能表示每天的习惯。考点: PSLE爱考 every day/morning 这类频率词定 simple present。"},{"sentence":"She ___ in this school since 2020.","opts":["has taught","taught","teaches","is teaching"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-present perfect since","explain":"since 2020 表示从2020年一直教到现在, 动作延续到今天, 要用 present perfect: has taught。最迷惑的 taught 是 simple past, 意思是过去教过、现在不教了, 和 since 矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考 since/for + 时间段 定 present perfect。"},{"sentence":"The children ___ when the teacher walked in.","opts":["were talking","talked","have talked","talk"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-past continuous","explain":"老师走进来那一刻, 孩子们「正在」讲话, 长动作被短动作打断, 用 past continuous: were talking。最迷惑的 talked 只说他们讲过话, 表达不出「当时正在进行、被撞见」的画面。考点: PSLE爱考 when + walked in 打断进行中动作, 选 was/were doing。"},{"sentence":"If it ___ tomorrow, we will cancel the picnic.","opts":["rains","rained","will rain","raining"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-conditional 1","explain":"这是 first conditional: if 从句用 simple present (rains), 主句才用 will。虽然说的是明天, if 后面也不能加 will。最迷惑的 will rain 就是掉进这个坑, if 从句禁用 will。考点: PSLE爱考条件句 If + present, main clause + will 的公式。"},{"sentence":"After he ___ his homework, he watched television.","opts":["had finished","finished","has finished","finishes"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-past perfect after","explain":"两件过去的事, 先做完作业(更早)用 past perfect: had finished, 后看电视用 simple past。After 明确点出先后。最迷惑的 finished 语法上勉强通, 但题目考的是 after + had done 强调「先完成」, 按标准答案选 A。考点: PSLE爱考 after/before 连接两个过去动作, 先发生的用 had + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"The train ___ at 9 am every day.","opts":["departs","departed","has departed","is departing"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"tense-context-timetable present","explain":"every day 加火车时刻表, 都是固定规律的事, 用 simple present: departs。最迷惑的 is departing 是进行式, 只能说此刻正在开出, 不能表示天天9点的时刻表安排。考点: PSLE爱考时刻表/习惯性动作用 simple present, 认准 every day 信号词。"},{"sentence":"She ___ her keys and could not enter the house.","opts":["had lost","lost","has lost","loses"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-past perfect result","explain":"先弄丢钥匙, 后进不了门, 丢是更早的过去, 用 past perfect: had lost。最迷惑的 has lost 是 present perfect, 强调影响到「现在」, 但这句全是过去的事(could not), 时间对不上。考点: PSLE爱考过去两动作分先后, 更早的那个用 had + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"Look! The bird ___ towards us.","opts":["is flying","flies","flew","has flown"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"tense-context-present continuous look","explain":"Look! 是现场喊你看, 鸟这一刻正飞过来, 用 present continuous: is flying。最迷惑的 flies 是 simple present, 表示鸟平时会飞的习惯, 表达不了眼前正在发生的动作。考点: PSLE爱考 Look!/Listen! 这类信号词定 present continuous。"},{"sentence":"I ___ this book yet. Can I keep it longer?","opts":["have not finished","did not finish","do not finish","am not finishing"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-present perfect yet","explain":"yet 配否定句, 表示到现在还没读完, 而且还想继续借, 影响延续到当下, 用 present perfect: have not finished。最迷惑的 did not finish 是过去式, 说的是过去某次没读完, 和 yet 不搭。考点: PSLE爱考 yet/already/just 信号词定 present perfect。"},{"sentence":"While she ___ the dishes, she heard a loud crash.","opts":["was washing","washed","has washed","is washing"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-while past cont","explain":"While 引导正在进行的长动作(洗碗), 中途被巨响打断, 用 past continuous: was washing。最迷惑的 is washing 时态是现在, 但 heard 已锁定整句在过去, 前后要一致。考点: PSLE爱考 while + was/were doing 搭配 simple past 的打断句型。"},{"sentence":"He promised that he ___ help us move house.","opts":["would","will","can","shall"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-reported future","explain":"主句 promised 是过去式, 宾语从句要跟着退一步, will 变 would, 这叫 reported speech 时态后移。最迷惑的 will 就是没退时态, 主句过去从句不能停在将来式。考点: PSLE爱考 said/promised/told 后从句 will→would 的时态一致。"},{"sentence":"By next year, they ___ married for 25 years.","opts":["will have been","are","were","have been"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"tense-context-future perfect","explain":"By next year 表示「到明年为止」将满25年, 用 future perfect: will have been。最迷惑的 have been 只说到「现在」为止, 缺了 will, 够不到明年那个时间点。考点: PSLE爱考 by + 将来时间 定 will have + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"She ___ to the gym three times a week.","opts":["goes","went","has gone","is going"],"ans":0,"diff":2,"tag":"tense-context-habit present","explain":"three times a week 是频率词, 讲每周固定的习惯, 用 simple present, 第三人称加s = goes。最迷惑的 is going 是进行式, 不能表达每周三次的规律, 只能说此刻正去。考点: PSLE爱考 once/twice/three times a week 频率词定 simple present。"},{"sentence":"Before I ___ you, I had never eaten durian.","opts":["met","meet","have met","had met"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-before past","explain":"Before I met you: 从句用 simple past, 主句「从没吃过榴莲」是更早的经历, 已用了 had never eaten。最迷惑的 had met 把 past perfect 放错位置, 一句里更早的动作才用 had, 从句这边只需 met。考点: PSLE爱考 before/after 句中 had + p.p. 该放哪半句。"},{"sentence":"The concert ___ already ___ by the time we arrived.","opts":["had/started","has/started","was/starting","is/starting"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-past perfect already","explain":"我们到场之前音乐会已开始, 更早的动作用 past perfect: had already started, already 插在 had 和 started 中间。最迷惑的 has/started 是 present perfect, 但 by the time we arrived 锁定全句在过去, has 不能用。考点: PSLE爱考 by the time + arrived 搭配 had + p.p.。"},{"sentence":"Don't call me at 8 pm. I ___ dinner then.","opts":["will be having","have","had","am having"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-future continuous","explain":"晚上8点这个将来的时间点, 我会「正在」吃饭, 用 future continuous: will be having。最迷惑的 am having 可表安排好的将来, 但表达不出「8点那一刻正吃到一半」的进行画面, then 指向将来某刻。考点: PSLE爱考将来某时刻正在做的事, 选 will be + doing。"},{"sentence":"She ___ English since she was five years old.","opts":["has been learning","learned","learns","is learning"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"tense-context-present perfect continuous","explain":"since she was five 表示从五岁一直学到现在还在学, 用 present perfect continuous: has been learning。最迷惑的 learned 是过去式, 意思是学过但停了, 和 since 的「延续到现在」冲突。考点: PSLE爱考 since + 过去时间点 定 has been doing/has done。"},{"sentence":"The letter ___ yesterday but I haven't read it yet.","opts":["arrived","arrives","has arrived","had arrived"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-simple past yesterday","explain":"yesterday 是明确的过去时间, 信到达用 simple past: arrived。最迷惑的 has arrived 是 present perfect, 它不能和 yesterday 这种具体过去时间连用, 这是铁规则。考点: PSLE爱考 yesterday/last week 与 present perfect 不能同框。"},{"sentence":"I ___ to Paris before, so I know the way around.","opts":["have been","went","go","had been"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"tense-context-present perfect experience","explain":"before 在这里指「以前去过」, 是到现在为止的人生经历, 用 present perfect: have been, 所以现在才认路。最迷惑的 went 是过去式, 需要具体过去时间配合, 而且接不上后半句「现在认路」的效果。考点: PSLE爱考 have been to 表经历, before/ever 是信号词。"},{"sentence":"The ___ student was praised by the principal for his excellent results.","opts":["diligent","lazy","naughty","careless"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-diligent","explain":"被校长表扬、成绩优秀, 只有 diligent(勤奋的)是正面词, 和句意匹配。最迷惑的 careless(粗心的)是负面词, 粗心的学生不会考出 excellent results, 逻辑不通。考点: PSLE爱考形容词褒贬要和句子结果一致, 先判断句子是夸还是批。"},{"sentence":"Despite the ___ weather, the hikers pressed on.","opts":["harsh","pleasant","mild","warm"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-harsh","explain":"Despite 表示「尽管」, 后面的天气必须是坏的, 徒步者才需要「咬牙前进」(pressed on), 所以选 harsh(恶劣的)。最迷惑的 pleasant 是好天气, 好天气不需要 despite 来转折。考点: PSLE爱考 despite/although 转折词决定空格选反方向的词。"},{"sentence":"The old man walked with a ___ pace due to his injured leg.","opts":["sluggish","brisk","rapid","swift"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-sluggish","explain":"腿受伤了, 走路自然慢, sluggish 意思是缓慢无力的, 和 injured leg 因果吻合。最迷惑的 brisk 是轻快的, 恰恰相反, 伤腿的人快不起来。考点: PSLE爱考 due to 因果线索, 空格要和原因逻辑一致, brisk/swift/rapid 全是快, 排除。"},{"sentence":"She spoke in a ___ voice so as not to wake the baby.","opts":["hushed","loud","shrill","harsh"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-hushed","explain":"为了不吵醒宝宝, 说话要压低声音, hushed 意思是轻声的, 正好呼应 so as not to wake。最迷惑的 shrill 是尖锐刺耳的, 一喊宝宝立刻醒, 和目的完全相反。考点: PSLE爱考 so as to/in order to 目的句, 空格必须服务这个目的。"},{"sentence":"The ___ sunset painted the sky in shades of orange and pink.","opts":["magnificent","dull","ordinary","plain"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-magnificent","explain":"magnificent对: 橙粉相间的晚霞是壮丽美景, 要选褒义形容词「壮丽的」。最迷惑的dull错: dull是「暗淡无趣」, 和后面painted the sky in shades of orange and pink的绚烂画面矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考形容词感情色彩要和句子画面一致, 先看后半句描写再选词。"},{"sentence":"He gave a ___ sigh of relief when the results were announced.","opts":["audible","quiet","silent","muted"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-audible","explain":"audible对: 听得见的sigh of relief才叫「gave a sigh」, audible=能听到的, 说明他松了一大口气。最迷惑的silent错: silent是无声的, 无声的叹气别人察觉不到, 和gave(发出)矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考形容词与动词搭配的逻辑, 发出来的声音必须listen得到。"},{"sentence":"The crowd erupted in ___ applause after the performance.","opts":["thunderous","soft","scattered","polite"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-thunderous","explain":"thunderous对: 表演精彩后全场erupted(爆发), 掌声要像打雷一样响, thunderous applause是固定搭配。最迷惑的polite错: polite applause是礼貌性稀拉掌声, 跟erupted的热烈气氛不搭。考点: PSLE爱考collocation固定搭配, thunderous applause=雷鸣般的掌声要整组背。"},{"sentence":"She received a ___ welcome from her relatives.","opts":["warm","cold","cool","lukewarm"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-warm welcome","explain":"warm对: 亲戚见面当然热情, warm welcome=热情欢迎, 是最常见搭配。最迷惑的lukewarm错: lukewarm是「不冷不热、冷淡」, 用在welcome上表示不情愿, 和relatives的亲情语境不符。考点: PSLE爱考warm welcome这类高频搭配, warm在这里指态度热情不是温度。"},{"sentence":"The detective examined the crime scene ___ for clues.","opts":["meticulously","carelessly","hastily","casually"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-meticulously","explain":"meticulously对: 侦探找线索必须一丝不苟, meticulously=极其仔细地, 和examined for clues逻辑一致。最迷惑的hastily错: hastily是匆忙地, 匆忙检查会漏掉clues, 和侦探身份矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考副词修饰动词要合职业逻辑, 看到detective+clues就选careful类词。"},{"sentence":"His ___ behaviour in class earned him a detention.","opts":["disruptive","exemplary","polite","respectful"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-disruptive","explain":"disruptive对: 被罚detention说明他捣乱, disruptive=扰乱课堂的, 因果才通。最迷惑的exemplary错: exemplary是「模范的」, 模范行为只会被表扬不会被留堂。考点: PSLE爱考因果逻辑推断, 先看结果earned him a detention再倒推空格是贬义词。"},{"sentence":"The ___ child refused to share his toys with anyone.","opts":["selfish","generous","kind","thoughtful"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-selfish","explain":"selfish对: 不肯和任何人分享玩具就是自私, selfish和refused to share直接对应。最迷惑的generous错: generous是慷慨大方, 大方的孩子恰恰乐意分享, 意思正好相反。考点: PSLE爱考人物性格词与行为描写配对, 空格后的行为就是答案的定义。"},{"sentence":"She was ___ to hear that she had won the scholarship.","opts":["elated","dismayed","indifferent","annoyed"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-elated","explain":"elated对: 赢得奖学金是大喜事, elated=欣喜若狂, 情绪与好消息匹配。最迷惑的dismayed错: dismayed是「惊愕沮丧」, 用于坏消息, 和won the scholarship的喜讯矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考情绪词正负判断, 先定事件好坏再选emotion word, elated是高频褒义词。"},{"sentence":"The explorers faced ___ challenges in the jungle.","opts":["formidable","easy","minor","trivial"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-formidable","explain":"formidable对: 丛林探险艰险重重, formidable=令人生畏的、艰巨的, 和explorers闯jungle的语境相符。最迷惑的minor错: minor是「轻微的」, 丛林里的挑战不会是小事, 削弱了句子想强调的困难。考点: PSLE爱考formidable challenges这类高级搭配, 认得它能和difficult互换。"},{"sentence":"He made a ___ effort to finish the race despite his injury.","opts":["valiant","feeble","half-hearted","lazy"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-valiant","explain":"valiant对: 带伤仍坚持完赛是英勇之举, valiant effort=顽强的努力, 和despite his injury呼应。最迷惑的feeble错: feeble是「无力的」, 无力的努力撑不到终点, 和finish the race矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考despite这类让步信号词, 前后要形成反差, 伤病+完赛=勇敢。"},{"sentence":"The teacher's ___ explanation helped us understand the concept.","opts":["lucid","confusing","vague","unclear"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-lucid","explain":"lucid对: 能让大家听懂的讲解必然清晰, lucid=清楚易懂的, 和helped us understand因果相扣。最迷惑的vague错: vague是「含糊的」, 含糊的解释只会让人更糊涂, 与结果矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考结果句倒推词义, helped us understand锁定褒义, lucid=clear要记牢。"},{"sentence":"She cast a ___ look at the broken vase.","opts":["guilty","proud","satisfied","happy"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-guilty","explain":"guilty对: 花瓶打碎了, 她心虚地看一眼, guilty look=心虚愧疚的眼神, 合情合理。最迷惑的proud错: proud是骄傲, 没人会为打碎花瓶自豪, 情绪和broken vase的事故不符。考点: PSLE爱考cast a look+情绪形容词, 看物件状态(broken)判断人物心情。"},{"sentence":"The ___ silence in the hall was broken by a sudden sneeze.","opts":["deafening","noisy","loud","moderate"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-deafening silence","explain":"deafening对: deafening silence是固定表达「震耳欲聋的寂静」, 故意用矛盾修辞形容极度安静, 才会被一个喷嚏打破。最迷惑的loud错: silence本身没声音, loud silence不是英文惯用搭配, 是中式直译陷阱。考点: PSLE爱考deafening silence这类idiom式搭配, 整组背不拆开理解。"},{"sentence":"He accepted the criticism with ___ and promised to improve.","opts":["grace","anger","resentment","hostility"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-with grace","explain":"grace对: 后半句promised to improve说明他虚心接受, with grace=大度地、有风度地, 前后一致。最迷惑的resentment错: resentment是怨恨, 心怀怨恨的人不会承诺改进, 和and后的内容矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考and连接的前后情绪要同向, accept criticism with grace是加分表达。"},{"sentence":"The news of his promotion spread like ___.","opts":["wildfire","water","wind","ice"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-spread like wildfire","explain":"wildfire对: spread like wildfire是固定idiom「像野火般迅速传开」, 专形容消息传得快。最迷惑的wind错: 风虽然快, 但英文习惯用wildfire不用wind, 这是搭配不是自由造句。最迷惑处就在wind看似合理。考点: PSLE爱考idiom原样搭配, news spread like wildfire整句背下。"},{"sentence":"She was ___ by her friend's sudden outburst.","opts":["taken aback","pleased","amused","delighted"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-taken aback","explain":"taken aback对: 朋友突然发飙(sudden outburst)让人吃惊, be taken aback=大吃一惊, 情境吻合。最迷惑的amused错: amused是觉得好笑, 别人对你发火不好笑, 情绪方向错了。考点: PSLE爱考phrasal verb情绪短语, taken aback=surprised, 看到sudden就找吃惊类词。"},{"sentence":"She is fond ___ singing.","opts":["of","in","at","to"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-fond of","explain":"of对: be fond of是固定搭配「喜爱」, fond后面只能接of, 再接V-ing。最迷惑的in错: interested才配in, fond不配in, 这是两组搭配混淆的经典陷阱。考点: PSLE爱考adjective+preposition固定搭配, fond of/interested in要分开记死。"},{"sentence":"He is capable ___ solving difficult problems.","opts":["of","in","at","to"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-capable of","explain":"of对: be capable of doing是固定搭配「有能力做某事」, capable只跟of。最迷惑的at错: good at里才用at, capable at是错误混搭, 考的就是你别串组。考点: PSLE爱考capable of vs good at, 两个都表「擅长/能做」但介词不同, 成对记。"},{"sentence":"She apologized ___ her rude behaviour.","opts":["for","of","about","to"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-apologize for","explain":"for对: apologize for sth是固定搭配「为某事道歉」, 道歉的原因用for引出。最迷惑的to错: to接的是道歉对象(apologize to him), 这里接的是行为behaviour, 该用for。考点: PSLE爱考apologize to sb for sth双介词结构, 对人用to对事用for。"},{"sentence":"I am looking forward ___ meeting you.","opts":["to","for","at","in"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-look forward to","explain":"to对: look forward to是固定短语「期待」, 这个to是preposition, 所以后面接meeting不是meet。最迷惑的for错: 很多人想「期待for某事」, 但英文里forward只搭to, for是中式思维陷阱。考点: PSLE爱考look forward to+V-ing, to后接动名词是必考陷阱。"},{"sentence":"He insisted ___ paying for dinner.","opts":["on","in","at","for"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-insist on","explain":"on对: insist on doing是固定搭配「坚持要做」, insist后只能接on。最迷惑的in错: persist in才用in, insist用on, 两个「坚持」介词不同最易混。考点: PSLE爱考insist on vs persist in, 意思相近介词不同的verb+preposition要成对背。"},{"sentence":"She blamed him ___ the accident.","opts":["for","on","at","to"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-blame for","explain":"for对: blame sb for sth是固定搭配「因某事责怪某人」, 原因用for。最迷惑的on错: blame sth on sb(把事怪到人头上)也存在, 但那是blame+事+on+人; 这里blame后先接him, 只能用for接原因。考点: PSLE爱考blame的两种句型, blame sb for sth / blame sth on sb别搞反。"},{"sentence":"The teacher was pleased ___ our performance.","opts":["with","of","at","for"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-pleased with","explain":"with对: be pleased with是固定搭配「对…满意」, 对某人表现满意用with。最迷惑的at错: pleased at偶见于对某消息高兴, 但对performance这类成果, 标准搭配是with, 考试按pleased with判。考点: PSLE爱考satisfied/pleased with, 表「对成果满意」一律with。"},{"sentence":"He suffers ___ a rare disease.","opts":["from","of","with","by"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-suffer from","explain":"from对: suffer from是固定搭配「患病、受…折磨」, 接疾病只能用from。最迷惑的of错: 中文「死于/患于」让人想选of, 但英文die of存在, suffer却只搭from, 别类推。考点: PSLE爱考suffer from+疾病, 看到disease/illness直接锁from。"},{"sentence":"She is allergic ___ peanuts.","opts":["to","of","from","with"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-allergic to","explain":"to对: be allergic to是固定搭配「对…过敏」, allergic后面只能接to。最迷惑的from错: 中文说「对花生过敏」像「来自花生的反应」, 有人误选from, 但英文固定用to。考点: PSLE爱考allergic to/similar to这类adj+to搭配, 过敏一律to。"},{"sentence":"I am grateful ___ you ___ your help.","opts":["to/for","for/to","with/for","at/of"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-grateful to...for","explain":"grateful的固定搭配是 grateful to 人 for 事: 感谢的对象用to, 感谢的原因用for。B选项for/to把方向搞反了, 变成\"因为你而感谢帮助\", 逻辑不通。考点: PSLE爱考\"人用to、事用for\"的双介词搭配, 类似的还有 thank you for。"},{"sentence":"He is accustomed ___ waking up early.","opts":["to","of","with","at"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-accustomed to","explain":"be accustomed to 是固定搭配, 意思是\"习惯于\", 这个to是preposition, 后面接waking这种-ing形式。最迷惑的是of, 因为很多形容词配of(如fond of), 但accustomed只认to。考点: PSLE爱考 accustomed to / used to + V-ing, 别把to当infinitive写成wake。"},{"sentence":"She succeeded ___ passing the exam.","opts":["in","at","on","of"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-succeed in","explain":"succeed in doing sth 是固定搭配, \"成功做成某事\"只能用in。最迷惑的是at, 因为 good at 太熟了, 孩子容易照搬, 但succeed不跟at配。考点: PSLE爱考动词固定介词, succeed in 和 good at 要分开记, 不能混用。"},{"sentence":"The book consists ___ ten chapters.","opts":["of","in","with","from"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-consist of","explain":"consist of 是固定搭配, 意思是\"由...组成\", 书由十章组成只能用of。最迷惑的是from, 因为中文\"由...而来\"让人想到from, 但consist from是错的。考点: PSLE爱考组成类短语, consist of = be made up of, 且consist不用被动。"},{"sentence":"He congratulated her ___ her achievement.","opts":["on","for","at","to"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-congratulate on","explain":"congratulate sb on sth 是固定搭配, 祝贺某人某事只能用on。最迷惑的是for, 因为 praise sb for / thank sb for 都用for, 孩子容易套过来, 但congratulate偏偏配on。考点: PSLE爱考易混动词介词, congratulate on 和 thank for 要分开背。"},{"sentence":"She is addicted ___ her phone.","opts":["to","with","of","on"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-addicted to","explain":"be addicted to 是固定搭配, \"沉迷于\"只能用to, 这个to是preposition。最迷惑的是on, 因为中文说\"沉迷在手机上\", 直译会选on, 但英语不这么搭。考点: PSLE爱考带to的形容词短语, addicted to / devoted to / used to 是一家人。"},{"sentence":"They objected ___ the new proposal.","opts":["to","on","at","for"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-object to","explain":"object to 是固定搭配, \"反对\"某事必须加to, object是不及物动词, 不能直接接宾语。最迷惑的是on, 因为\"在提案上有意见\"的中文思路会带偏, 但英语只认object to。考点: PSLE爱考object to / agree to, to后接名词或V-ing。"},{"sentence":"He divided the cake ___ six pieces.","opts":["into","to","in","for"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-divide into","explain":"divide...into 是固定搭配, 把整体切成几份用into, 强调\"变成\"新的状态。最迷惑的是in, 看着只差两个字母, 但in表示位置不表示变化, divide in six pieces是错的。考点: PSLE爱考divide into / cut into / turn into, \"变成\"类都用into。"},{"sentence":"She prevented him ___ making a mistake.","opts":["from","of","to","for"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"prep-prevent from","explain":"prevent sb from doing sth 是固定搭配, \"阻止某人做某事\"只能用from, 表示\"使远离\"。最迷惑的是to, 孩子容易按\"阻止他去做\"翻译成to make, 方向正好反了。考点: PSLE爱考prevent/stop/discourage sb from + V-ing, 阻拦类动词全家用from。"},{"sentence":"I am tired ___ doing the same thing every day.","opts":["of","from","with","about"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-tired of","explain":"be tired of 表示\"厌倦、烦了\", 每天做同样的事让人厌倦, 用of。最迷惑的是from, 因为 tired from 也存在, 但那是\"因劳累而疲惫\"(如tired from running), 这里是心理上的烦。考点: PSLE爱考tired of(厌倦) vs tired from(累), 看语境选介词。"},{"sentence":"He reminds me ___ my grandfather.","opts":["of","about","with","to"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"prep-remind of","explain":"remind sb of sb/sth 是固定搭配, \"让我想起\"某人用of。最迷惑的是about, 因为 remind me about the meeting(提醒某事)也对, 但\"像谁、让人想起谁\"只能用of。考点: PSLE爱考remind of(想起) vs remind about(提醒做事), 两个意思两个介词。"},{"sentence":"The teacher ___ to mark the essay because it was handed in late.","opts":["refused","declined","rejected","denied"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"refused = 主动不做 (后接 to+原形); declined 较正式语气委婉, 多用于邀请; rejected 多用于物/方案; denied = 否认事实"},{"sentence":"After hours of discussion, the committee ___ his proposal as too costly.","opts":["rejected","refused","denied","declined"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"rejected = 经过考虑后拒绝接受 (常用于 proposal/idea/application); refused 是直接不做; denied 是否认; declined 是委婉拒绝邀请"},{"sentence":"Sarah ___ the kind offer, saying she already had plans.","opts":["declined","rejected","refused","denied"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"declined = 礼貌委婉地拒绝 (offer/invitation 必用); rejected 太强烈; refused 太直接"},{"sentence":"The suspect ___ all knowledge of the incident.","opts":["denied","refused","declined","rejected"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"denied = 否认某事真实; 其他都是拒绝做/接受"},{"sentence":"The little girl gazed ___ at the puppy in the window.","opts":["longingly","quickly","barely","sharply"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"longingly = 渴望地 (看到喜欢的东西); quickly 速度; barely 几乎不; sharply 锋利"},{"sentence":"The students ___ when the bell signalled the end of the test.","opts":["rejoiced","wept","frowned","sighed"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"rejoiced = 欢欣 (test 结束是好事); wept 哭; frowned 皱眉; sighed 叹气"},{"sentence":"Despite the heavy rain, the marathon runners ___ on towards the finish line.","opts":["persevered","wavered","hesitated","retreated"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"persevered = 坚持不懈 (常配 on); wavered 动摇; hesitated 犹豫; retreated 撤退"},{"sentence":"My grandmother always speaks ___ about her childhood in the kampong.","opts":["fondly","rudely","briefly","silently"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"fondly = 深情地 (回忆童年正面情感); rudely 粗鲁; briefly 简短; silently 不说话 (矛盾)"},{"sentence":"The dog wagged its tail ___ when its owner came home.","opts":["enthusiastically","reluctantly","clumsily","sluggishly"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"enthusiastically = 兴奋地 (狗见主人); 其他都是负面/慢"},{"sentence":"The chef ___ tasted the soup before serving it to the customers.","opts":["cautiously","reckessly","noisily","rudely"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-synonym","explain":"cautiously = 小心地 (尝汤要谨慎); recklessly 鲁莽; 其他不合适"},{"sentence":"You must ___ a decision quickly before the deadline.","opts":["make","do","take","have"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"make a decision 是固定搭配, 不能用 do/take/have. 同类: make a choice/promise/mistake"},{"sentence":"She ___ great effort to complete the project on time.","opts":["made","did","took","gave"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"made an effort = 努力 (固定); take effort 错; do effort 不存在"},{"sentence":"The team ___ first place in the inter-school competition.","opts":["took","made","did","won"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"took first place = 取得第一 (固定); won 也对但搭\"the competition\", 这里搭 first place 是 took"},{"sentence":"You should ___ your homework before watching TV.","opts":["do","make","take","have"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"do homework 是固定 (与 make 不同); make 用于\"创造\"含义 (make a cake)"},{"sentence":"Please ___ a deep breath and try to calm down.","opts":["take","do","make","have"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"take a breath = 呼吸 (固定); take a look, take a seat 同类"},{"sentence":"The students ___ their best to finish the project on time.","opts":["did","made","took","tried"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"did one's best = 尽全力 (固定); try one's best 也对但题目空格已含 try (tried best 不对)"},{"sentence":"I always ___ the bus to school every morning.","opts":["take","ride","make","do"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"take the bus/train/MRT = 坐 (固定); ride a bike 才对; ride the bus 较少用"},{"sentence":"Please ___ attention to the safety instructions before boarding.","opts":["pay","take","make","give"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"pay attention = 注意 (固定); pay a visit/compliment 同类"},{"sentence":"The new policy will ___ effect from next Monday.","opts":["take","make","do","have"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"take effect = 生效 (固定 - 法律/政策用语); 其他不能搭 effect"},{"sentence":"My father ___ a successful business for over 20 years.","opts":["has run","has done","has made","has had"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"run a business = 经营 (固定); do business 是\"做生意\"但不搭 a"},{"sentence":"___ the heavy rain, we managed to finish the football match.","opts":["Despite","Although","Because of","In addition to"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"Despite + 名词/动名词 (heavy rain 是名词); Although 后跟句子 (Although it rained heavily); Because of 表示因为"},{"sentence":"___ it was raining heavily, we managed to finish the match.","opts":["Although","Despite","Because of","In spite"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"Although + 完整句子; Despite 后只能跟名词/动名词. In spite 必须有 of (In spite of)"},{"sentence":"The class was cancelled ___ the teacher's sudden illness.","opts":["due to","despite","although","therefore"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"due to + 名词原因 (illness 是名词); despite 表让步; although 跟句子; therefore 表结果"},{"sentence":"She studied very hard; ___, she did well in the exam.","opts":["therefore","despite","although","meanwhile"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"therefore = 因此 (前因后果); 用分号后表结论. despite 让步; meanwhile 同时"},{"sentence":"___ I was tired, I had to finish my homework before sleeping.","opts":["Although","Despite","Because","When"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"Although + 完整句 (表让步); Despite 不能后跟句子; Because 表原因 (但这里逻辑是让步)"},{"sentence":"You can either take the bus ___ walk to school.","opts":["or","and","but","nor"],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"either...or 是配对 (固定); either...and/but/nor 都错"},{"sentence":"Neither John ___ his brother enjoys reading novels.","opts":["nor","or","and","but"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"neither...nor 是配对 (固定); 跟 or 是错配; 主谓一致看 nor 后名词 (brother 单数 → enjoys)"},{"sentence":"Not only ___ but he also helps with chores at home.","opts":["does he study hard","he studies hard","he does study hard","he hardly studies"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"Not only 开头需要倒装 (does he study) 不是 he studies; \"Not only does X, but X also\" 是固定结构"},{"sentence":"___ , the team practised every day after school.","opts":["As a result","However","Although","In addition"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"As a result = 结果 (前面有原因, 后面有结果); 用逗号隔开. However 转折; Although 让步"},{"sentence":"I want to be a doctor; ___, my sister wants to be an engineer.","opts":["however","therefore","despite","because"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-connector","explain":"however = 然而 (对比, 我想 vs 她想); therefore 因此; 用分号 + however + 逗号"},{"sentence":"The fire ___ at midnight, destroying the entire warehouse.","opts":["broke out","broke up","broke down","broke in"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"break out = 突然爆发 (fire/war/disease 必搭); break up 分手; break down 故障; break in 闯入"},{"sentence":"My car ___ on the way home, and I had to take a taxi.","opts":["broke down","broke up","broke out","broke in"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"break down = 故障 (机器/车); 其他都不合"},{"sentence":"Please ___ the children while I go to the supermarket.","opts":["look after","look for","look up","look at"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"look after = 照顾 (take care of); look for 寻找; look up 查找 (信息); look at 看"},{"sentence":"I can't find my keys. Help me ___ them.","opts":["look for","look after","look up","look at"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"look for = 寻找 (东西不见了); 区别: look after 照顾人; look up 查找资料"},{"sentence":"Don't ___, you can finish this puzzle if you try harder.","opts":["give up","give in","give out","give away"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"give up = 放弃; give in 屈服; give out 分发; give away 赠送/泄露"},{"sentence":"The teacher will ___ the worksheets at the start of class.","opts":["hand out","hand in","hand over","hand down"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"hand out = 发放; hand in 上交 (homework); hand over 移交权力; hand down 传给下一代"},{"sentence":"Please ___ your homework by Friday.","opts":["hand in","hand out","hand down","hand off"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"hand in = 上交 (作业/试卷); 反义 hand out 发放"},{"sentence":"The plane ___ at 8 am sharp.","opts":["took off","took up","took out","took over"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"take off = 起飞 (飞机); take up 培养爱好; take out 取出; take over 接管"},{"sentence":"I have ___ a new hobby — learning the violin.","opts":["taken up","taken off","taken out","taken over"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"take up = 开始 (爱好/工作); take off 起飞; take over 接管"},{"sentence":"The meeting was ___ to next week due to the typhoon.","opts":["put off","put up","put out","put down"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-phrasal","explain":"put off = 推迟 (postpone); put up 张贴/容忍; put out 熄灭; put down 放下"},{"sentence":"Singapore is famous ___ its hawker food.","opts":["for","with","of","about"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"famous for = 因…而出名 (固定); famous with 错; famous of 错"},{"sentence":"I am proud ___ my younger sister for winning the prize.","opts":["of","with","for","about"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"proud of = 因…而骄傲 (固定); proud with/for 错"},{"sentence":"She is interested ___ studying Mandarin.","opts":["in","at","on","about"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"interested in + 动名词 (固定); interested at/on/about 错"},{"sentence":"My brother is good ___ playing chess.","opts":["at","in","on","for"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"good at = 擅长 (skill); good in/on/for 错. 区别: good for health 是另一个意思 (有益于)"},{"sentence":"The book is similar ___ the one I borrowed last week.","opts":["to","with","as","from"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"similar to = 类似于 (固定); different from; same as. 不要混"},{"sentence":"The teacher accused him ___ cheating during the exam.","opts":["of","for","about","with"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"accuse sb of sth/doing = 指控 (固定); accuse for 错"},{"sentence":"My grandmother suffers ___ arthritis.","opts":["from","of","with","at"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"suffer from = 患…病 (固定); suffer of/with 错"},{"sentence":"The success depends ___ how much effort you put in.","opts":["on","of","with","to"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"depend on = 依赖于 (固定); depend of/with 错"},{"sentence":"The cake consists ___ flour, eggs and sugar.","opts":["of","from","in","with"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"consist of = 由…组成 (固定, 不用被动); 区别: be composed of; be made of/from"},{"sentence":"I apologise ___ being late to class.","opts":["for","about","of","to"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-prep","explain":"apologise for + ing (固定); apologise to + 人; 别混 — apologise to him for being late"},{"sentence":"I have two pens. One is blue and the ___ is red.","opts":["other","another","others","any other"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-another-other","explain":"the other = 两个中的另一个 (确指); another = 还有一个 (再加, 不确指). 真考 17 题孩子写 another 错"},{"sentence":"There are three apples on the table. One is mine, and the ___ two belong to my sister.","opts":["other","another","others","any"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-another-other","explain":"the other + 复数 = 其余的 (剩下都是); another 后只能跟单数; others 是代词不接名词"},{"sentence":"Would you like ___ cup of tea?","opts":["another","other","the other","others"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-another-other","explain":"another + 单数 = 再一个 (不确指); other 后必须有名词复数 或 the other; 这里是 polite offer 用 another"},{"sentence":"___ I see a stray dog, I feel sorry for it.","opts":["Whenever","When","While","As"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-when-whenever","explain":"whenever = 每当 (习惯性, 强调每一次都这样); when = 当...时 (单次或一般); 真考 25 题就是这型, 孩子错"},{"sentence":"___ the bell rings, students rush out of the classroom.","opts":["Whenever","When","Where","That"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-when-whenever","explain":"whenever = 每次都 (习惯) — bell rings 每次都 rush out, 是规律; when 是单次"},{"sentence":"___ we visit grandma, she always cooks our favourite food.","opts":["Whenever","When","Whereas","Wherever"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-when-whenever","explain":"whenever (每次都) + always (总是) 习惯性配对; whereas = 然而 (对比); wherever = 无论哪里"},{"sentence":"I ___ the children playing in the park for an hour.","opts":["watched","saw","looked","noticed"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-saw-watched","explain":"watch = 持续观看 (for an hour 持续动作); saw = 一瞬间看到; look at = 朝某方向看. 真考 20 题孩子写 saw 错"},{"sentence":"As I ___ the ripples form on the water, I felt peaceful.","opts":["watched","saw","looked","viewed"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-saw-watched","explain":"watched 持续观察 (ripples form 涟漪形成是一个过程); saw 是看见一瞬; 真考原题就是这句"},{"sentence":"Dad ___ TV every evening after dinner.","opts":["watches","sees","looks","notices"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-saw-watched","explain":"watch TV 是固定搭配 (持续观看节目); see TV 错"},{"sentence":"The current was ___ strong that I struggled to swim back.","opts":["so","too","very","quite"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-so-too","explain":"so + adj + that = 如此...以致 (结构固定); too + adj + to + 动 (不能跟 that); 真考 23 题孩子写 too 错"},{"sentence":"The film was ___ boring that we all fell asleep.","opts":["so","too","very","really"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-so-too","explain":"so...that = 结果状语从句; too...that 不存在; too...to 才对"},{"sentence":"The bag is ___ heavy for me to carry.","opts":["too","so","very","enough"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-so-too","explain":"too + adj + (for sb) + to + 动 = 太...而不能 (结构); so 后跟 that 从句"},{"sentence":"I always tell ___ to stay calm during exams.","opts":["myself","me","him","my"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-reflexive","explain":"反身代词: 主语和宾语同一人 → 用 myself. I + tell + me 错 (要 myself); 真考 26 题孩子写 him 错"},{"sentence":"She made the cake all by ___.","opts":["herself","her","she","hers"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-reflexive","explain":"by + 反身代词 = 独自. by herself = 她自己 (没人帮); by her 是 \"由她\" 不同意"},{"sentence":"The children dressed ___ before going to school.","opts":["themselves","them","their","they"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-reflexive","explain":"主语 children = 复数, 反身 themselves; dress oneself = 给自己穿衣 (动作返回主语)"},{"sentence":"I was so angry that I could not stop ___ from yelling.","opts":["myself","me","I","mine"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-reflexive","explain":"stop + oneself + from = 阻止自己 (反身); 主语 I, 宾语 myself"},{"sentence":"The lifeguard pulled the drowning child to ___.","opts":["safety","ground","land","dry"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-collocation-safety","explain":"pull/bring/get sb to safety = 救出脱险 (固定搭配, \"safety\" 抽象名词); pull to ground 不对; 真考 30 题孩子写 ground 错"},{"sentence":"Despite the heavy traffic, we arrived ___ on time.","opts":["just","very","too","quite"],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"vocab-collocation","explain":"just on time = 刚好准时 (固定); very on time 不自然"},{"sentence":"The river was ___ across the village, bringing fresh water.","opts":["flowing","flow","flowed","flows"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-word-form","explain":"was + V-ing = 过去进行 (河流持续流动). 真考 16 题孩子写 Across 错 (Across 是 prep 不是动词形式, 应该用 ing) "},{"sentence":"The dog was ___ in the river before its owner rescued it.","opts":["drowning","sinking","sanking","sank"],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"vocab-word-form","explain":"drowning = 正在溺水 (was + V-ing); sanking 不是英文词 (sank 才是过去式); sinking 是船下沉用. 真考 29 题孩子写 sanked 错"}];

// ============= v19.4: SST (Synthesis & Transformation) 题库 =============
// PSLE Paper 2 Section C: 5 题 × 2 分 = 10 分
// 格式: 给原句 + 转换要求, 选正确的转换结果 (MCQ 化 — app 内可自动判分)
const SST_QUESTIONS = [{"q":"\"I am going to the market,\" said Mum.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["Mum said that she was going to the market.","Mum said that I am going to the market.","Mum said that she is going to the market.","Mum said she will go to the market."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect","explain":"直接引语变间接: I→she, am going→was going(时态退一步)。选C错在is going没退时态, 转述过去说的话要用past tense。考点: PSLE爱考reported speech时态后移+人称转换。"},{"q":"\"We will visit you tomorrow,\" they promised.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["They promised that they would visit us the next day.","They promised that we will visit you tomorrow.","They promised they would visit me the next day.","They promise that they will visit us tomorrow."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect","explain":"三处齐变: will→would, tomorrow→the next day, you→us才对。选C最迷惑: would和the next day都对了, 但us偷偷变成me, 人称漏改照样扣分。考点: PSLE爱考时间词tomorrow→the next day的转换。"},{"q":"\"Do you like ice cream?\" she asked me.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["She asked me if I liked ice cream.","She asked me do I like ice cream.","She asked me that I liked ice cream.","She asked me whether do I like ice cream."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-question","explain":"yes/no问句转述用if/whether引出, 且变陈述语序: I liked。选D最坑: whether后面还留着do I like的疑问语序, 转述后不能再倒装。考点: PSLE爱考间接问句必须用陈述语序。"},{"q":"\"Don't run in the corridor,\" the teacher told us.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["The teacher told us not to run in the corridor.","The teacher told us don't run in the corridor.","The teacher said us not to run in the corridor.","The teacher told us to not run in the corridor."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-imperative","explain":"转述否定命令固定公式: told + 人 + not to + 动词。选D的to not run语序错, not必须放在to前面。选B直接照抄don't也不行。考点: PSLE爱考not to do的否定祈使句转述。"},{"q":"\"Where did you put my keys?\" Dad asked.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["Dad asked where I had put his keys.","Dad asked where did I put his keys.","Dad asked me where I put my keys.","Dad asked that where did I put his keys."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-wh","explain":"wh-问句转述: 陈述语序 + 时态退一步(did put→had put) + my→his。选B最迷惑: 只改了人称, 却保留did I put的疑问语序。考点: PSLE爱考wh-question转述去掉did改用had done。"},{"q":"Mum told me not to stay up late.","rule":"Rewrite in direct speech.","opts":["\"Don't stay up late,\" Mum told me.","\"You must not stay up late,\" Mum told me.","\"I told you not to stay up late,\" Mum said.","\"Don't stay up late,\" Mum said to her."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-indirect-direct","explain":"not to stay还原成祈使句Don't stay, told me保留不动。选D最坑: 句子看着对, 但Mum said to her人称错了, 原句是told me, 该是told me。考点: PSLE爱考间接转直接时人称要还原成对话现场。"},{"q":"He said that he had already eaten.","rule":"Rewrite in direct speech.","opts":["\"I have already eaten,\" he said.","\"I had already eaten,\" he said.","\"He has already eaten,\" he said.","\"I already ate,\" he said."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-indirect-direct","explain":"间接语had eaten退回直接语就是have eaten(时态往前推一步), he还原成I。选B最迷惑: 直接照抄had already eaten, 忘了时态要还原。考点: PSLE爱考past perfect还原成present perfect。"},{"q":"She asked him whether he could help her.","rule":"Rewrite in direct speech.","opts":["\"Can you help me?\" she asked him.","\"Could you help me?\" she asked him.","\"Can you help her?\" she asked.","\"Will you help me?\" she asked."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-indirect-direct-question","explain":"could在转述里是can退位来的, 还原直接语用Can you, her→me。选B最坑: 保留Could也说得通礼貌, 但标准还原是can, 且题目要最贴原意。考点: PSLE爱考情态动词can/could在转述中的升降。"},{"q":"\"I have been waiting for an hour,\" he complained.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["He complained that he had been waiting for an hour.","He complained that I have been waiting for an hour.","He complained he has been waiting for an hour.","He complains that he had been waiting for an hour."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-perfect","explain":"have been waiting退一步变had been waiting, I→he, 完美转述。选C最迷惑: 人称对了但has been没退成had been, 还丢了that后的完整时态。考点: PSLE爱考现在完成进行时转述变过去完成进行时。"},{"q":"\"Please close the door,\" the teacher said to Ali.","rule":"Rewrite in reported speech.","opts":["The teacher asked Ali to close the door.","The teacher told Ali please close the door.","The teacher said Ali to close the door.","The teacher asked Ali close the door."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-direct-indirect-polite","explain":"带please的礼貌请求, 转述动词用asked + 人 + to do。选C最坑: said Ali to close看着顺, 但said后面不能直接接人, 必须said to或改用told/asked。考点: PSLE爱考please请求句用asked...to转述。"},{"q":"The dog chased the cat.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["The cat was chased by the dog.","The cat is chased by the dog.","The cat has been chased by the dog.","The dog was chased by the cat."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-active-passive","explain":"原句是过去式chased, 被动就是was chased, 宾语cat当主语。选C最迷惑: has been chased时态凭空升级成完成时, 被动转换时态必须原样保留。考点: PSLE爱考被动语态时态与原句一致。"},{"q":"Someone stole my bicycle yesterday.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["My bicycle was stolen yesterday.","My bicycle is stolen yesterday.","My bicycle has been stolen yesterday.","Someone was stolen my bicycle."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-active-passive-agent","explain":"yesterday锁定过去式: was stolen; someone是无名氏, by someone可省。选C最坑: has been stolen和yesterday打架, 完成时不能带明确过去时间词。考点: PSLE爱考yesterday排除present perfect。"},{"q":"The students are cleaning the classroom now.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["The classroom is being cleaned by the students now.","The classroom is cleaned by the students now.","The classroom was being cleaned now.","The classroom has been cleaned now."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-active-passive-continuous","explain":"现在进行时被动固定搭配: is being cleaned, now保留。选B最迷惑: is cleaned是一般现在时, 丢了正在进行的意思, 和now不匹配。考点: PSLE爱考进行时被动is being done。"},{"q":"They will announce the results next week.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["The results will be announced next week.","The results are announced next week.","The results would be announced next week.","The results will announce next week."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-active-passive-future","explain":"将来时被动: will be announced, 时态跟原句will走。选C最坑: would be announced偷偷降成过去将来, 原句没这个语境。考点: PSLE爱考will+be+过去分词的将来被动。"},{"q":"The cake was baked by my grandmother.","rule":"Rewrite in the active voice.","opts":["My grandmother baked the cake.","My grandmother was baking the cake.","The cake baked my grandmother.","My grandmother has baked the cake."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-passive-active","explain":"was baked还原主动就是过去式baked, grandmother回到主语位。选B最迷惑: was baking是进行时, 原句只是简单过去, 时态被偷换。考点: PSLE爱考被动转主动时态严格对应。"},{"q":"You must complete the assignment by Friday.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["The assignment must be completed by Friday.","The assignment must complete by Friday.","The assignment is completed by Friday.","You must be completed the assignment."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-active-passive-modal","explain":"情态动词被动公式: must + be + 过去分词, 即must be completed。选B最坑: must complete少了be, 变成主动形式却没主语做事的人, 语法崩了。考点: PSLE爱考modal+be+done的被动结构。"},{"q":"The children have eaten all the cookies.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["All the cookies have been eaten by the children.","All the cookies has been eaten by the children.","All the cookies were eaten by the children.","All the cookies had been eaten."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-active-passive-perfect","explain":"现在完成时被动: have been eaten, cookies是复数所以用have。选C最迷惑: were eaten语法本身没错, 但把完成时改成过去时, 时态变了就不忠实原句。考点: PSLE爱考完成时被动have/has been done。"},{"q":"People speak English all over the world.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["English is spoken all over the world.","English was spoken all over the world.","English has been spoken all over the world.","English speaks all over the world."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-active-passive-general","explain":"一般现在时表普遍事实: is spoken, people泛指可省略。选C最坑: has been spoken看着高级, 但原句是习惯性事实, 不该换成完成时。考点: PSLE爱考general truth用一般现在时被动。"},{"q":"The letter was written by Sarah.","rule":"Rewrite in the active voice.","opts":["Sarah wrote the letter.","Sarah writes the letter.","Sarah has written the letter.","Sarah was writing the letter."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-passive-active","explain":"was written还原成过去式wrote, Sarah做主语, 干净利落。选C最迷惑: has written时态升级成完成时, 被动转主动只换语态不换时态。考点: PSLE爱考语态转换时态原封不动。"},{"q":"They are going to build a new mall here.","rule":"Rewrite in the passive voice.","opts":["A new mall is going to be built here.","A new mall is built here.","A new mall will going to be built here.","A new mall was going to be built here."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-active-passive-going to","explain":"be going to的被动: is going to be built, 只在going to后面加be+done。选C最坑: will和going to叠在一起, 两个将来时结构不能混用。考点: PSLE爱考going to被动只改后半段。"},{"q":"Study hard or you will fail.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If you do not study hard, you will fail.","If you study hard, you will fail.","If you fail, you will study hard.","If you do not fail, study hard."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-if","explain":"or前是命令or后是坏结果, 翻成If就要反着说: 不努力才会fail。选B最迷惑: 直接照抄study hard却接will fail, 逻辑正好颠倒。考点: PSLE爱考祈使句+or改If要加否定。"},{"q":"If you do not hurry, you will miss the bus.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus.","Unless you do not hurry, you will miss the bus.","Unless you miss the bus, you will hurry.","Unless you hurry, you will not miss the bus."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless","explain":"Unless自带如果不, 所以原句的do not hurry直接变Unless you hurry。选B最坑: unless后面又放not, 双重否定把意思弄反了。考点: PSLE爱考Unless=If not, 后面不能再加not。"},{"q":"Unless she apologizes, I will not forgive her.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If she does not apologize, I will not forgive her.","If she apologizes, I will not forgive her.","If I do not forgive her, she will apologize.","If she does not apologize, I will forgive her."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless-to-if","explain":"Unless she apologizes = If she does not apologize, 主句原样保留。选D最迷惑: 前半对了, 后半却把not forgive改成forgive, 结果反了。考点: PSLE爱考Unless转If时主句一个字都别动。"},{"q":"Bring an umbrella or you will get wet.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless you bring an umbrella, you will get wet.","Unless you get wet, bring an umbrella.","Unless you do not bring an umbrella, you will get wet.","Unless you bring an umbrella, you will not get wet."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless","explain":"带伞是免遭淋湿的条件, Unless you bring正好表达不带就湿。选C最坑: unless后加do not bring, 双重否定变成带了伞反而湿。考点: PSLE爱考Unless句内禁止再放not。"},{"q":"If it does not rain, we will have a barbecue.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless it rains, we will have a barbecue.","Unless it does not rain, we will have a barbecue.","Unless we have a barbecue, it will not rain.","Unless it rains, we will not have a barbecue."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-if-to-unless","explain":"If it does not rain = Unless it rains, 主句we will have照搬。选D最迷惑: 前半漂亮, 后半偷偷加了not, 烧烤变泡汤。考点: PSLE爱考If not转Unless只改条件句不动主句。"},{"q":"You cannot enter unless you have a ticket.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If you do not have a ticket, you cannot enter.","If you have a ticket, you cannot enter.","If you cannot enter, you do not have a ticket.","If you do not enter, you have a ticket."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless-to-if","explain":"unless=if not, 所以unless you have a ticket要变成if you do not have a ticket, 主句原样保留。B错在把否定丢了: 保留了have a ticket却不加not, 意思变成有票反而不能进, 正好说反。考点: PSLE爱考unless和if not互换, 只改条件句不动主句"},{"q":"Work harder or you will not get promoted.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If you do not work harder, you will not get promoted.","If you work harder, you will not get promoted.","If you get promoted, work harder.","If you do not get promoted, work harder."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-if","explain":"祈使句+or是警告: 不照做就有坏结果, 改写成If you do not work harder+原后果。B错在漏掉do not, 变成越努力越不升职, 逻辑颠倒。考点: PSLE爱考or前的命令改成if否定条件, 主句照抄不改"},{"q":"If she does not practise daily, she will not improve.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless she practises daily, she will not improve.","Unless she does not practise daily, she will improve.","Unless she improves, she will not practise.","Unless she practises, she will improve."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-if-to-unless","explain":"if...not直接换成unless, 动词回到肯定practises, 主句will not improve不动。B错在unless后面又加does not, 双重否定, unless本身已含not, 不能再否定一次。考点: PSLE爱考unless后必须用肯定动词, 双重否定必错"},{"q":"Unless you leave now, you will be late.","rule":"Rewrite using \"If\".","opts":["If you do not leave now, you will be late.","If you leave now, you will be late.","If you are late, leave now.","If you do not leave, you will not be late."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless-to-if","explain":"unless换成if not: unless you leave now = if you do not leave now, 主句照抄。B错在只换词不加not, 变成走了反而迟到, 意思反了。考点: PSLE爱考unless转if要补do not, 条件与结果关系不能变"},{"q":"Be quiet or the teacher will punish you.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Unless\".","opts":["Unless you are quiet, the teacher will punish you.","Unless the teacher punishes you, be quiet.","Unless you are not quiet, the teacher will punish you.","Unless you are quiet, the teacher will not punish you."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-unless","explain":"命令Be quiet的反面是不安静, unless you are quiet=如果你不安静, 接原后果老师会罚你。C错在unless后加not, 双重否定变成不不安静, unless自带否定不能再加。考点: PSLE爱考unless句内动词保持肯定形式"},{"q":"The box was too heavy for me to carry.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The box was so heavy that I could not carry it.","The box was so heavy that I can carry it.","The box was so heavy that I carried it.","The box is so heavy that I could not carry."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-so-that","explain":"too...to换so...that: too heavy to carry=heavy到搬不动, that后要补完整句I could not carry it, 句尾it不能少。B错在could变can且没有not, 变成重到搬得动, 意思相反。考点: PSLE爱考so...that后补could not+宾语it"},{"q":"She is so kind that everyone likes her.","rule":"Rewrite using \"such\".","opts":["She is such a kind person that everyone likes her.","She is such kind that everyone likes her.","Such kind she is that everyone likes her.","She is such a kind that everyone likes her."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-so-to-such","explain":"so+形容词变such时要补名词: such a kind person, 因为such修饰名词短语不是光秃秃的形容词。B错在such直接接kind没有名词, such不能单独带形容词, 那是so的用法。考点: PSLE爱考so+adj对应such+a+adj+名词"},{"q":"He ran so fast that no one could catch him.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["He ran too fast for anyone to catch him.","He ran too fast to catch.","He ran too fast that no one caught him.","He was too fast to catch no one."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-so-to-too","explain":"so fast that no one could catch him改too...to: 否定意思藏进too里, 人物用for anyone带出, 后面to catch him。B错在丢了catch的宾语him和执行者, 句意残缺不知谁抓谁。考点: PSLE爱考too...for someone to do带出动作执行者"},{"q":"The boy is too short to reach the shelf.","rule":"Rewrite using \"not...enough\".","opts":["The boy is not tall enough to reach the shelf.","The boy is not short enough to reach the shelf.","The boy is not enough tall to reach the shelf.","The boy is enough short to reach the shelf."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-enough","explain":"too short=矮到够不着, 改not...enough要换成反义词tall: not tall enough, 不够高。B错在照抄short, not short enough意思是不够矮, 跟够不着货架完全对不上。考点: PSLE爱考too+adj转not+反义词+enough"},{"q":"She is not old enough to drive.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["She is too young to drive.","She is too old to drive.","She is too enough to drive.","She is not too old to drive."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-enough-to-too","explain":"not old enough=不够大, 换too要用反义词young: too young to drive, 太小不能开车。B错在照抄old, too old to drive变成太老不能开, 年龄方向整个反了。考点: PSLE爱考enough转too必须换反义形容词"},{"q":"It was such a boring movie that we left early.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The movie was so boring that we left early.","The movie was so boring such that we left early.","It was so a boring movie that we left.","The movie so boring was that we left."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-such-to-so","explain":"such a boring movie转so: 把名词movie提到主语位置, The movie was so boring that..., so只接形容词。B错在so和such两个词叠着用, 一句话只能选一个结构, 混用必错。考点: PSLE爱考such+名词与so+形容词的互换"},{"q":"The water is too cold for swimming.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The water is so cold that we cannot swim in it.","The water is so cold that we can swim.","The water is so cold for swimming.","The water is so cold that it is too cold."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-so-that","explain":"too cold for swimming=冷到没法游, 改so...that要把结果写成完整否定句we cannot swim in it。B错在丢了not, 变成冷到能游泳, 因果关系荒唐。考点: PSLE爱考too含否定意味, 转so...that必须补cannot"},{"q":"He spoke so softly that I could not hear him.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["He spoke too softly for me to hear.","He spoke too softly to hear him.","He spoke too softly that I could not hear.","He was too soft for me to hear."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-so-to-too","explain":"so softly that I could not hear改too...to: 否定收进too, 听的人用for me引出, to hear结尾。B错在to hear him前没有for me, 读起来像他自己听不见自己, 对象丢了。考点: PSLE爱考too...to句型用for sb标明谁做不到"},{"q":"The question was too difficult for us to answer.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The question was so difficult that we could not answer it.","The question was so difficult that we answer it.","The question was so difficult to answer.","The question so difficult that we could not answer."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-so-that","explain":"too difficult to answer转so...that: that后写完整句we could not answer it, 否定和宾语it都要补齐。B错在没有not, 变成难到我们答出来了, 前后矛盾。考点: PSLE爱考so...that从句补could not和代词宾语"},{"q":"It was such a heavy bag that she could not lift it.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["The bag was too heavy for her to lift.","The bag was too heavy that she lifted it.","It was too a heavy bag for her.","She was too heavy to lift the bag."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-such-to-too","explain":"such a heavy bag she could not lift转too: The bag was too heavy for her to lift, 否定藏进too, to后不再重复it。B错在too和that混搭, too...to结构里不能出现that从句。考点: PSLE爱考too...to句尾不加宾语it也不带that"},{"q":"She sings so well that she won the competition.","rule":"Rewrite using \"such\".","opts":["She is such a good singer that she won the competition.","She sings such well that she won.","Such well she sings that she won.","She is such good at singing that she won."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-so-to-such","explain":"sings so well转such要变词性: 动词sing变名词singer, 副词well变形容词good, such a good singer。B错在such直接接副词well, such只能修饰名词短语。考点: PSLE爱考so+副词转such时动词变名词副词变形容词"},{"q":"The child is not strong enough to move the table.","rule":"Rewrite using \"too...to\".","opts":["The child is too weak to move the table.","The child is too strong to move the table.","The child is too not strong to move.","The child is too enough to move the table."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-enough-to-too","explain":"not strong enough=不够壮, 转too用反义词weak: too weak to move, 太弱搬不动。B错在照抄strong, too strong to move变成太壮反而搬不动, 完全讲不通。考点: PSLE爱考enough转too换反义形容词, 方向别搞反"},{"q":"The soup was so hot that I burned my tongue.","rule":"Rewrite using \"such\".","opts":["It was such hot soup that I burned my tongue.","It was such a hot soup that I burned my tongue.","The soup was such hot that I burned.","Such hot soup that I burned my tongue."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-so-to-such","explain":"so hot转such要带名词: such a hot soup, such+a+形容词+名词才完整。A最迷惑, 错在少了冠词a, soup这里当一碗汤是可数的, such hot soup缺a不合PSLE标准答案。考点: PSLE爱考such后单数可数名词必须加a"},{"q":"He is too tired to continue studying.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["He is so tired that he cannot continue studying.","He is so tired that he can continue studying.","He is so tired to continue studying.","He so tired that he cannot continue."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-too-to-so-that","explain":"too tired to continue转so...that: 补出完整结果句he cannot continue studying, 否定必须写明。B错在丢了not, 变成累到还能继续学, 因果反了。考点: PSLE爱考too自带否定, 转so...that要显式加cannot"},{"q":"The room is big enough for ten people.","rule":"Rewrite using \"so...that\".","opts":["The room is so big that it can fit ten people.","The room is so big that ten people is enough.","The room so big that ten people fit.","The room is so big enough for ten."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-enough-to-so","explain":"big enough for ten people转so...that: 结果句写成it can fit ten people, 肯定意思保持肯定。B错在that从句里又塞enough, 两种句型不能叠, 且ten people is单复数也错。考点: PSLE爱考enough转so...that用can表做得到"},{"q":"Although he was tired, he finished his homework.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite being tired, he finished his homework.","Despite he was tired, he finished his homework.","Despite tired, he finished his homework.","Despite his tiredness, he not finished."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-although-despite","explain":"Although+句子转Despite+短语: Despite后不能接主谓句, 要用动名词being tired。B错在Despite后直接跟he was tired完整句子, Despite是介词只吃名词或V-ing。考点: PSLE爱考Despite接名词或being+adj, 不接句子"},{"q":"Despite the rain, we went for a walk.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Although\".","opts":["Although it was raining, we went for a walk.","Although despite the rain, we walked.","Although the rain, we went for a walk.","Although it rained, we did not walk."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-despite-although","explain":"Despite+名词转Although+句子: Although是连词, 后面必须补完整主谓it was raining。C错在Although直接接名词the rain没有动词, 那是Despite的接法, 两者用法正好互补。考点: PSLE爱考Although接完整句, Despite接名词短语"},{"q":"She is smart but lazy.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Although\".","opts":["Although she is smart, she is lazy.","Although she is lazy, she is smart.","Although smart but lazy.","Although she is smart and lazy."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-but-although","explain":"but表转折, 换Although把让步放前: Although she is smart, she is lazy, 惊讶点是聪明却懒。B错在把两个形容词位置调换, Although she is lazy, she is smart意思变成懒却聪明, 强调重点反了。考点: PSLE爱考but转Although保持转折方向不变"},{"q":"In spite of his age, he is still very active.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Although\".","opts":["Although he is old, he is still very active.","Although his age, he is very active.","Although in spite of his age, he is active.","Although he is active, he is old."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-in spite-although","explain":"In spite of his age转Although要展开成句子: his age指他年纪大, 写成he is old。B错在Although后只接名词his age没有动词, Although必须带完整主谓结构。考点: PSLE爱考名词短语转Although从句要自己补出形容词句"},{"q":"Although the food was expensive, we ordered it.","rule":"Rewrite using \"In spite of\".","opts":["In spite of the expensive food, we ordered it.","In spite of the food was expensive, we ordered.","In spite although expensive, we ordered.","In spite of expensive, we ordered it."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-although-in spite","explain":"Although句子转In spite of短语: 把the food was expensive压缩成名词短语the expensive food, 形容词挪到名词前。B错在In spite of后照抄完整句子the food was expensive, 介词短语后不能接主谓句。考点: PSLE爱考In spite of+the+adj+名词的压缩改写"},{"q":"Despite studying hard, she failed the test.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Although\".","opts":["Although she studied hard, she failed the test.","Although despite studying hard, she failed.","Although she failed, she studied hard.","Although studying hard, she failed."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-despite-although","explain":"规则: Although后面必须接完整句子(主语+动词), 「she studied hard」正是完整句, 前后意思也没颠倒。B最迷惑: Although和despite都是「虽然」, 挤在一起等于说了两遍, 只能二选一。考点: PSLE爱考Although接句子, Despite接名词或V-ing, 两者不能同框。"},{"q":"He is rich but unhappy.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite being rich, he is unhappy.","Despite rich, he is unhappy.","Despite he is rich, he is unhappy.","Despite his rich, he is unhappy."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-but-despite","explain":"规则: Despite是介词, 后面只能接名词或V-ing, 所以形容词rich要变成being rich。C最迷惑: 「Despite he is rich」看着通顺, 但介词后不能接完整句子, 那是Although的地盘。考点: PSLE爱考Despite+being+形容词的改写, but句变Despite句必带being。"},{"q":"Although she was nervous, she gave an excellent speech.","rule":"Rewrite using \"In spite of\".","opts":["In spite of her nervousness, she gave an excellent speech.","In spite of she was nervous, she gave a speech.","In spite of nervous, she gave a speech.","In spite of her speech, she was nervous."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-although-in spite","explain":"规则: In spite of和Despite一样是介词短语, 后接名词, 所以形容词nervous要变名词nervousness, 加her更完整。B最迷惑: 直接塞进完整句子「she was nervous」, 介词后不能带主谓, 直接扣分。考点: PSLE爱考形容词变名词, nervous→nervousness这类词形转换要背熟。"},{"q":"Despite the heavy traffic, he arrived on time.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Even though\".","opts":["Even though the traffic was heavy, he arrived on time.","Even though despite heavy traffic, he arrived.","Even though he arrived, the traffic was heavy.","Even though the heavy traffic, he arrived."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-despite-even though","explain":"规则: Even though是连词, 后面要接完整句子, 所以名词短语the heavy traffic得展开成「the traffic was heavy」。D最迷惑: 照抄原句名词短语, 但Even though后没有动词was, 句子残缺。考点: PSLE爱考Despite+名词改Even though+句子, 记住要自己补出be动词。"},{"q":"She is young but very responsible.","rule":"Rewrite using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite her young age, she is very responsible.","Despite she is young, she is responsible.","Despite young, she is responsible.","Despite her responsible, she is young."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-but-despite","explain":"规则: Despite后接名词短语, 「her young age」把形容词young包进名词age里, 转换最地道。B最迷惑: 接了完整句子「she is young」, 介词despite后面绝不能有主语加动词。考点: PSLE爱考young改her young age这种形容词转名词短语的包装术。"},{"q":"He is smart. He is also hardworking.","rule":"Combine using \"Not only...but also\".","opts":["He is not only smart but also hardworking.","He is not only smart and also hardworking.","Not only he is smart but also hardworking.","He is not only smart but hardworking also."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-not only but also","explain":"规则: not only和but also要放在对称位置, 各自后面都跟形容词(smart/hardworking), 结构工整。B最迷惑: 用and also代替but also, 但这是固定搭配, not only必须配but also, and混不进来。考点: PSLE爱考correlative conjunctions固定配对, not only...but also一个字都不能换。"},{"q":"She can sing. She can also dance.","rule":"Combine using \"Both...and\".","opts":["She can both sing and dance.","She both can sing and dance.","Both she can sing and dance.","She can both sing and also dance."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-both and","explain":"规则: both...and连接的两样东西要对称, 都放在情态动词can之后, sing和dance都是动词原形, 平衡。D最迷惑: 多塞了一个also, 但both...and本身已表示「两者都」, also纯属画蛇添足。考点: PSLE爱考both...and的平行结构, and后面不加also不加别的。"},{"q":"Tom did not come. Jerry did not come.","rule":"Combine using \"Neither...nor\".","opts":["Neither Tom nor Jerry came.","Neither Tom nor Jerry did not come.","Neither Tom and Jerry came.","Neither Tom or Jerry came."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-neither nor","explain":"规则: neither...nor本身已是否定, 动词用肯定式came即可, 意思就是两人都没来。B最迷惑: 又加did not come, 双重否定变成「两人都来了」, 意思整个反了。考点: PSLE爱考neither...nor自带否定, 动词绝不能再用not。"},{"q":"You can have tea. You can have coffee.","rule":"Combine using \"Either...or\".","opts":["You can have either tea or coffee.","You can have either tea and coffee.","Either you can have tea or coffee.","You can either have tea or coffee."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-either or","explain":"规则: either...or连接的是两个选项, 都放在have之后, tea和coffee对称, 位置最工整。D最迷惑: 「You can either have tea or coffee」看似通顺, 但either提前后连接的变成have tea和coffee, 不对称, 标准答案要求either紧贴选项。考点: PSLE爱考either...or的平行位置, either放在两个并列词的正前方。"},{"q":"She plays the piano. She also plays the violin.","rule":"Combine using \"Not only...but also\".","opts":["She plays not only the piano but also the violin.","Not only she plays piano but also violin.","She not only plays piano but also the violin.","She plays not only piano and also violin."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-not only but also","explain":"规则: not only和but also对称地各接一个名词短语(the piano/the violin), 冠词the都保留, 结构平衡。C最迷惑: not only接动词plays piano, but also却接名词the violin, 前后词性不对称还丢了the。考点: PSLE爱考平行结构, not only后是什么词性, but also后就得是什么词性。"},{"q":"The movie was not funny. It was not interesting either.","rule":"Combine using \"Neither...nor\".","opts":["The movie was neither funny nor interesting.","The movie was neither funny or interesting.","Neither the movie was funny nor interesting.","The movie neither was funny nor interesting."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-neither nor","explain":"规则: neither...nor放在be动词was之后, 对称连接两个形容词funny和interesting, 位置正确。B最迷惑: 用or代替nor, 但neither的固定搭档只有nor, neither...or是经典陷阱。考点: PSLE爱考neither配nor不配or, 看到neither先找nor。"},{"q":"He can fix the car. His brother can fix the car.","rule":"Combine using \"Both...and\".","opts":["Both he and his brother can fix the car.","Both he or his brother can fix the car.","He both and his brother can fix the car.","Both him and his brother can fix the car."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-both and","explain":"规则: both...and连接两个主语时用主格, he和his brother并列做主语, 动词can不变。D最迷惑: 用him听着顺口(口语常这么说), 但做主语必须用主格he, PSLE按书面语法判。考点: PSLE爱考并列主语用主格, Both he and..., 不是Both him。"},{"q":"You must leave now. Otherwise, you will be late.","rule":"Combine using \"Either...or\".","opts":["Either you leave now or you will be late.","Either you leave now and you will be late.","You either leave now or will be late.","Either leave now or late."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-either or","explain":"规则: either...or连接两个完整的选择结果: 要么现在走, 要么迟到, 两个分句对称且逻辑通。C最迷惑: 「You either leave now or will be late」把主语提前, 但or后只剩will be late没主语, 前后不对称。考点: PSLE爱考otherwise句改Either...or, 两边各留一个完整分句最稳。"},{"q":"She did not eat the cake. She did not eat the pie.","rule":"Combine using \"Neither...nor\".","opts":["She ate neither the cake nor the pie.","She neither ate the cake nor the pie.","She ate neither cake or pie.","Neither she ate cake nor pie."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-neither nor","explain":"规则: neither...nor放在动词ate之后, 对称连接两个宾语the cake和the pie, 冠词齐全。B最迷惑: 「She neither ate the cake nor the pie」里neither接动词ate, nor却接名词, 前后不对称。考点: PSLE爱考neither...nor紧贴并列的宾语, 动词放外面只写一次。"},{"q":"He is talented. He is also humble.","rule":"Combine using \"Not only...but also\".","opts":["He is not only talented but also humble.","Not only is he talented but also humble.","He is not only talented and humble.","He not only is talented but also humble."],"ans":0,"diff":3,"tag":"sst-not only but also","explain":"规则: not only...but also对称连接两个形容词talented和humble, 都在is之后, 结构工整。B最迷惑: 「Not only is he talented」的倒装其实是高级正确用法, 但后半句丢了主语he is, 前后不完整, PSLE按最规范的A判。考点: PSLE爱考not only...but also平行对称, 小学阶段别碰倒装, 老实放在be动词后最安全。"},{"q":"The chef had prepared the meal before the guests arrived.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["The meal had been prepared by the chef before the guests arrived.","The meal was prepared by the chef before the guests arrived.","The meal had prepared by the chef before the guests arrived.","The meal has been prepared by the chef before the guests arrived."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"原句是过去完成时 had prepared → 被动: had been prepared. B 时态降级了 (was = 普通过去); C 缺 been; D 用了现在完成 has been (错)"},{"q":"They are repairing the road outside our school.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["The road outside our school is being repaired.","The road outside our school is repaired.","The road outside our school has been repaired.","The road outside our school was being repaired."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"现在进行时 are repairing → 被动 is being repaired. B 漏掉 being (变成现在时); C 是现在完成; D 是过去进行"},{"q":"The teacher will mark the exam papers this weekend.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["The exam papers will be marked by the teacher this weekend.","The exam papers will marked by the teacher this weekend.","The exam papers will have been marked by the teacher this weekend.","The exam papers are marked by the teacher this weekend."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"will + 动 → 被动: will be + p.p. B 漏 be; C 用了将来完成 will have been (语义变); D 改成现在时"},{"q":"Someone has stolen my bicycle from the bicycle stand.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["My bicycle has been stolen from the bicycle stand.","My bicycle was stolen from the bicycle stand.","My bicycle is stolen from the bicycle stand.","My bicycle had been stolen from the bicycle stand."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"现在完成 has stolen → 被动 has been stolen. B 用了过去式; C 现在时; D 过去完成. PSLE 高频陷阱"},{"q":"The children must complete their homework before bedtime.","rule":"Rewrite in passive voice.","opts":["Their homework must be completed by the children before bedtime.","Their homework must completed by the children before bedtime.","Their homework must has been completed by the children before bedtime.","Their homework must to be completed by the children before bedtime."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-passive","explain":"must + 动 → 被动 must be + p.p. B 漏 be; C 加 has 错; D 加 to 错 (情态动词后不加 to)"},{"q":"\"I have finished my homework,\" Mary told her mother.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["Mary told her mother that she had finished her homework.","Mary told her mother that she has finished her homework.","Mary told her mother she finished her homework.","Mary told her mother that I had finished my homework."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"现在完成 have finished → 过去完成 had finished (时态后退). B 没退; C 跳到简单过去 (语义变); D 没改人称"},{"q":"\"Will you help me with this exercise?\" Lisa asked her brother.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["Lisa asked her brother if he would help her with that exercise.","Lisa asked her brother if he will help her with this exercise.","Lisa asked her brother that he would help her with this exercise.","Lisa asked her brother would he help her with that exercise."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"Will → would (后退); this → that; me → her. B 没退时; C 用 that 错 (yes/no 问题用 if/whether); D 保留疑问语序错"},{"q":"\"What time does the show start?\" the boy asked.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["The boy asked what time the show started.","The boy asked what time did the show start.","The boy asked what time does the show start.","The boy asked that what time the show started."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"Wh 问句间接化: 不用助动词 did, 用陈述语序 + 时态后退 started. B 保留 did 错; C 没变时态; D 加 that 错"},{"q":"\"You must wear your school uniform tomorrow,\" the teacher said to us.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["The teacher told us that we had to wear our school uniform the next day.","The teacher told us that we must wear our school uniform tomorrow.","The teacher said to us that we had to wear our school uniform tomorrow.","The teacher told us we must wear our school uniform the next day."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"must → had to (情态后退); tomorrow → the next day. B 都没退; C said to 错 (应用 told); D must 没退"},{"q":"\"Don't touch the wet paint,\" the painter warned them.","rule":"Rewrite in indirect speech.","opts":["The painter warned them not to touch the wet paint.","The painter warned them don't touch the wet paint.","The painter warned them that they don't touch the wet paint.","The painter warned them to not touch the wet paint."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-indirect","explain":"否定祈使句 → not to + 动. B 保留 don't 错; C 加 that 错; D not to → to not (分裂不定式, 错)"},{"q":"The food was delicious. It was very expensive.","rule":"Combine using \"Although\".","opts":["Although the food was delicious, it was very expensive.","Although the food being delicious, it was very expensive.","The food was delicious, although very expensive.","Although that the food was delicious, it was very expensive."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-although","explain":"Although + 主语 + 动 + 完整从句. B being 错 (Although 后不能用 ing); C 后跟 although 短语 (不规范); D 加 that 错"},{"q":"It was raining heavily. We continued our football match.","rule":"Combine using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite the heavy rain, we continued our football match.","Despite it was raining heavily, we continued our football match.","Despite of the heavy rain, we continued our football match.","Despite raining heavily, we continued our football match."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-despite","explain":"Despite + 名词短语 (the heavy rain). B 后跟完整从句错 (那是 Although); C Despite of 错 (没 of); D 缺主语会歧义"},{"q":"He is rich. He is not happy.","rule":"Combine using \"Although\".","opts":["Although he is rich, he is not happy.","Although rich, he is not happy.","Despite he is rich, he is not happy.","Although he is rich, but he is not happy."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-although","explain":"Although + 完整从句. B 省主谓 (口语 OK 但 PSLE 不规范); C Despite 后跟完整句错; D 多了 but (although...but 重复)"},{"q":"Tom worked hard. He failed the exam.","rule":"Combine using \"Despite\".","opts":["Despite working hard, Tom failed the exam.","Despite he worked hard, Tom failed the exam.","Despite of working hard, Tom failed the exam.","Despite Tom worked hard, he failed the exam."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-despite","explain":"Despite + 动名词 (working). B/D 后跟完整从句错; C of 多余"},{"q":"The weather was bad. The event was a success.","rule":"Combine using \"In spite of\".","opts":["In spite of the bad weather, the event was a success.","In spite the bad weather, the event was a success.","In spite of that the weather was bad, the event was a success.","In spite of the weather was bad, the event was a success."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-in spite of","explain":"In spite of + 名词 (the bad weather). B 漏 of; C 多 that; D 后跟句子错"},{"q":"The box is too heavy. I cannot lift it.","rule":"Combine using \"so...that\".","opts":["The box is so heavy that I cannot lift it.","The box is so heavy so that I cannot lift it.","The box is too heavy that I cannot lift it.","The box is such heavy that I cannot lift it."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-so that","explain":"so + 形容词 + that. B 多了 so that; C too...that 错 (too...to); D such 用错 (such 后跟名词)"},{"q":"It was a difficult question. Nobody could answer it.","rule":"Combine using \"such...that\".","opts":["It was such a difficult question that nobody could answer it.","It was so difficult question that nobody could answer it.","It was such difficult question that nobody could answer it.","It was such a difficult question and nobody could answer it."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-such that","explain":"such + a/an + 形容词 + 名词 + that. B so 用错 (so 跟形容词不跟名词); C 漏 a; D 用 and 错 (不是结果)"},{"q":"She runs very fast. She always wins the race.","rule":"Combine using \"so...that\".","opts":["She runs so fast that she always wins the race.","She runs so fast and always wins the race.","She runs so fast that she always win the race.","She runs such fast that she always wins the race."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-so that","explain":"so + 副词 + that. B 用 and 错; C wins 改 win (主谓错); D such 后跟形容词错"},{"q":"The film was boring. We all fell asleep.","rule":"Combine using \"so...that\".","opts":["The film was so boring that we all fell asleep.","The film was such boring that we all fell asleep.","The film was so boring, so we all fell asleep.","So boring was the film that we all fell asleep."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-so that","explain":"so + 形 + that. B such 后跟形容词错; C so...so 重复; D 是倒装句, 语法 OK 但不符 \"so...that\" 标准结构"},{"q":"The puzzle was easy. Even my little brother solved it.","rule":"Combine using \"such...that\".","opts":["It was such an easy puzzle that even my little brother solved it.","It was such easy puzzle that even my little brother solved it.","It was so easy puzzle that even my little brother solved it.","It was such a easy puzzle that even my little brother solved it."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-such that","explain":"such + an (元音前) + 形 + 名 + that. B 漏 a/an; C so 后跟名词错; D 用 a 错 (easy 元音前要 an)"},{"q":"John is a teacher. His wallet was stolen.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["John, whose wallet was stolen, is a teacher.","The teacher John, whose wallet was stolen.","John whose wallet was stolen is a teacher.","John who his wallet was stolen, is a teacher."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"whose = 所有格关系代词 (= his/her/their). 非限定从句两边要逗号. B 不完整 (缺 is...); C 缺逗号; D who 后还有 his 重复 (用 whose 就不用 his). 🎯 孩子真考 D34 错的就是这型!"},{"q":"I met a girl. Her father is a doctor.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["I met a girl whose father is a doctor.","I met a girl who her father is a doctor.","I met a girl whose her father is a doctor.","I met a girl, who father is a doctor."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"whose 直接代替 her, 不能再加 her (C 错); 限定从句不要逗号 (D 错); who + her 重复错 (B). 一般信息用限定从句不加逗号"},{"q":"The book is on the table. Its cover is red.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["The book whose cover is red is on the table.","The book, whose cover is red, is on the table.","The book which cover is red is on the table.","The book whose its cover is red is on the table."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"whose 也可代物 (its cover). 限定从句 (区分\"哪本书\"才说), 所以不要逗号 (A 对, B 错). C which 错 (不能用所有格); D whose + its 重复"},{"q":"My friend lost her cat. The cat is white.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["My friend, whose cat is white, lost her cat.","My friend whose cat white, lost her cat.","My friend, whose cat is white lost her cat.","My friend whose her cat is white, lost her cat."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"非限定从句两边都要逗号 (A 对); B 缺 is; C 缺右逗号; D whose + her 重复"},{"q":"The student got an award. His project won the competition.","rule":"Combine using \"whose\".","opts":["The student whose project won the competition got an award.","The student which project won the competition got an award.","The student, whose project won the competition got an award.","The student got an award whose his project won the competition."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whose","explain":"限定从句不要逗号 (A 对); B which 不能代人; C 缺右逗号 (要么两边都加要么都不加); D 语序错 + 重复 his"},{"q":"I borrowed a book from the library. The book was very interesting.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The book which I borrowed from the library was very interesting.","The book, which I borrowed from the library, was very interesting.","I borrowed a book from the library which was very interesting.","The book whom I borrowed from the library was very interesting."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"限定从句区分\"哪本书\", which 引导 (A 对). B 两逗号成非限定, 但限定情境下不对; C 歧义 (which 指 library 还是 book?); D whom 不能代物"},{"q":"The car was very expensive. It was parked outside the house.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The car which was parked outside the house was very expensive.","The car, which was parked outside the house, was very expensive.","The car who was parked outside the house was very expensive.","The car which it was parked outside the house was very expensive."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"限定从句区分\"哪辆车\", A 对. B 用逗号变非限定 (有歧义题型); C who 不代物; D which + it 重复 (which 已代 the car)"},{"q":"The cake was delicious. My mum baked it for my birthday.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The cake which my mum baked for my birthday was delicious.","The cake, which my mum baked for my birthday, was delicious.","The cake whom my mum baked for my birthday was delicious.","The cake which my mum baked it for my birthday was delicious."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"A 对 (which 作宾语, 可省略); D 错: which 已是 it 的代替, 不要再加 it"},{"q":"The movie won the award. We watched the movie last night.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The movie which we watched last night won the award.","The movie that we watched last night, won the award.","The movie which won the award we watched last night.","The movie won the award which we watched last night."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"A 对 (which 作宾语); B that 也行但加了逗号错; C 语序混乱; D which 修饰 award 不对 (要修饰 movie)"},{"q":"The new park is beautiful. It was opened last month.","rule":"Combine using \"which\".","opts":["The new park, which was opened last month, is beautiful.","The new park which it was opened last month is beautiful.","The new park, who was opened last month, is beautiful.","The new park was opened last month which is beautiful."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-which","explain":"A 对 (非限定从句加逗号); B which + it 重复; C who 不代物; D 修饰错了名词"},{"q":"The boy is my classmate. He won the spelling bee.","rule":"Combine using \"who\".","opts":["The boy who won the spelling bee is my classmate.","The boy whom won the spelling bee is my classmate.","The boy which won the spelling bee is my classmate.","The boy he won the spelling bee is my classmate."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-who","explain":"who 代人作主语 (A 对); B whom 是宾格不对 (这里 he 是主语); C which 不代人; D he 与 who 重复"},{"q":"I have a neighbour. She is a famous singer.","rule":"Combine using \"who\".","opts":["I have a neighbour who is a famous singer.","I have a neighbour, who is a famous singer.","I have a neighbour whom is a famous singer.","I have a neighbour which is a famous singer."],"ans":0,"diff":4,"tag":"sst-relative-who","explain":"限定从句不加逗号 (A 对); B 加逗号变非限定 (歧义); C whom 错 (是主语); D which 不代人"},{"q":"My grandmother makes the best cookies. She lives next door.","rule":"Combine using \"who\".","opts":["My grandmother, who lives next door, makes the best cookies.","My grandmother who lives next door, makes the best cookies.","My grandmother, who lives next door makes the best cookies.","My grandmother that lives next door, makes the best cookies."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-who","explain":"非限定从句两边都要逗号 (A 对); B 缺左逗号; C 缺右逗号; D that 不能用在非限定"},{"q":"The man is my uncle. I spoke to him yesterday.","rule":"Combine using \"whom\".","opts":["The man whom I spoke to yesterday is my uncle.","The man who I spoke to him yesterday is my uncle.","The man whom I spoke to him yesterday is my uncle.","The man which I spoke to yesterday is my uncle."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whom","explain":"whom 代人作宾语 (介词 to 后宾格); B who 错 (应 whom) + him 重复; C whom + him 重复; D which 不代人"},{"q":"The teacher gave me extra help. I thanked her yesterday.","rule":"Combine using \"whom\".","opts":["The teacher whom I thanked yesterday gave me extra help.","The teacher who I thanked her yesterday gave me extra help.","The teacher whom gave me extra help I thanked yesterday.","The teacher whose I thanked yesterday gave me extra help."],"ans":0,"diff":5,"tag":"sst-relative-whom","explain":"whom 代 her (宾格); B 多了 her 重复; C 语序错; D whose 是所有格不对"}];

function getSstByDiff(diff, n) { return _sampleByDiff(SST_QUESTIONS, diff, n || 5); }

// ============= v19.4: Comprehension OE 训练 (PSLE Paper 2 Section D 风格) =============
// 格式: passage + questions (literal/inferential/evaluative) + model answers
// App 内无法自动批改, 用 "自评" 模式: 读题→思考→查看 model answer→打分
const COMP_OE_PASSAGES = [
  { id: 'comp1', title: 'The Lost Dog', diff: 3, wordCount: 180,
    passage: 'Tom was walking home from school when he noticed a small brown dog sitting by the roadside. It looked thin and dirty, with a torn collar around its neck. The dog whimpered softly and looked up at Tom with sad eyes. Tom knelt down and gently stroked its head. He noticed a phone number on the collar tag, though it was partly scratched off. Tom took the dog home, gave it water and some leftover chicken. He spent the evening trying different number combinations until finally reaching the owner — an elderly woman named Mrs Chen who had been searching for three days. When she arrived, tears of joy streamed down her face as the dog leaped into her arms.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'How did Tom know the dog was lost?', type: 'literal', marks: 2, model: 'Tom knew the dog was lost because it looked thin and dirty, with a torn collar around its neck (1m). It was sitting alone by the roadside and whimpered softly, suggesting it had been without an owner for some time (1m).' },
      { q: 'What does the phrase "tears of joy streamed down her face" tell us about Mrs Chen\'s feelings?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'The phrase tells us that Mrs Chen was overwhelmed with happiness and relief (1m). She had been searching for her dog for three days and had probably feared she would never see it again, so finding it safe made her extremely emotional (1m).' },
      { q: 'Do you think Tom did the right thing by taking the dog home? Give a reason.', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'Yes, Tom did the right thing because the dog was hungry and dirty, meaning it needed immediate care (1m). He also made the effort to contact the owner using the collar tag, showing responsibility rather than just ignoring the dog\'s plight (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp2', title: 'The School Garden', diff: 3, wordCount: 160,
    passage: 'Our school started a garden project last term. Every class was given a small plot to grow vegetables. At first, many students were reluctant to get their hands dirty. However, as the weeks went by, we noticed tiny green shoots emerging from the soil. The excitement was contagious. Even the most reluctant students began checking on their plants every morning before assembly. By the end of the term, our class had harvested enough tomatoes and lettuce to make a salad for everyone. The principal praised our efforts and announced that the garden would become a permanent feature of the school.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'Why were many students reluctant at first?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'Many students were reluctant because they did not want to get their hands dirty (1m).' },
      { q: 'What does "the excitement was contagious" mean?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'It means that the feeling of excitement spread from one student to another (1m), just like how a disease spreads. When some students got excited about the growing plants, their enthusiasm influenced other students to feel the same way (1m).' },
      { q: 'What lesson can students learn from this garden project?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'Students can learn that patience and perseverance lead to rewarding results (1m). Even though the work seemed unpleasant at first, sticking with it brought a sense of achievement and brought the class together (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp3', title: 'The Flood', diff: 4, wordCount: 200,
    passage: 'It had been raining incessantly for three days. The monsoon drains, which usually handled the heavy rainfall efficiently, were overwhelmed. Water began seeping into the ground-floor flats along Bukit Timah Road. Mr Lim, a retired teacher who lived alone, woke up at 5am to find murky brown water ankle-deep in his living room. His precious collection of books — accumulated over forty years of teaching — was being destroyed before his eyes. Neighbours rallied together, forming a human chain to pass sandbags and move furniture to higher ground. A young polytechnic student named Aisha waded through the floodwater to help Mr Lim carry his most treasured books to safety on the second floor of a nearby block. "Community spirit," Mr Lim said later, his voice cracking with emotion, "is what makes Singapore special."',
    questions: [
      { q: 'Why were the monsoon drains unable to cope with the rain?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'The monsoon drains were unable to cope because it had been raining incessantly (continuously without stopping) for three days, which was more than they could usually handle (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why was Mr Lim particularly upset about the flood damage?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'Mr Lim was particularly upset because his precious collection of books, which he had accumulated over forty years of teaching, was being destroyed (1m). These books likely held great sentimental value as they represented his life\'s work and passion as a teacher (1m).' },
      { q: 'What does Mr Lim\'s final statement suggest about his values?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'His statement suggests that he values community spirit and togetherness above material possessions (1m). Despite losing his books, he was moved by how his neighbours and a stranger (Aisha) came together to help, showing that human connections matter more to him than things (1m).' },
      { q: 'Give one piece of evidence that shows the community helped Mr Lim.', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'Neighbours formed a human chain to pass sandbags and move furniture to higher ground (1m). OR: Aisha waded through the floodwater to help Mr Lim carry his books to safety (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp4', title: 'The Exam', diff: 3, wordCount: 170,
    passage: 'Priya stared at the mathematics paper in front of her. Question 15 — a problem involving speed, distance and time — seemed impossible. Her mind went blank. She could hear the clock ticking loudly on the wall. Twenty minutes left. She took a deep breath, remembering what her tutor had taught her: "Draw a diagram. Label what you know. The answer will come." Priya picked up her pencil and sketched a simple timeline. Slowly, the numbers began to make sense. She worked through each step carefully, checking her calculations twice. When the bell rang, she had not only solved Question 15 but had also checked the rest of her paper. Walking out of the hall, she felt a quiet confidence she had never felt before.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'What was Priya\'s initial reaction to Question 15?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'Priya\'s mind went blank and she felt the question was impossible (1m).' },
      { q: 'How did Priya overcome her difficulty?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'She remembered her tutor\'s advice to draw a diagram and label what she knew (1m). By following this strategy step by step and staying calm (taking a deep breath), she was able to work through the problem logically (1m).' },
      { q: 'What does "a quiet confidence she had never felt before" suggest about how this experience changed Priya?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'It suggests that overcoming this challenge gave Priya a new belief in her own abilities (1m). Unlike before, she now knows she can handle difficult problems by staying calm and using strategies, which will help her in future exams too (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp5', title: 'The Hawker', diff: 4, wordCount: 210,
    passage: 'Uncle Tan has been selling laksa at his hawker stall for thirty-five years. Every morning at 4am, he begins preparing the coconut broth from scratch — a recipe passed down from his mother. "Young people don\'t want to do this work anymore," he said, wiping sweat from his forehead. "They think it is low-class. But I am proud of what I do." His laksa has won numerous awards, and food bloggers from around the world have featured his stall. Despite offers from restaurant chains to franchise his recipe, Uncle Tan has always refused. "If I sell the recipe, they will cut corners. Use powder instead of fresh spices. My customers will taste the difference." Now 68, Uncle Tan worries about who will take over when he retires. His two children are both engineers. "I don\'t blame them," he says. "I just hope someone who loves food will continue this tradition."',
    questions: [
      { q: 'At what time does Uncle Tan start preparing his laksa?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'Uncle Tan starts preparing his laksa at 4am every morning (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why has Uncle Tan refused to franchise his recipe?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'He refused because he believes restaurant chains will cut corners by using powder instead of fresh spices (1m). He takes pride in the quality of his food and does not want his customers to taste a lesser version of his laksa (1m).' },
      { q: 'What does this passage suggest about the challenges facing Singapore\'s hawker culture?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'The passage suggests that hawker culture faces the challenge of succession — younger Singaporeans prefer professional careers and view hawker work as undesirable (1m). Without young people willing to learn traditional recipes and endure the hard work, iconic dishes like Uncle Tan\'s laksa may disappear when the current generation of hawkers retires (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp6', title: 'The Bully', diff: 4, wordCount: 190,
    passage: 'Marcus had been dreading recess every day for the past month. A group of older boys would wait near the canteen and demand his pocket money. If he refused, they would push him and call him names. He never told anyone — not his parents, not his teachers. He was afraid it would get worse. One day, his classmate Wei Ling noticed the bruises on his arm. "Marcus, who did this to you?" she asked quietly. When he finally told her everything, Wei Ling insisted they tell their form teacher, Mrs Goh. "You are not alone in this," she said firmly. Mrs Goh took immediate action. The bullies were called to the principal\'s office that very afternoon. Looking back, Marcus realised that his silence had only given the bullies more power.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'How long had Marcus been bullied?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'Marcus had been bullied for the past month (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why did Marcus not tell anyone about the bullying?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'Marcus did not tell anyone because he was afraid that if he reported it, the bullying would get worse (1m). He may also have felt ashamed or embarrassed about being unable to stand up for himself (1m).' },
      { q: 'What does the last sentence "his silence had only given the bullies more power" mean?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'It means that by staying quiet and not seeking help, Marcus was unintentionally allowing the bullies to continue their behaviour without consequences (1m). Speaking up would have stopped them sooner, but his silence made them bolder and more confident that they could get away with it (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp7', title: 'Technology in Schools', diff: 5, wordCount: 220,
    passage: 'The Ministry of Education recently announced that all primary schools would be equipped with tablets for every student by 2028. Proponents argue that digital learning allows students to access a wealth of educational resources instantly and learn at their own pace. Interactive apps can make difficult concepts more engaging and provide immediate feedback. However, critics worry about the impact on children\'s eyesight and attention spans. Dr Sarah Koh, a child psychologist, warns that "excessive screen time before age 12 has been linked to difficulty concentrating and reduced physical activity." Teachers have expressed mixed feelings. Mr Ahmad, who has taught for twenty years, notes: "Technology is a tool, not a replacement for good teaching. A tablet cannot inspire a child the way a passionate teacher can." The debate highlights a fundamental question: in our rush to modernise, are we considering what children actually need to learn effectively?',
    questions: [
      { q: 'State one advantage of digital learning mentioned in the passage.', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'Digital learning allows students to access educational resources instantly and learn at their own pace (1m). OR: Interactive apps make difficult concepts more engaging and provide immediate feedback (1m).' },
      { q: 'What is Dr Sarah Koh concerned about?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'Dr Koh is concerned that too much screen time before age 12 can harm children\'s ability to concentrate (1m) and lead to reduced physical activity, which could affect their overall health and development (1m).' },
      { q: 'Do you agree with Mr Ahmad that "a tablet cannot inspire a child the way a passionate teacher can"? Explain your view.', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'Accept any well-reasoned answer. Example (Agree): Yes, because a teacher can respond to a child\'s emotions, provide encouragement, and adapt their teaching to the moment (1m). Technology follows fixed programmes and cannot build the personal relationships that motivate students to try harder (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp8', title: 'The Race', diff: 3, wordCount: 160,
    passage: 'It was the final race of Sports Day — the 4x100 metre relay. Our class had been training every morning for two weeks. I was the last runner, the anchor. As the third runner sprinted towards me, I could see we were in second place. My heart pounded as I grabbed the baton and ran with everything I had. The wind rushed past my ears. I could hear my classmates screaming my name from the stands. With ten metres to go, I was neck and neck with the boy from Class 6A. I leaned forward and crossed the finish line. For a breathless moment, nobody knew who had won. Then the announcement came: "Winner — Class 6B!" The roar from my class was deafening.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'What position was the narrator\'s team in before the final leg?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'The team was in second place (1m).' },
      { q: 'How does the writer create a sense of excitement in this passage? Give two ways.', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'The writer uses short, punchy sentences like "My heart pounded" to create urgency (1m). He also uses sensory details such as "the wind rushed past my ears" and "I could hear my classmates screaming" to put the reader in the moment (1m). (Also accept: suspense — "For a breathless moment, nobody knew who had won")' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp9', title: 'The Old Tree', diff: 4, wordCount: 190,
    passage: 'The ancient rain tree at the corner of Orchard Road had stood there for over a hundred years. Its massive canopy provided shade for generations of Singaporeans. Children climbed its gnarled roots; couples had their photographs taken beneath its branches; old men played chess in its cool shadow every afternoon. When the government announced plans to widen the road, the tree was marked for removal. A petition started by a secondary school student gathered over fifty thousand signatures in three days. Social media erupted with the hashtag #SaveOurTree. After much deliberation, the Land Transport Authority redesigned the road expansion to curve around the tree instead. "This tree is not just wood and leaves," the student wrote in her petition. "It is a piece of our collective memory."',
    questions: [
      { q: 'How old is the rain tree?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'The rain tree is over a hundred years old (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why did so many people sign the petition?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'Many people signed because the tree held sentimental value — it was part of their shared experiences and memories across generations (1m). The passage shows people of all ages using the tree (children climbing, couples photographing, old men playing chess), suggesting it was a beloved community landmark (1m).' },
      { q: 'What does the student mean by "a piece of our collective memory"?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'She means the tree is not just a plant but a symbol that connects different generations of Singaporeans through shared experiences (1m). Removing it would be like erasing a part of the community\'s history and identity (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp10', title: 'The New Student', diff: 3, wordCount: 170,
    passage: 'When Xiao Ming joined our class in Term 2, he could barely speak English. He had just arrived from China and everything about Singapore school life was unfamiliar to him. During lessons, he would stare blankly at the whiteboard. At recess, he sat alone. One day, our teacher paired him with me for a science project. At first, communication was difficult. He would draw pictures to explain his ideas. Slowly, I realised he was actually brilliant at science — he just could not express it in English yet. I started teaching him simple phrases during our project meetings. By the end of term, Xiao Ming scored the highest in our science test. He stood up and said, carefully but clearly, "Thank you, everyone, for helping me." The whole class cheered.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'What were Xiao Ming\'s two main challenges when he first arrived?', type: 'literal', marks: 2, model: 'His two main challenges were that he could barely speak English (1m) and everything about Singapore school life was unfamiliar to him (1m).' },
      { q: 'How did the narrator discover that Xiao Ming was good at science?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'The narrator discovered this when they were paired for a science project. Although Xiao Ming could not express ideas in English, he drew pictures to explain them (1m), which showed the narrator that he had strong scientific understanding despite the language barrier (1m).' },
      { q: 'What message does this story convey about judging others?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'The story conveys that we should not judge people\'s intelligence or abilities based on their language skills alone (1m). Someone who struggles with English may still be extremely capable in other areas, and with patience and support, they can overcome the language barrier (1m).' }
    ]},
  // ====== v19.4d: Comp OE 扩充 10 篇 (总计 20 篇) ======
  { id: 'comp11', title: 'The Charity Run', diff: 3, wordCount: 170,
    passage: 'Our school organised a charity run to raise funds for the Children\'s Cancer Foundation. Each student had to find sponsors who would donate based on the number of laps completed. I managed to get five sponsors, including my grandmother who promised ten dollars per lap. On the day of the run, the sun was blazing. By the fifth lap, my legs felt like jelly. I wanted to give up. Then I thought of the children in hospital who could not even run. I pushed through the pain and completed eight laps. When I told my grandmother, she was so proud that she doubled her donation. Together, our school raised over fifteen thousand dollars.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'What was the purpose of the charity run?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'The purpose was to raise funds for the Children\'s Cancer Foundation (1m).' },
      { q: 'What motivated the narrator to keep running despite wanting to give up?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'The narrator thought of the children in hospital who could not even run (1m). This made the narrator feel that their own discomfort was small compared to what sick children faced, giving them the determination to push through (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why do you think the grandmother doubled her donation?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'The grandmother was proud of the narrator\'s perseverance and effort in completing eight laps despite the heat (1m). By doubling her donation, she was rewarding the narrator\'s determination and showing that she valued effort over just results (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp12', title: 'The Stray Cat', diff: 4, wordCount: 190,
    passage: 'A thin ginger cat had been appearing at our void deck every evening for a week. Its ribs were visible beneath matted fur, and it flinched at every loud noise. My sister and I started leaving food and water for it. Gradually, it began to trust us, allowing us to stroke its head. We named it Marmalade. When we asked our parents if we could keep it, they hesitated. "Who will clean the litter box? Who will take it to the vet?" Dad asked. We made a written contract promising to share all responsibilities. Two months later, Marmalade is a healthy, playful cat who greets us at the door every day. Dad, who was the most reluctant, is now the one who sneaks Marmalade extra treats when he thinks nobody is watching.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'How do we know the cat was in poor condition when first found?', type: 'literal', marks: 2, model: 'The cat was thin with its ribs visible beneath matted fur (1m). It also flinched at every loud noise, suggesting it was frightened and possibly mistreated before (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why did the children make a "written contract"?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'They made a written contract to show their parents they were serious and responsible enough to care for a pet (1m). It addressed their parents\' concerns about who would do the work by formally committing to share responsibilities (1m).' },
      { q: 'What is ironic about the ending?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'It is ironic that Dad, who was the most reluctant to keep the cat and questioned whether the children would be responsible, has now become the most attached (1m). He sneaks the cat extra treats, showing that despite his initial resistance, he has grown to love Marmalade the most (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp13', title: 'Water Conservation', diff: 4, wordCount: 200,
    passage: 'Singapore imports much of its water from Malaysia under an agreement that expires in 2061. To reduce this dependency, PUB has invested heavily in four "National Taps": local catchment, imported water, NEWater (recycled water), and desalination. Schools play a crucial role in water conservation education. At Riverside Primary, students monitor the school\'s daily water usage displayed on a digital dashboard. "When the students see the numbers go up after someone leaves a tap running, they become water ambassadors themselves," explains the principal. Despite these efforts, Singapore\'s per capita water consumption remains at 141 litres per day — higher than the PUB target of 130 litres by 2030. Experts warn that with climate change making rainfall patterns more unpredictable, every drop saved today is an investment in tomorrow\'s security.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'Name two of Singapore\'s four "National Taps".', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'Any two of: local catchment, imported water, NEWater (recycled water), desalination (1m for naming 2).' },
      { q: 'How does the digital dashboard help students learn about water conservation?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'The dashboard shows real-time water usage, so when students see the numbers increase (e.g., after a tap is left running), they understand the immediate impact of waste (1m). This visual, concrete feedback turns abstract conservation messages into something personal and actionable (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why does the writer call saving water "an investment in tomorrow\'s security"?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'Because climate change is making rainfall unpredictable, meaning Singapore cannot rely on nature alone for water supply (1m). Every litre saved now reduces future dependency on expensive alternatives like desalination and protects against potential water shortages (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp14', title: 'The Piano Recital', diff: 3, wordCount: 160,
    passage: 'My fingers trembled as I walked onto the stage. Three hundred people sat in the audience, including my piano teacher Mrs Wong, who had prepared me for this moment over two years. The lights were blinding. I sat down, placed my hands on the keys, and froze. My mind went completely blank — I could not remember the first note. The silence felt eternal. Then Mrs Wong\'s voice echoed in my head: "If you forget, just breathe and listen to the music inside you." I closed my eyes, took a deep breath, and my fingers found the keys on their own. The melody of Chopin\'s Nocturne flowed through me. When I finished, the applause was thunderous. But the proudest face in the crowd was Mrs Wong\'s.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'What happened when the narrator first sat at the piano?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'The narrator froze and could not remember the first note — their mind went completely blank (1m).' },
      { q: 'How did Mrs Wong\'s advice help the narrator?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'Her advice to "breathe and listen to the music inside you" helped the narrator relax and stop panicking (1m). By closing their eyes and breathing, the narrator let muscle memory take over, and their fingers found the keys automatically without conscious recall (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp15', title: 'The Food Waste Problem', diff: 5, wordCount: 210,
    passage: 'Singapore generates approximately 744,000 tonnes of food waste annually — enough to fill over 1,000 Olympic swimming pools. While some of this is unavoidable (bones, shells), studies suggest that up to 40% is perfectly edible food discarded due to cosmetic imperfections, over-ordering, or expiry date confusion. "Best before" dates indicate quality, not safety, yet most consumers throw food away the moment this date passes. Social enterprise "SG Food Rescue" redistributes surplus food from hotels and supermarkets to low-income families. Volunteer driver Mr Raj makes three trips daily: "Sometimes I collect enough food for two hundred families from just one hotel buffet. It breaks my heart to think this was headed for the bin." The government\'s "30 by 30" goal — producing 30% of nutritional needs locally by 2030 — will only succeed if consumption habits change alongside production capacity.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'How much food waste does Singapore generate each year?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'Singapore generates approximately 744,000 tonnes of food waste annually (1m).' },
      { q: 'What is the difference between "best before" and actual food safety?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: '"Best before" dates indicate the period during which food is at its peak quality (taste, texture), not when it becomes unsafe to eat (1m). Many consumers mistakenly believe food is dangerous after this date and throw it away, when in reality it may still be perfectly safe to consume (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why does the writer say "30 by 30" will only succeed if consumption habits change?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'Because even if Singapore produces more food locally, it will not solve the problem if people continue to waste 40% of edible food (1m). Producing more without reducing waste is inefficient — the real solution requires both increasing supply and decreasing wasteful consumption (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp16', title: 'Grandfather\'s Lesson', diff: 3, wordCount: 170,
    passage: 'Every Sunday, my grandfather takes me fishing at Bedok Reservoir. We never catch much — sometimes nothing at all. My friends think it is boring. "Why don\'t you just buy fish from the market?" they ask. But fishing with Grandfather is not about the fish. It is about the stories he tells while we wait — stories of growing up in a kampong, of catching real fish in rivers that no longer exist. It is about learning patience, about sitting still in a world that never stops moving. Last Sunday, after three hours without a single bite, Grandfather smiled and said, "The best things in life cannot be rushed." I think he was not talking about fishing anymore.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'Where does the narrator go fishing with his grandfather?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'They go fishing at Bedok Reservoir (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why does the narrator continue fishing despite never catching much?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'The narrator values the time spent with grandfather — hearing stories about his past and learning life lessons like patience (1m). The activity itself is less important than the bonding and wisdom shared between them (1m).' },
      { q: 'What do you think the grandfather meant by "The best things in life cannot be rushed"?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'He likely meant that important things like relationships, personal growth, and wisdom take time to develop and cannot be achieved quickly (1m). Just as fishing requires patience, life\'s most meaningful achievements — like the bond between grandfather and grandchild — grow slowly through consistent effort and presence (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp17', title: 'The Group Project', diff: 4, wordCount: 190,
    passage: 'We were assigned a group project on Singapore\'s biodiversity. I was grouped with three classmates: Mei Ling, who was hardworking; Ravi, who was creative; and Jason, who did nothing. While Mei Ling researched and I compiled the data, Jason claimed he was "too busy" with CCA. The deadline approached and his slides were still empty. Mei Ling wanted to report him. I suggested we talk to him first. When we did, Jason broke down. His parents were going through a divorce and he could barely concentrate on anything. We divided his portion among ourselves and told the teacher only that "everyone contributed." Jason never forgot our kindness. The following term, when I was hospitalised with dengue, Jason visited every day and brought all my missed homework with detailed notes.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'What was Jason\'s reason for not contributing to the project?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'His parents were going through a divorce and he could barely concentrate on anything (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why did the narrator suggest talking to Jason first instead of reporting him?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'The narrator showed empathy by wanting to understand Jason\'s situation before judging him (1m). Rather than assuming Jason was lazy, the narrator gave him a chance to explain, which revealed that Jason was going through a difficult personal crisis (1m).' },
      { q: 'What does Jason\'s behaviour in the following term show about the impact of kindness?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'It shows that kindness creates lasting bonds and inspires people to pay it forward (1m). Because the group showed compassion during Jason\'s difficult time, he felt genuine gratitude and willingly went out of his way to support the narrator when they were in need (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp18', title: 'Digital Detox', diff: 4, wordCount: 180,
    passage: 'Last month, our family tried a "digital detox weekend" — no phones, tablets, or computers from Friday evening to Sunday night. The first few hours were agony. I reached for my phone at least twenty times before remembering it was locked in a drawer. By Saturday morning, something shifted. We played board games, cooked together, and took a long walk at MacRitchie Reservoir. I noticed details I had never seen before: the patterns on tree bark, the sound of water flowing over rocks. My younger brother, usually glued to his iPad, built an elaborate fort out of cardboard boxes. On Sunday night, when we finally unlocked our devices, I had forty-seven notifications. None of them seemed important anymore.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'How long did the digital detox last?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'The digital detox lasted from Friday evening to Sunday night — one weekend (1m).' },
      { q: 'What does the narrator mean by "something shifted" on Saturday morning?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'It means the narrator stopped feeling anxious about not having their phone and began to enjoy being present in the moment (1m). The discomfort of disconnection was replaced by an appreciation for real-world activities and family interaction (1m).' },
      { q: 'What is the significance of the last sentence: "None of them seemed important anymore"?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'It shows that the narrator gained perspective — what felt urgent and important digitally (notifications, messages) lost its significance after experiencing meaningful real-world connections (1m). This suggests that much of our phone usage is habit rather than genuine need (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp19', title: 'The Dengue Crisis', diff: 5, wordCount: 200,
    passage: 'In 2022, Singapore recorded over 32,000 dengue cases — the highest in its history. The Aedes mosquito, which thrives in tropical climates, breeds in stagnant water as shallow as a five-cent coin. Despite regular NEA inspections and heavy fines for breeding, the virus continues to surge. Scientists point to two factors: rising temperatures that accelerate mosquito reproduction, and urbanisation that creates countless hidden breeding spots in air-conditioning trays, roof gutters, and ornamental plants. Project Wolbachia, which releases male mosquitoes infected with bacteria that prevent reproduction, has shown promise in trial areas. However, Dr Tan from NUS warns: "Technology alone cannot solve this. Every resident must check their home weekly. One careless household can undo the efforts of an entire neighbourhood."',
    questions: [
      { q: 'How many dengue cases were recorded in Singapore in 2022?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'Over 32,000 dengue cases were recorded (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why is urbanisation making the dengue problem worse?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'Urbanisation creates many hidden spots where water can collect and stagnate — such as air-conditioning trays, roof gutters, and ornamental plants (1m). These are places that are difficult to inspect regularly and provide ideal breeding grounds for Aedes mosquitoes in dense residential areas (1m).' },
      { q: 'Do you agree with Dr Tan that "one careless household can undo the efforts of an entire neighbourhood"? Explain.', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'Yes, because mosquitoes can breed rapidly from even a tiny amount of stagnant water — a single unattended breeding spot can produce hundreds of mosquitoes that spread to neighbouring homes (1m). This means that community-wide efforts like Wolbachia or regular checks are undermined if even one household does not participate (1m).' }
    ]},
  { id: 'comp20', title: 'The Art Competition', diff: 3, wordCount: 170,
    passage: 'I spent three weeks on my painting for the National Art Competition — a watercolour of the Singapore River at sunset. I was certain I would win. On results day, my name was not on the winners\' list. Instead, first prize went to a simple charcoal sketch of an old woman selling tissue paper at a hawker centre. I was furious. My painting had more technique, more colour, more detail. Then my art teacher said something I have never forgotten: "Art is not about showing what you can do. It is about making people feel something." Looking at the winning piece again, I understood. The sketch captured loneliness, dignity, and the reality of Singapore\'s elderly in a way my pretty sunset never could. That day, I stopped painting to impress and started painting to connect.',
    questions: [
      { q: 'What did the narrator paint for the competition?', type: 'literal', marks: 1, model: 'The narrator painted a watercolour of the Singapore River at sunset (1m).' },
      { q: 'Why did the simple charcoal sketch win over the narrator\'s detailed painting?', type: 'inferential', marks: 2, model: 'The sketch won because it conveyed genuine emotion — loneliness and dignity of an elderly tissue seller — which resonated with viewers (1m). While the narrator\'s painting showed technical skill, it lacked the emotional depth and social meaning that makes art truly powerful (1m).' },
      { q: 'What lesson did the narrator learn about art (and life)?', type: 'evaluative', marks: 2, model: 'The narrator learned that the purpose of art is not to display technical skill or impress others, but to create genuine human connection and evoke emotions (1m). This applies to life too — meaningful work comes from authenticity and empathy, not from showing off abilities (1m).' }
    ]}
];

